{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5","id":1528497,"title":"What do you think in hindsight would have been better for V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-13T14:00:18-08:00","id":1528497,"title":"What do you think in hindsight would have been better for V5?","content":"Me personally, I feel they should have done the same thing they did with WtA 5th editon and just remade the game. I understand not all the changes were liked, but I feel it could have been a more welcome change instead of VTM continuing the overall same routine from the older editions. Maybe they could have taken stuff from VTR or Sorcerer(which imo fits vampire a little better). Perhaps they could have added a concept like the covenants to the game, or even give vampires a light boost in regards to powers and the options for powers. <br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyway. What about you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T14:02:54-08:00","id":1528498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5#post1528497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me personally, I feel they should have done the same thing they did with WtA 5th editon and just remade the game. I understand not all the changes were liked, but I feel it could have been a more welcome change instead of VTM continuing the overall same routine from the older editions. Maybe they could have taken stuff from VTR or Sorcerer(which imo fits vampire a little better). Perhaps they could have added a concept like the covenants to the game, or even give vampires a light boost in regards to powers and the options for powers.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyway. What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely think that's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> I really really hope they will reverse course and embrace the canon and lore like Beckett's Jyhad Diary. The history of the setting is what makes the game and the more generic they make it, the crappier it gets. I mean, they ALREADY did a completely new reboot of the game and people wanted the OLD Vampire: The Masquerade back.<br /> <br /> Cults of the Blood Gods and Chicago by Night are the best supplements by far. What do they have the most in common? DING DING DING. They continue the old lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T15:06:57-08:00","id":1528499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528498#post1528498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely think that's a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> I really really hope they will reverse course and embrace the canon and lore like Beckett's Jyhad Diary. The history of the setting is what makes the game and the more generic they make it, the crappier it gets. I mean, they ALREADY did a completely new reboot of the game and people wanted the OLD Vampire: The Masquerade back.<br /> <br /> Cults of the Blood Gods and Chicago by Night are the best supplements by far. What do they have the most in common? DING DING DING. They continue the old lore.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\"><b>But Chicago by Night 5TH EDITION DOES NOT PROPERLY CONTINUE THE LORE AND ABANDONS PLOT POINTS,</b><br /> <br /> They just end Menele vs Helena the central plot/lore bit of Chicago By Night 1ST and 2ND editions, without proper resolution saying he has now retuned to his planet like Poochie in The Simpsoms (Beckoning/he is in middle east) and replaced Menele with a character with ZERO BACKGROUND, because she does not have memories.<br /> <br /> A lot of previous plots are abandoned without resolution using the Beckoning as an excuse. A lot of characters do not behave as they should or are made stupid like all the primogen not to mention the severe nerfs which makes defeating an elder a non acomplismishment. There is 3 dices of difference in certain rolls between ancilla characters and elders/methusaleah in certain aspects like dominate.<br /> <br /> Talking about nerfs the LaSombra where made unplayable with their weakness against technology, A mere camera means a masquerade breach for them in the era of phones... Even an automatic door is a problem for them, or a car as today they have a lot of eletronic parts.... Which makes impossible to justify their entry in the Camarilla where the main rule is &quot;SECRECY/THE MASQUERADE&quot;. The mechanics ignore the concept that is in the Tittle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1271292-these-new-lasombras\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1271292-these-new-lasombras\"> These new Lasombras - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1271292-these-new-lasombras\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1271292-these-new-lasombras </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I saw something on Facebook about these new Lasombras and I agree with that poster: Making the Lasombra bane have a Bane Severity +2 to use any modern technology will ruin the play for many concepts of playing a Lasombra. This will be the only clan who is forced to put dots in technology and maybe drive just to being able to exist. They will not be able to use smartphones modern radions, mp3s, TVs DVDs Videos or cameras. This was prbably the worst thing i have seen in this book. Most appartment houses/blocks in Scandinavia has a electronic lock to get into the building before you can go up to your </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not to mention Oblivion being a nerfed fusion between &quot;Obtenebration and Nigromancy&quot; means that the LaSombra and the Giovanni/Hecata lose their identity in their process specially given their similar discipline spread, which makes anyone who is thinking on using Obtenebration, not choose a LaSombra and instead choose a Hecata. In other words Chicago 5TH EDITION is anti-LaSombra.<br /> <br /> And i am not gonna even gonna talk about the souless political propaganda that permeates the book. I am not against media covering political issues, but if you do, you must do it with maturity, but the quality of the writting remembers me to Chechenya chapters...<br /> <br /> Yes the artstyle is good because they use the artist from CoD instead of the cringe art that they used in the core and other supplements, but you buy a book because of the writting and in the same way you have expectations that a steak is properly cooked when you go to a restaurant, you also should have spectations of a writting being consistently good when you read a book. Something that the 5TH EDITION does not do.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 01-13-2024, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T16:17:05-08:00","id":1528502,"title":"","content":"It's OK for stories to end. And to be blunt, the story of the original World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade ended 20 years ago with the Time of Judgment event. While the 20th anniversary editions were well meaning love letters to the games, by fans for fans, the fifth editions are not. They are just another in a long list of &quot;zombie franchises&quot;, formerly successful properties from a generation or more ago being forced to shuffle around by corporations trying to use nostalgia and brand recognition to squeeze the last drops of profit from something because they are all unwilling - and often unable - to create new intellectual properties of their own. <br /> <br /> If V5 was going to be a thing, I'm of the opinion that it should have simply started over at square one, doing a core book about the original seven Clans focused entirely on the personal and city-level of things, with very little in the way of history/metaplot beyond the legendary origins of the Kindred and the late medieval/early modern upheavals which created the Masquerade. However, such a book would also have to account for the fact that Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles are no longer the main gateway entry for people under 35 when it comes to young and hip vampires. Likewise, the fact that the post 9/11 surveillance state, the corporatization of the internet, and the plague of social media has radically altered the sort of world vampires hide and hunt in. <br /> <br /> Anything beyond that should have been presented entirely as options. A book reintroducing the other Clans should have presented GMs with tools for using them as new/alternate Clans, as offshoots of the existing Clans, or as sects/cults made up of members of the already existing clans. Similarly, a Sabbat book should have presented multiple options for the sect, and a Hunters book should have presented the tools for GMs to create their own vampire hunting organizations of various scales. <br /> I think the old meta plot should have been addressed in a similar book, one that gave an overview of what was in the old material, how it may or may not have played out in the original game's Final Nights, and different ways it might have continued into the 21st century. But all of it should have been optional. <br /> <br /> Such are my opinions, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T16:57:24-08:00","id":1528503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528502#post1528502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's OK for stories to end. And to be blunt, the story of the original World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade ended 20 years ago with the Time of Judgment event. While the 20th anniversary editions were well meaning love letters to the games, by fans for fans, the fifth editions are not. They are just another in a long list of &quot;zombie franchises&quot;, formerly successful properties from a generation or more ago being forced to shuffle around by corporations trying to use nostalgia and brand recognition to squeeze the last drops of profit from something because they are all unwilling - and often unable - to create new intellectual properties of their own.<br /> <br /> If V5 was going to be a thing, I'm of the opinion that it should have simply started over at square one, doing a core book about the original seven Clans focused entirely on the personal and city-level of things, with very little in the way of history/metaplot beyond the legendary origins of the Kindred and the late medieval/early modern upheavals which created the Masquerade. However, such a book would also have to account for the fact that Anne Rice's Vampire Chronicles are no longer the main gateway entry for people under 35 when it comes to young and hip vampires. Likewise, the fact that the post 9/11 surveillance state, the corporatization of the internet, and the plague of social media has radically altered the sort of world vampires hide and hunt in.<br /> <br /> Anything beyond that should have been presented entirely as options. A book reintroducing the other Clans should have presented GMs with tools for using them as new/alternate Clans, as offshoots of the existing Clans, or as sects/cults made up of members of the already existing clans. Similarly, a Sabbat book should have presented multiple options for the sect, and a Hunters book should have presented the tools for GMs to create their own vampire hunting organizations of various scales.<br /> I think the old meta plot should have been addressed in a similar book, one that gave an overview of what was in the old material, how it may or may not have played out in the original game's Final Nights, and different ways it might have continued into the 21st century. But all of it should have been optional.<br /> <br /> Such are my opinions, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Beckett's Jyhad Diary was probably the best VTM supplement ever.<br /> <br /> And starting over was a BAD IDEA.<br /> <br /> They tried that!<br /> <br /> It was fine and a good game but people wanted the original. I'm just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T21:31:52-08:00","id":1528523,"title":"","content":"I don't think &quot;starting over&quot; would have made things much better. I'm not as adamant about things as CT is, but H5 and W5 are not good games. They are way more &quot;zombie franchise&quot; releases than V5 is. V5 worked OK as a new entry that wasn't a zombie, but instead of trying to really work on the parts that didn't work to make it great, they moved to just shoveling out generic bland takes on old games that hope to cash in on brand recognition and so on.<br /> <br /> If they wanted to not be bound to the 90s setting that had a simpler option: giving the Chronicles of Darkness the financial support it never really got after the CCP buy-out of White Wolf. CofD has pedigree, an existing fan base, a more modern sensibility, and is frankly better for building a new transmedia franchise on because it's lore and setting are way easier to work with. <br /> <br /> Since they went with trying to revitalize the WoD instead, IMO V5's biggest mistakes are trying to be clever instead of being innovative, failure to really speak to a new era instead of copying other newer games, and really just having ideas without and design vision for executing them well. Paradox's obsession with hitting arbitrary deadlines instead of giving games adequate testing and refinement didn't help either. I don't think V5 was ever going to be my favorite edition, but so many of its problems were obvious in the play testing, identified by multiple play testers and... Gencon! Release now! If it had another year or two to respond to some pretty essential core game-play criticisms, and some humility from the original V5 team (since it was pretty clear some of them had design darlings that they weren't letting go of even if they weren't really making the game better), it would at least been an edition folks like me would play if the rest of our group really wanted to do that instead of passing on it.<br /> <br /> All of the parts of V5 being a solid game are there. It just feels like an amateurs first try at assembling them all together instead of letting either a more experience hand guide things (like why they kept Onyx Path at arms length is beyond me, except for that lack of humility issue), or let it get assembled, broken back down, and reassembled a few more times to get a lot of the rookie mistakes out and just have a better handle on what was working and what wasn't with their initial approach.<br /> <br /> The idea that V5 was fundamentally wrong in concept doesn't fly with me... and I never want to play V5. But I don't want to play V5 for the same reason I don't want chicken noodle soup from a restaurant where nobody in the kitchen has made it before. The idea of the soup isn't bad. The cooks/chefs might even have some personal flair to make a classic soup unique (I might love that, or not, but that's always going to be preference based). But I'm either going to get something so basic I might as well have bought something canned and heated it up myself, or something too unsure of itself to be enjoyable.<br /> <br /> I do not, at all, agree with CT on how S+ great BJD, CbN5, or CotBG are as supplements. But they're good solid books. CbN5 and CotBG certainly show that V5 is not so fundamentally broken at its core that a radically different approach would have been better in hindsight. They're like having a bowl of soup that's how the chef's family has been making it for generations: you can taste the love, the culture, the respect for what's come before without having to be a stickler about every detail; esp. if you just finish tasting a few &quot;soups&quot; that are all some trend chasing haute cuisine taken too far. You can't make that bowl of soup if everything in your kitchen is wrong and you needed to completely rethink things from the ground up. You can make that soup in a kitchen that was designed by someone that put way too much money into fancy machines to do new trendy things, and skimped out on all the fundamental basics being arranged properly; because you can do that soup in a home kitchen too, and those are never as good as a properly done kitchen.<br /> <br /> That's V5's failing to me. Though I kinda want to go watch The Menu again after that extended analogy (or maybe I should have made the analogy a cheeseburger).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T21:50:43-08:00","id":1528525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they wanted to not be bound to the 90s setting that had a simpler option: giving the Chronicles of Darkness the financial support it never really got after the CCP buy-out of White Wolf. CofD has pedigree, an existing fan base, a more modern sensibility, and is frankly better for building a new transmedia franchise on because it's lore and setting are way easier to work with. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly confused about the idea behind the transmedia franchise.<br /> <br /> They have iconic characters, lore, and stories to tell.<br /> <br /> And they don't seem like they want to use them.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness had great systems for gaming but very little in the way of characters or iconic groups. I'm not saying they didn't exist just they weren't nearly as iconic.<br /> <br /> I also feel really surprised they don't seem to want to use the Signature Characters or create their own. That would be very useful for transmedia properties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-14-2024, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T22:54:26-08:00","id":1528526,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, this new V5 game I'm running I explicitly sold to my players as &quot;Fallout, but for vampires&quot;.<br /> <br /> Gehenna's over. The Second Inquisition won, vampires lost. There was no big apocalyptic event, no nukes, no time travel, no Lilith and no Caine, no [Tzimisce] Evangelion-flavor orange juice, nothing you could soundtrack to &quot;Ode to Joy&quot;, no epic jet-setting adventure, nothing in the news. Vampires went out not with a bang, but a whimper, and those still around were <i>not </i>the lucky ones.<br /> <br /> There's only one true elder in the chronicle, and she survived because she was being held captive by the Inquisition and couldn't respond to the Beckoning. And she's the last one you'd want to have survived Gehenna because once unleashed on the chronicle, <i>well</i>... <div align=\"center\"><img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1434_1705214373515_119\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1434\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1434\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1434&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <br /> <br /> A pissed-off &quot;blood god&quot; doing a bunch of stupid evil shit is one thing. A pissed-off &quot;blood god&quot; who's somewhere between a D&amp;D Paladin and a 40K Adepta Sororitas, who can't comprehend it's no longer the 15th Century, running around being the Fun Police is another, entirely.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I'm unconvinced there's another way you really ought to play V5 while paying due respect to earlier editions' content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 01-14-2024, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T03:21:42-08:00","id":1528531,"title":"","content":"rather than pushing against the diversified play styles of a 30 year game I'd have played into it ala v20, I'd also have probably built a more robust combat system than just skip it after 3 turns and downplayed the larp influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T05:00:04-08:00","id":1528537,"title":"","content":"I admit, I am heavily biased.<br /> <br /> All I wanted was a urban fantasy-horror game about vampires continuing on alongside our world indefinitely. No need for huge world shaking events ala Ravnos but occasional metaplot twists and turns every couple of years.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T05:15:44-08:00","id":1528538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528525#post1528525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly confused about the idea behind the transmedia franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? OG VtM had one: novels, comics, a licensed WWE wrestler, a card game, two video games, a TV show, a few board games too. VtM during it's old height easily branched out into lots of different forms of entertainment (we just didn't call that &quot;transmedia&quot;).<br /> <br /> Paradox didn't want to get into the TTRPG business. They wanted to buy a brand they could make far more profitable things with. VtM makes lots of sense from that perspective. Though how they handled V5 not so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have iconic characters, lore, and stories to tell.<br /> <br /> And they don't seem like they want to use them. </div> </div> </div>Because you're already emotionally attached to them. You value characters that most people that have engaged in VtM media have never heard of. Characters that were big enough to VtM fans that they got their own action figures didn't make it into the TV show or either video game. Imagine it's 2004, you've play Redemption and Bloodlines, and someone you know is going to college and wants to give away all their VtM books. You hop on this because you loved the games and wanted to jump in on the TTRPG stuff... then you find out exactly how few of the characters you loved from the video games were ever actually in the books, that the plots aren't out of character for the TTRPG setting but they're basically completely different time-lines where nothing that your characters did in the video games actually matters to the TTRPG setting. Etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Sure, some people are going to dive deep into all this expanded stuff that they had barely scratched the surface of. But most people didn't. Their iconic characters and lore, and stories aren't in the TTRPG books.<br /> <br /> VtM's vast setting material is a mixed bag in this regard. There's all of this material that already exists. But it's made for TTRPGs. I you want to make an anthology TV show, or new video game, you're going to start with new characters to tell different stories because you need to material that fits the media you work in. If you go lore heavy, you might make hardcore fans happy to see all the stuff they love show up, but you run a serious risk of people new to the franchise via other media not understanding, and not investing to find out more. <br /> <br /> The CofD and to an extent V5 clearly went in the direction of reducing the barrier to entry. You get a consistent atmosphere and broad strokes setting, so that people making traditional media stories can tell the best stories for their art, and new people get sucked in, and try other things in the franchise. You don't need to know who Theo Bell is, or understand the politics of Chicago. The core TTRPG experience is you telling your stories with your characters in your take on the setting. All the rest of the transmedia stuff are artists doing the same thing but with budgets. That's easier without being tied down to the massive existing lore. Do you think Bloodlines 1 would have been better if you needed to read a 160 page book to appreciate the story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T08:26:36-08:00","id":1528542,"title":"","content":"Well, erase the whole damn thing and retry as VtM, not the cursed child of VtM and VtR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T09:41:02-08:00","id":1528545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528542#post1528542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, erase the whole damn thing and retry as VtM, not the cursed child of VtM and VtR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preach it!<br /> Pick up from Becketts Jyhad Diary ended and make a V30!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T11:03:04-08:00","id":1528550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528545#post1528545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Preach it!<br /> Pick up from Becketts Jyhad Diary ended and make a V30!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather not destroy the fantastic work done for Fall of London, Chicago by Night V5, or Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> I also think LA by Night is fantastic as well as the visual novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T11:03:47-08:00","id":1528551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528550#post1528550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather not destroy the fantastic work done for Fall of London, Chicago by Night V5, or Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> I also think LA by Night is fantastic as well as the visual novels.</div> </div> </div> </div>But fall of london isnt very good.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T13:28:36-08:00","id":1528561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528550#post1528550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather not destroy the fantastic work done for Fall of London, Chicago by Night V5, or Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> I also think LA by Night is fantastic as well as the visual novels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's easy enough to solve: multiverse. [Ravnos], Malkav, or any of the mental/illusion dealers created this both as a pocket dimension or a very strong hallucination. They exist there, encapsulated, and we can again have Lasombras as an independent clan of the children of Cappadocius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T07:32:00-08:00","id":1528590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528551#post1528551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div 