"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T10:05:57-08:00","id":1528596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528550#post1528550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather not destroy the fantastic work done for Fall of London, Chicago by Night V5, or Cults of the Blood Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of these things is not like the others,<br /> One of these things just doesn't belong,<br /> Can you tell which thing is not like the others<br /> By the time I finish my song?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T10:11:45-08:00","id":1528598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528596#post1528596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of these things is not like the others,<br /> One of these things just doesn't belong,<br /> Can you tell which thing is not like the others<br /> By the time I finish my song?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I really liked it as the &quot;End&quot; of Mithras' story from 2nd Edition onward. Mithras has the chance to recover ALL of his power but ends up finally destroyed by treachery from people he fully believed he could control.<br /> <br /> Or simply settling down in a tiny kingdom to pretend to be a god some more.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I can't have London, the Camarilla can't. NYAH!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T15:51:04-08:00","id":1528625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528598#post1528598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I really liked it as the &quot;End&quot; of Mithras' story from 2nd Edition onward. Mithras has the chance to recover ALL of his power but ends up finally destroyed by treachery from people he fully believed he could control.<br /> <br /> Or simply settling down in a tiny kingdom to pretend to be a god some more.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I can't have London, the Camarilla can't. NYAH!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the concept was fine.......though the pre-gens and set pieces were pretty garbage overall. It was just extremely badly written and gauche and borrowed heavily from a bunch of sources without even pretending to be transformative enough to disguise it.<br /> <br /> Solid concept, terrible in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T01:55:18-08:00","id":1528640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528598#post1528598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I really liked it as the &quot;End&quot; of Mithras' story from 2nd Edition onward. Mithras has the chance to recover ALL of his power but ends up finally destroyed by treachery from people he fully believed he could control.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But, as I have pointed out before, this makes it into Mithras's story, rather than the players' story, and, really, this is the completely wrong focus for a story or chronicle. <br /> <br /> One of the interesting developments in the World of Darkness as a publishing phenomenon is a shift, in the late 1990s, in White Wolf's intended audience. Prior to the revised edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, there was an expectation of a broad audience. Lots of players were expected to buy a few books, based upon their interests, and there was no great attempt to build a running narrative. Books were designed to be focused primarily on the player characters; you will notice in the early stories published for the game (<i>Alien Hunger</i>, <i>Blood Bond</i>, whatever) there are basically no big-name NPCs. Even the Diablerie series, which sees the appearance of a powerful Methuselah in each book, do not have much in the way of larger consequences through the survival, or otherwise, of their supporting case. <br /> <br /> This shifts massively with the revised edition. There seems to be an expectation that there are fewer people purchasing books, but that these are not players, but fans, and they are expected to be buying every book. All of a sudden we have signature characters. We have random bits of plot stuck in the back of books (for some fans, Lucita's defection to the Sabbat at the back of <i>Midnight Siege</i> was a big event; for people like me it was when we stopped bothering to buy books). Above all, published stories became slide shows where the actions of the players were inconsequential, and effectively fans were expected to be excited by witnessing important events in the game. The nadir of this trend is the Baba Yaga adventure in <i>Nights of Prophecy</i>, where the players have not one single meaningful choice. But it doesn't matter; they get to see the death of Baba Yaga, which, apparently, is the important bit. <br /> <br /> <i>Fall of London</i> takes all the wrong lessons from earlier incarnations of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. I don't care about what happens to Mithras, and I suspect that very few people other than the superfans do either. I don't even understand why anyone should care, unless we are treating these not as game supplements, but as (bad) novels masquerading as game supplements. <br /> <br /> One of the best adventures released for <i>Vampire</i> is <i>Clash of Wills,</i> which is arguably the last story published before the trend of catering to fans took off. There aren't any famous characters, pretty much everyone dies, and the events are inconsequential for the wider world. And it's fun. I wish the writers for the game would actually remember to focus on that last bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T07:59:55-08:00","id":1528650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528542#post1528542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, erase the whole damn thing and retry as VtM, not the cursed child of VtM and VtR.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Vampire The Requiem 2ND ED has the best mechanics of the franchise, it has nothing to do with V5 in fact is the opposite<br /> <br /> While V5 is restrictive, Requiem is a toolbox designed to allow you to customize your world. The entire CoDverse is designed as a toolbox, we even have alternate settings like how would Vampires operate in a space operate similar to Star Wars just because it sounds fun (Mirrors). We also have rules for ciborgs, mutant virus etc...<br /> <br /> Dammnation City is one of the best suplements ever, Danse Macabre has tiers or tweaks to mechanics that allows to choose what kind of gameplay you want: </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Tier 1= Stret level, </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Tier 2= City level, </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Tier 3= Global Scale, </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Tier 4= Cosmic Scale (Through this is more archmage stuff).</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">And in terms of power levels Requiem has vampires and beings that can compete and even defeat antediluvians like the Worm, llorona, Zagreus etc...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T10:23:03-08:00","id":1528654,"title":"","content":"Let's go, again. Since Time of Judgement, and the end of the second biggest franchise 1999, the WW was trying to hit the million again, erasing a decade of history, and we have Requiem 1. It was one of the biggest wars inside Vampire fandom. Of course, Requiem has it's merits, but is not the Masurradez and the VtM fandom wanted the Masquerade. Now we have Requiems mechanics (touchstones, bloody potency, streamlined disciplines). And as you can see in the forums, it is not accepted in the VtM fandom. We wanted the Masquerade, not, well, this. There were a reason to clans and lineages, to generation and disciplines as they were. And now that this mix up was done, they killed two lines: VtM and VtR. VtR is redundant and VtM, well, is VtM in name only","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T11:36:57-08:00","id":1528657,"title":"","content":"Tbh, it should've never existed but it's too late for that. Instead, here's my suggestions for V6.<br /> <br /> Officially retcon the entire metaplot. Yes, really. Don't just go metaplot neutral like V20 did and don't fully scrap the setting like Requiem did. Declare Beckett's Jyhad Diary to be non-canon. Officially de-canonize every book released after the Revised Edition corebook but keep them for sale on Storyteller's Vault with a disclaimer.<br /> <br /> Literally reset the canon back to the way it was in 1e. And I mean the ACTUAL 1e/early 2e, NOT the revisionist &quot;boring pretentious street level personal horror uber alles&quot; narrative that parts of the V5 crowd like to push. Fully embrace the &quot;Vampions/Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas&quot; badwrongfun and give the middle finger to the hoity-toity above-it-all &quot;Personal horror and metaplot uber alles! Anything else is badwrongfun&quot; extremely toxic subsect of the fanbase.<br /> <br /> Like fully declare &quot;Revised and V5 never happened:<br /> <br /> Let's be real here, Vampire 1e was pure Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas badwrongfun even though it paid lip service to personal horror in a ploy to sell the game to goths, punks, and arthouse hipsters. Chicago By Night 1e, Alien Hunger, Ashes to Ashes, or the more out there stuff in The Hunters Hunted. It's all badwrongfun Supers With Fangs that pays bare minimum lip service to the &quot;woe is me&quot; bourgeois types and that's when VTM is at its best. Having their cake and eating it too.<br /> <br /> No changing the names of clans or eliminating clans, just do a hard reset and declare that all the events of Revised never happened. No Week of Nighmares, no Gangrel or Brujah leaving the Camarilla, no Ministry of Set (it's still Followers of Set), no Second Inquisition, none of that garbage.<br /> <br /> Maybe have V5 and the like be declared an alternate continuity exiled from the main WoD but still supported via the Storytellers Vault to satisfy the angst-ridden bourgeoisie who cling to WW metaplot as if it were holy scriptures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-16-2024, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T12:34:54-08:00","id":1528662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528502#post1528502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's OK for stories to end. And to be blunt, the story of the original World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade ended 20 years ago with the Time of Judgment event.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem as I see it is that while stories have endings, Vampire the Masquerade was not a story. It was a roleplaying game with the World of Darkness as its setting. The stories that have endings would be the individual chronicles that the gamemaster and players created at their game table. And people will always have more stories to create as long as they and their friends have ideas. Simply because Justin Achilli had one story he wanted to tell and created a metaplot to force down everyone's throats does not mean anyone else wanted that story. Obviously they didn't.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't people who liked playing a game where the protagonists are vampires in 1991, 1994, 2000, 2004, and any number of historical settings not want to play stories set &quot;today&quot; when today becomes 2008, 2011, 2014, 2023, and so on?<br /> <br /> Stories end. Settings go on. There's very few stories out there where we know the world itself ends simply because we're on the last page.<br /> <br /> There was no reason why VtM or the other WoD gamelines had to become a zombie franchise. New people are entering the hobby and enjoying the genre every year. Most people on this forum, I believe, were not around - perhaps not even born - when my friends and I first played VtM back in 1992. Companies still sell the original Stratego, Risk, Monopoly, Clue, and many other boardgames. They just update the marketing and trade design every so often. And while there are spin offs from some of these games tying them into other franchises (the various Monopoly games that simply rename the street names), it's understood that these are merely collectible versions, not replacements.<br /> <br /> The idea that RPGs and their settings are essentially fiction written by the game developers to be read passively by players rather than a game that tells an emergent story collaboratively created by gamemasters and players has been very destructive to the hobby. We have entire sourcebooks that aren't actually meant to be used by gamemasters in play, but passively consumed like it was fiction. I understand some people really like this &quot;form&quot; of fiction, but in my experience it alienates a whole lot more people than it attracts.<br /> <br /> Metaplot kills gamelines. Having updated settings just to update settings and try to force people to buy new sourcebooks just pisses people off because there is no value for their money. This does not mean that the chronology of the setting has to remain static. People will always set new chronicles in more recent years. It doesn't have to remain in 1991 forever. But that doesn't mean in terms of vampire society that 2024 has to be different from 1991 in a way that 1991 was different from 1900, 1848, 1776, 1648, or 1525. No reason to start moving clans around sects and other fundamental alterations of the setting that both Revised and V5 have done.<br /> <br /> I am willing to carve out partial exemptions to time-limited &quot;mystery bombs&quot; that were meant to go off during the production of the game. The mystery behind the origins of the Devil Kindred, their predecessors, the Antedeluvian they killed, etc. was always something (I think) that was meant to be resolved. So after introducing the Cappadocans in the Giovanni Chronicles and Vampire: the Dark Ages, something like the Hecata was always inevitable. Recognizing that there were many other Cappadocian survivors and their childer than just the Giovanni was OK. Something like the Hecata simply brings the various strands together in a more coherent and universal framework like how the Revised corebook initially just brought EVERYTHING together into one corebook so people didn't have to buy five separate books anymore just to have all the clans and various options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T12:39:51-08:00","id":1528663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528598#post1528598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;If I can't have London, the Camarilla can't. NYAH!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Mithras/Coven&quot;s fate is player-determined (thus no canon ending to him) and there are several possibilities what happens including Mithras' ritual is successful and gains his full power and became the ruler of United Kingdom...? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T12:48:40-08:00","id":1528664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528662#post1528662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand some people really like this &quot;form&quot; of fiction, but in my experience it alienates a whole lot more people than it attracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>A huge number of the original WW team would disagree at least for the WoD. That part of the WoD content sold, a lot, and was an essential part of making the WoD one of the biggest RPG franchises of the 90s.<br /> <br /> Whether it's still valuable today is something debatable, but at the time, it really wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T12:59:01-08:00","id":1528665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528664#post1528664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A huge number of the original WW team would disagree at least for the WoD. That part of the WoD content sold, a lot, and was an essential part of making the WoD one of the biggest RPG franchises of the 90s.<br /> <br /> Whether it's still valuable today is something debatable, but at the time, it really wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that approach came after the World of Darkness became successful. Prior to revised, the books published for <i>Vampire: the Masquerade </i>(and more broadly across the World of Darkness) were written primarily as game supplements, and this was the time when the World of Darkness was most successful. The shift to game-books-as-serial-fiction was a post-revised phenomenon, and one that was contentious even then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T13:22:30-08:00","id":1528668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given the TWENTY years the CofD has existed, then a person has to assume at least a portion of the fanbase has gotten over itself and no longer irrationally hates an IP and doesn't feel the necessity of spitting on an entire fanbase simply to utter untruths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have nothing against the CofD, since they keep being the CofD and not being hammered in the oWoD. These are different histories, with different premises, and because something works wonderfully on the CoD don't mean will work in the oWoD, as can be seen in the V5. Keeping both lines as different systems is better for everyone. New CoD material, new WoD material, less dissent between players. VtM is not VtR, and that doesn't mean VtR is horrible, just that is a different game, with different premises and the games shouldn't intermingle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T13:33:22-08:00","id":1528671,"title":"","content":"I don't have any strong links to the older versions of Chicago by Night and I enjoyed the sourcebook that they published considerably and preferred the fact that we had ended the war between Helena &amp; Menalus and got rid of the Ventrue ancient Rebekah who was also there. To many meths in one location can be a bad thing and don't we all take some creative liberties with the ongoing metaplot? I know from a post I did at least a year ago on that topic seemed to suggest that not many players followed the cannon that closely.<br /> <br /> In closing I actually enjoy the current setting right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T13:35:18-08:00","id":1528672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528551#post1528551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But fall of london isnt very good.....</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it was the weakest of the sourcebooks in the new setting and I just use it as a reference for my main character background and which of the Kindred he might have dealings with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:16:58-08:00","id":1528677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528665#post1528665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that approach came after the World of Darkness became successful. Prior to revised, the books published for <i>Vampire: the Masquerade </i>(and more broadly across the World of Darkness) were written primarily as game supplements, and this was the time when the World of Darkness was most successful. The shift to game-books-as-serial-fiction was a post-revised phenomenon, and one that was contentious even then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're viewing things with rose-tinted glasses here. There are serialized stories in the WoD source books that started in 92 an 93... well before the game completely took off, and was prominent throughout 2e (mostly because 1e was too brief to really see it happen).<br /> <br /> It only got more noticeable in Revised because (a) WW started more actively courting that part of the fanbase as the group most likely to support the supplement treadmill and (b) it was used heavily in the 2e-to-Revied transition period because of the major metaplot events that happened at the end of 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:30:28-08:00","id":1528678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then maybe don't say shit like VtR is redundant.<br /> <br /> For that matter, the decision to end the original WoD run was a commercial decision as much as a creative one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll break down to you. Since V5 is hammering VtR mechanics (very poorly) it makes no sense to keep publishing new material, because, editorially, the games are fused in one, so, VtR is editorially redundant. If V5 keeps like that, there won't be new CofD, because they're now canonically oWoD. Now is clearer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:53:43-08:00","id":1528679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528677#post1528677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're viewing things with rose-tinted glasses here. There are serialized stories in the WoD source books that started in 92 an 93... well before the game completely took off, and was prominent throughout 2e (mostly because 1e was too brief to really see it happen).<br /> <br /> It only got more noticeable in Revised because (a) WW started more actively courting that part of the fanbase as the group most likely to support the supplement treadmill and (b) it was used heavily in the 2e-to-Revied transition period because of the major metaplot events that happened at the end of 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can't say it wasn't serialized when Under a Blood Red Moon and Chicago by Night 2nd Edition utterly upended the Chicago Chronicles portion of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:55:26-08:00","id":1528682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528663#post1528663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Mithras/Coven&quot;s fate is player-determined (thus no canon ending to him) and there are several possibilities what happens including Mithras' ritual is successful and gains his full power and became the ruler of United Kingdom...?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how the story ends, Mithras burning London down and trying to gain ULTIMATE POWER at the end still happens.<br /> <br /> I think the PCs determining how that plays out is the best way to solve these kind of metaplot events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T14:57:58-08:00","id":1528683,"title":"","content":"The V5 supplements haven't done anything that particularly backs up the idea that V5 is going to continue to take ideas from VtR (in fact, it's more the opposite at this point), H5 and W5 even scaled back taking stuff from their CofD counterparts by a huge degree. The WoD5 books are still looking for ideas from other games to try to make games that seem more modern (H5's danger track for example, like Loresheets before it, was lifted from non-WoD related games), but the idea that the current teams at Paradox and Renegade are trying to further mash the WoD and CofD together doesn't hold up to a lick of scrutiny.<br /> <br /> And so, they didn't kill CofD because it was redundant, they killed it because CofD fans liked it better than WoD5. Vigil 2e outsold H5 on DTRPG, as a data point on that. Despite how much they liberally lift game ideas from other games, Paradox thinks stopping the CofD is going to magically &quot;reunify&quot; the different fan groups instead of just pissing people off so people go elsewhere (or just the STV) for new CofD stuff.<br /> <br /> And they have killed it in all but official cancellation: Paradox refuses to greenlight new CofD books. Calling it &quot;editorial&quot; redundancy is giving the decision makers far too much credit as business folks. The 20th books and the CofD 2e books coexisted just fine. They're not redundant. They're not redundant despite some cross-pollination that happened during that period as Onyx Path folks were working on both lines. V5 and VtR are only redundant on Paradox's financial spreadsheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T17:32:53-08:00","id":1528692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528682#post1528682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No matter how the story ends, Mithras burning London down and trying to gain ULTIMATE POWER at the end still happens.<br /> <br /> I think the PCs determining how that plays out is the best way to solve these kind of metaplot events.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the way I prefer to see metaplot in games. You get the broad outline &quot;this character dies. This event happens,&quot; and then the book provides information on the setting and the way the situation has built up to this point, but then leave it up to the ST and players to figure out how the events actually play out. The worst way is when the metaplot is on rails like To Grandmother's House We Go, which is (on many levels) among the worst metaplot adventures I've seen in an RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T17:34:15-08:00","id":1528693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528692#post1528692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the way I prefer to see metaplot in games. You get the broad outline &quot;this character dies. This event happens,&quot; and then the book provides information on the setting and the way the situation has built up to this point, but then leave it up to the ST and players to figure out how the events actually play out. The worst way is when the metaplot is on rails like To Grandmother's House We Go, which is (on many levels) among the worst metaplot adventures I've seen in an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is the nadir.<br /> <br /> The PCs don't even need to be there and Baba Yaga was a werewolf villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T19:38:35-08:00","id":1528700,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">What ideas does take V5 from Requiem?<br /> <br /> The only thing it takes are the &quot;names&quot; of two concepts Touchstones and Blood Potency but they operate in completely different way.<br /> <br /> <b>Ex:</b> In Requiem touchstones are optional and can be objects, rivals or even objectives.<br /> <br /> <b>Ex 2: </b>Blood Potency in requiem is incredible strong: it adds two dices per blood point spent to distribute between strengh, dexterity or stamina. If you frenzy you add your blood potency to physical stats with means that without accounting for disciplines a vampire with blood potency 10 can add +30 to physical stats and + 10 to all others before even accounting disciplines and devotions which can make the buff higher.<br /> <br /> Time of Judgement Sara the Maker vs Absimiliard trowing buildings to each other can be representated in requiem 2ND ed with the core mechanics.<br /> <br /> In other words requiem is a game that gives mechanics to actually represent antediluvian power level. Something that previous editions do not do, choosing instead to mask their lack of work in that regard as &quot;plot device powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Seriusly those comparing V5 to Vampire the Requiem have no idea and i would like to know the origin of their hate hard on. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T19:50:20-08:00","id":1528701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528678#post1528678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I'll break down to you. Since V5 is hammering VtR mechanics (very poorly) it makes no sense to keep publishing new material, because, editorially, the games are fused in one, so, VtR is editorially redundant. If V5 keeps like that, there won't be new CofD, because they're now canonically oWoD. Now is clearer?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">They are not hammering any mechanic from requiem. I wish they did, but they do not. <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b><u>In fact V5 is the Opposite or Requiem. </u></b></i></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Requiem is a toolbox, you have multiple mechanics that allow you to customize the game, </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">V5 is restrictive and the system is so interconect that you cannot change anything without affecting other things or the core experience.</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Also Touchstones and blood potency operate completely different in Requiem. V5 only takes the name of them.<br /> <br /> Touchstones in requiem are <b><u>completely optional</u></b> and &quot;can be anything&quot; while in V5 are tied to convictions<br /> <br /> Blood Potency in Requiem can lead to +40 dice without counting disciplines or devotions. There is no hunger in Requiem, there is also no generation, roll dificulties are different, etc... Antediluvian power level is represented with mechanics in requiem.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>VTR fans dislike V5 because they are completely different or even opposites.</b> If you are gonna compare at least know what you are talking about instead of repeating a preconceived idea you have in your head without any actual basis.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T05:22:18-08:00","id":1528707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528678#post1528678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I'll break down to you. Since V5 is hammering VtR mechanics (very poorly) it makes no sense to keep publishing new material, because, editorially, the games are fused in one, so, VtR is editorially redundant. If V5 keeps like that, there won't be new CofD, because they're now canonically oWoD. Now is clearer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with that, but I certainly believe that Paradox's position and that's why we're likely to se less support for CofD anymore. Paradox believes that the 5th edition lines have successfully combined WoD and CofD, and continued support of CofD will cannibalize sales of WoD. Again, I don't think I agree with that, but if it's what Paradox believes that's all that matters in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T11:55:11-08:00","id":1528727,"title":"","content":"People are still hating on Vampire The Reqium? I thought we had moved on that and found it a worthy addition to the series. Though to be fair we have people who can hold grudges from events decades in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-17-2024, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T12:06:11-08:00","id":1528732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528663#post1528663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Mithras/Coven&quot;s fate is player-determined (thus no canon ending to him) and there are several possibilities what happens including Mithras' ritual is successful and gains his full power and became the ruler of United Kingdom...?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they leave options for Mithras at the end of the game. From gaining his full power and control of his new body, to only gaining control of his body but only a portion of his old might back, or him leaving because of the beckoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T14:35:20-08:00","id":1528753,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a>, tell me: since V1 till V20, nWoD and oWod, where is the first time blood potency and touchstones were put un the game? What's the oldest mention you can trace on the Vampire franchise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T15:54:28-08:00","id":1528757,"title":"","content":"Semantic hair splitting isn't the the argument you seem to think it is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27825_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27825\" data-vbnamecard=\"27825\">MrDrika</a>. The idea of &quot;blood potency&quot; not the specific implementation, has been part of Vampire from the beginning: that's what Generation is. How potent your blood is. The idea that certain sources of blood are worth more than others has also been in the game from the beginning. V5 just added greater levels of variation within each Generation (something fans had been asking for since the 90s to decrease the incentives for everyone to start with five dots in Generation). It did so by clunkily meshing Generation and VtR's &quot;Blood Potency&quot; trait; but that doesn't mean VtR 1e was the first time &quot;blood potency&quot; actually was something the Vampire games cared about just because it was the first time one of the games used it as a name for a trait.<br /> <br /> The same this is true of Touchstones. VtR just formalized something that was already narratively present and discussed in VtM. It gave a name to mechanics to something that was already supposed to be there. VtM had very early on established that maintaining close connections to humans was a key part of keeping your Humanity high/raising it. Did it call that &quot;Touchstones&quot; or have mechanics? No. But it was there from pretty much the the beginning when discussing the role-playing aspects of Humanity.<br /> <br /> If you think some sort of &quot;gotcha!&quot; game where VtR was the first to use these as explicit terms with explicit mechanics means anything? I find it more likely you've never actually read a VtM book or played one, than the possibility that you have a serious point to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T16:50:46-08:00","id":1528764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528753#post1528753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a>, tell me: since V1 till V20, nWoD and oWod, where is the first time blood potency and touchstones were put un the game? What's the oldest mention you can trace on the Vampire franchise?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">You known that someone is losing an argument when they avoid the actual debate start debating semantics.</span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">Blood Potency was a thing since at least Chicago By Night 1st edition, there Helena and Menele where said to be weaker because they just woke up and their powers where recovering. Mitras blood potency/generation getting weakened by the diablerie of monty coven was also a thing. Not to mention that vampires growing stronger with age was always a thing.<br /> <br /> Revised also mentions this as one of the reasons why vampires fear the elders as devour other vampires to empower themselves back, diablerie was also a crucial plot point in time of judgement where it was necesary for vampires to stabilize their powers and for antediluvians to reach their end game.<br /> <br /> Even the iconic bloodlines pc game has characters mention how your blood is getting stronger. As others have said Requiem just give actual mechanics to things that where always in the game. Antediluvian power level is undefined, however in requiem we get mechanics for them in the form of devotions and up to +40 dice bonus to physical stats without disciplines.<br /> <br /> The same happened to touchstones, let\u00b4s rembember that there is a merit called true love in masquerade. Requiem just gave mechanics to a narrative element that was always there.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">That said</span> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">everybody knows that both a Ferrari and a Rusty Fiat Pinto are cars but also everybody knowns that they are not the same at all. In the same way V5 and VTR mechanics are different in how they operate as Day and Night or in more simple words: <i>&quot;opposites.</i></span><i>&quot; This is basic logic and coherency.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\">It is a little sad to see someone desperate enough go to debate semantics because they known they lack reason. Also the fact that you try to demand proof when you are the one who made an affirmation without proof, while also ignoring the proof of others... well... your falacies go Brrr...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T22:29:41-08:00","id":1528779,"title":"","content":"Elder rules beyond combo disciplines. Proper canon story, not just &quot;Second Inquisition got Jalan, Talley killed Lucita, etc.&quot; sensationalist headlines.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T23:14:12-08:00","id":1528781,"title":"","content":"The greatest thing that would have helped V5 would have bene Bloodlines 2 releasing of course, but this Is out of our reach.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly happy with V5 , but here are some ideas I have in regards to better managing the line:<br /> <br /> -Either fully playable Sabbat or a book which thoroughly metaplottily explained why the Sabbat had collapsed and how to use the Gehenna War in your Chronicles.<br /> <br /> -Getting the Players Guide out significantly earlier<br /> <br /> -Explaining there or in the Core how to create Elders and Paths in the V5 framework<br /> <br /> -A V20 and VtR translation guide<br /> <br /> A general concept: I think the one thing that V5 really needed was continuity: It has changed way too many hands.<br /> <br /> The original team led by Martin Ericsson had a clear visione, which combined the aim of getting new players on board with attention to metaplot and lore philology.<br /> <br /> They were under constant attack, but so weee the following trans, and the juxtaposition of different creative agendas has been a bit of a mess.<br /> <br /> Taking the counterfactual to the extreme, Martin shouldn't have hired Zack S. This alone would have saved a lot of &quot;you're a secret nazi alt righter&quot; attacks, and not soaring the RPG.net board and user base would also have reduced a lot of negative coverage.<br /> <br /> Of course he should have managed differently the Chechenya situation.<br /> <br /> With a less hostile situation, they could have used the talents of Matthew Dawkins, Justin Achilli, Jason Carl and Kenneth Hite at their fullest, and possibly also the collaboration with Onyx Path would have been smoother.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T05:26:23-08:00","id":1528788,"title":"","content":"White Wolf/Paradox seem to be going away from heavy continuity and trying to distance themselves from the Old World of Darkness (naming it &quot;Legacy&quot;) just like they did Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> This is a fucking terrible idea and I hope they reverse course rapidly.<br /> <br /> We don't need a THIRD World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T05:35:33-08:00","id":1528790,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if your aim is to exploit nostalgia for the old World of Darkness, the worst thing you can do is take only the name and jettison everything else. You're just fracturing an already broken base even further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T05:44:26-08:00","id":1528791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528790#post1528790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if your aim is to exploit nostalgia for the old World of Darkness, the worst thing you can do is take only the name and jettison everything else. You're just fracturing an already broken base even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's also clearly a fight going on behind the scenes because as Justin Achilli is saying this, they're re-releasing:<br /> <br /> * Chicago by Night 5th Edition<br /> * Fall of London<br /> * Cults of the Blood Gods<br /> * The Book of Nod<br /> * The Book of Nod Apocrypha expansion<br /> <br /> And fuck, the 100+ Old World of Darkness novels.<br /> <br /> Hell, Chapters is based on the old write up of Montreal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T10:47:28-08:00","id":1528811,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the disaster that is V5 just vindicated the Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas/Supers With Fangs crowd completely in the long run while H5 and W5 further cemented said vindication.<br /> <br /> And with said vindication comes a repudiation of the Pretentious Personal Horror Uber Alles/&quot;So Deep and Artsy&quot; crowd as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T10:52:10-08:00","id":1528813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528640#post1528640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, as I have pointed out before, this makes it into Mithras's story, rather than the players' story, and, really, this is the completely wrong focus for a story or chronicle.<br /> <br /> One of the interesting developments in the World of Darkness as a publishing phenomenon is a shift, in the late 1990s, in White Wolf's intended audience. Prior to the revised edition of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, there was an expectation of a broad audience. Lots of players were expected to buy a few books, based upon their interests, and there was no great attempt to build a running narrative. Books were designed to be focused primarily on the player characters; you will notice in the early stories published for the game (<i>Alien Hunger</i>, <i>Blood Bond</i>, whatever) there are basically no big-name NPCs. Even the Diablerie series, which sees the appearance of a powerful Methuselah in each book, do not have much in the way of larger consequences through the survival, or otherwise, of their supporting case.<br /> <br /> This shifts massively with the revised edition. There seems to be an expectation that there are fewer people purchasing books, but that these are not players, but fans, and they are expected to be buying every book. All of a sudden we have signature characters. We have random bits of plot stuck in the back of books (for some fans, Lucita's defection to the Sabbat at the back of <i>Midnight Siege</i> was a big event; for people like me it was when we stopped bothering to buy books). Above all, published stories became slide shows where the actions of the players were inconsequential, and effectively fans were expected to be excited by witnessing important events in the game. The nadir of this trend is the Baba Yaga adventure in <i>Nights of Prophecy</i>, where the players have not one single meaningful choice. But it doesn't matter; they get to see the death of Baba Yaga, which, apparently, is the important bit.<br /> <br /> <i>Fall of London</i> takes all the wrong lessons from earlier incarnations of <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>. I don't care about what happens to Mithras, and I suspect that very few people other than the superfans do either. I don't even understand why anyone should care, unless we are treating these not as game supplements, but as (bad) novels masquerading as game supplements.<br /> <br /> One of the best adventures released for <i>Vampire</i> is <i>Clash of Wills,</i> which is arguably the last story published before the trend of catering to fans took off. There aren't any famous characters, pretty much everyone dies, and the events are inconsequential for the wider world. And it's fun. I wish the writers for the game would actually remember to focus on that last bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T10:52:34-08:00","id":1528814,"title":"","content":"I do like that they gave more detailed explainations for predator types as the earlier editions I do have just make a casual mention but not what kind of skills you would need or backgrounds and what else and they explain the drawback of what a low humanity kindred all entail and what kind of troubles they would have moving around the humans. All in all I do like the game in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T11:34:42-08:00","id":1528819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528811#post1528811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the disaster that is V5 just vindicated the Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas/Supers With Fangs crowd completely in the long run while H5 and W5 further cemented said vindication.<br /> <br /> And with said vindication comes a repudiation of the Pretentious Personal Horror Uber Alles/&quot;So Deep and Artsy&quot; crowd as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean calling it a disaster just obscures the actual criticisms of the work that are valid. It also makes the whole discussion look like sour grapes rather than deal with the artistic versus economic merits.<br /> <br /> It's a success financially. It's paid for itself. The brand is once more active and now has a global reach that it never did in 1999. Books are being put out. There have been multiple video games even if they're of dubious quality. Bloodlines 2 WILL be released. WOD5 is more successful than any previous edition has ever been. You can certainly criticize it ARTISTICALLY but critics for some reason think it FINANCIALLY somehow determines quality and I fucking hate that these days.<br /> <br /> Because whether its a<i> financial </i>success or not means shit. Yet all of these Youtube videos and critiques talk about the sales versus whether or not it's GOOD.<br /> <br /> I feel like people should be discussing that. Controversy has dogged WoD5. RIDICULOUS amounts of controversy up to and including governments threatening the lives of distributors. However, controversy sells and every time one of them happens, it just serves as publicity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T11:38:21-08:00","id":1528821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528662#post1528662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem as I see it is that while stories have endings, Vampire the Masquerade was not a story. It was a roleplaying game with the World of Darkness as its setting. The stories that have endings would be the individual chronicles that the gamemaster and players created at their game table. And people will always have more stories to create as long as they and their friends have ideas. Simply because Justin Achilli had one story he wanted to tell and created a metaplot to force down everyone's throats does not mean anyone else wanted that story. Obviously they didn't.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't people who liked playing a game where the protagonists are vampires in 1991, 1994, 2000, 2004, and any number of historical settings not want to play stories set &quot;today&quot; when today becomes 2008, 2011, 2014, 2023, and so on?<br /> <br /> Stories end. Settings go on. There's very few stories out there where we know the world itself ends simply because we're on the last page.<br /> <br /> There was no reason why VtM or the other WoD gamelines had to become a zombie franchise. New people are entering the hobby and enjoying the genre every year. Most people on this forum, I believe, were not around - perhaps not even born - when my friends and I first played VtM back in 1992. Companies still sell the original Stratego, Risk, Monopoly, Clue, and many other boardgames. They just update the marketing and trade design every so often. And while there are spin offs from some of these games tying them into other franchises (the various Monopoly games that simply rename the street names), it's understood that these are merely collectible versions, not replacements.<br /> <br /> The idea that RPGs and their settings are essentially fiction written by the game developers to be read passively by players rather than a game that tells an emergent story collaboratively created by gamemasters and players has been very destructive to the hobby. We have entire sourcebooks that aren't actually meant to be used by gamemasters in play, but passively consumed like it was fiction. I understand some people really like this &quot;form&quot; of fiction, but in my experience it alienates a whole lot more people than it attracts.<br /> <br /> Metaplot kills gamelines. Having updated settings just to update settings and try to force people to buy new sourcebooks just pisses people off because there is no value for their money. This does not mean that the chronology of the setting has to remain static. People will always set new chronicles in more recent years. It doesn't have to remain in 1991 forever. But that doesn't mean in terms of vampire society that 2024 has to be different from 1991 in a way that 1991 was different from 1900, 1848, 1776, 1648, or 1525. No reason to start moving clans around sects and other fundamental alterations of the setting that both Revised and V5 have done.<br /> <br /> I am willing to carve out partial exemptions to time-limited &quot;mystery bombs&quot; that were meant to go off during the production of the game. The mystery behind the origins of the Devil Kindred, their predecessors, the Antedeluvian they killed, etc. was always something (I think) that was meant to be resolved. So after introducing the Cappadocans in the Giovanni Chronicles and Vampire: the Dark Ages, something like the Hecata was always inevitable. Recognizing that there were many other Cappadocian survivors and their childer than just the Giovanni was OK. Something like the Hecata simply brings the various strands together in a more coherent and universal framework like how the Revised corebook initially just brought EVERYTHING together into one corebook so people didn't have to buy five separate books anymore just to have all the clans and various options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a very different view on metaplot. Forgive me if I go on a bit of a rant.<br /> <br /> A bit more explanation but a simple question for any person who wants to talk about metaplot. &quot;Do you give a shit about the characters in your favorite media?&quot; This is the most fundamental question you can ask about any property you have any investment in. Do you care about Spider-Man? Do you care about Mary Jane? Do you have any investment in Iron Man or Captain America or Wolverine or so on? What about Harry Potter or Katniss Everdeen. They are fictional characters and nothing that happens to them matters. HOWEVER, it is a story that you must fundamentally have BUY IN for if you want to buy anything.<br /> <br /> I CARE about the characters of Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I care about Lucita, I care about Theo Bell, I care about Victoria Ash, and I care about Lodin and Modius. So much so that I wrote an adventure to wrap up the characters in Gary for Storyteller's Vault and have played HUNDREDS of stories involving them with my player characters. They are not as real to me as real people but they are toys that I have played with and I want to see/read/hear more about them.<br /> <br /> I don't need rituals, I don't need Disciplines, and i certainly don't need books about new Clans.<br /> <br /> I am here because the game world as established in Legacy/OWOD has enough characters that I want to know more about what they've been up to for the past 20 years. I *LIKE* The Old World of Darkness because I like the characters that live in it. I don't play it because of the system, I play it for the world that has been created and the chance to play around in it.<br /> <br /> It's why I fundamentally enjoy Beckett's Jyhad DIary more than any other book ever written because it is the book of, &quot;Hey, remenber these guys?&quot; Without metaplot, the characters are frozen and static and the supplements don't provide you anything other than empty rules. It's why I've never really cared about Eberron versus, say, Dragonlance or Forgotten Realms.<br /> <br /> &quot;What is Raistlin up to?&quot; is a question far more press than King Boranal. Because King Boranal is the same place he was a decade ago. Because Eberron's timeline doesn't advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-18-2024, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T12:39:29-08:00","id":1528823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528788#post1528788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf/Paradox seem to be going away from heavy continuity and trying to distance themselves from the Old World of Darkness (naming it &quot;Legacy&quot;) just like they did Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> This is a fucking terrible idea and I hope they reverse course rapidly.<br /> <br /> We don't need a THIRD World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm usually a lurker, but I've been wanting to post on this specific topic for a couple days now. What you're saying is part of the reason. I'm going to try and keep my post as short as I can because I could write a whole darn essay on this. Just the important information: I was brought into the VTM fandom via V5, I've never played a game outside of that edition, and I frequent multiple WoD communities to try and get an all-around view of fan opinions.<br /> <br /> V5 had me in the first half. I enjoyed the Corebook, played Bloodlines and proceeded to buy every book that was currently out (Chicago by Night was the latest). I went on wiki pages and fell in love with the lore. I know not everyone is going to do as I do, but it's not nearly as bone-crushing a feat like I see it made out to be. Unless you're trying to be a true VTM scholar you can get the gist of a lot of things through wiki-surfing and asking older players. <br /> <br /> So that's why I'm always really surprised when people get so frustrated with old lore. The whole &quot;Make up your own thing&quot; is IMO evident in any TTRPG you play, but lore should be there for people who <i>don't </i>want to do that, also, it's much easier to drop something than make something up from scratch. When I first got into the V5 fandom people did dismiss some older stuff, but they were the most commonly dismissed content (ie. the Kuei Jin). still they enjoyed a lot of legacy and waited with bated breath for new releases old material. Then this odd shift started happening where there was, the best way I can put it, <i>hostility </i>towards old lore among some fans. This hostility is very odd to me for several reasons, but the biggest is that a lot of these players seemed just fine with old lore until-well, rather recently?<br /> <br /> Paradox distancing themselves from old lore came as a comment in the official Discord server via the pipelines. The exact comment was something like: &quot;The game is imagined as a complete reboot now, if we don't reference something it's not true in-lore anymore.&quot; I can't even say this is absolute truth. Like, it might be true technically <i>now,</i> but right at the same time, they released the DoC loresheet. We still had Bloodhunt kicking and dropping old names, and they've continued to reintroduce old (albeit with new tweaks/definitions ie. Gargoyles) powers and concepts. It's very much a &quot;Trying to have your cake and eat it too&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> They say they desire to distance themselves, but at this point that's impossible. You don't really get to say &quot;No, nothing matters anymore&quot; when that wasn't and had not been the concept. When you still expect a certain level of old player onboarding with newer players because if lore doesn't matter, why are you name-dropping things that only legacy players have an understanding of? Why aren't you explaining in detail those things if you want to bring them back? No new player cares about Gargoyles, so why did you name a new line of ghouls after them, and then talk about their legacy history in a curtly? Why do I care about Custos being the childe of Beckett?Why did you release the Book of Nod PDF? Because you're using an old gameline's history to sell your current edition.<br /> <br /> VTM is VTM because it's VTM. I could have played other vampire games, but chose this one because I was intrigued by its history. My group which also consists of new players feels similar. Hell, my friends who have never played think the choice to remove old lore is odd. V5 is my first time coming across such an obvious attempt at fracturing a fanbase. Ad if embracing the old will ruin your chances for the new. It's confounding.<br /> <br /> I still really like V5, but I don't like its current direction. If you aren't going to include &quot;old lore&quot; then write me up a new city book please, because the only reference I have is steeped in the old lore. Do the work it requires for having a &quot;new&quot; line. Give me full explanations and more tools since you don't seem to want me to use the old ones previously suggested. Just my current thoughts as a V5 player. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27814-agornitha","name":"Agornitha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27814_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T12:59:52-08:00","id":1528826,"title":"","content":"Awesome response and I 100% agree.<br /> <br /> Humorously, I *DID* end up writing an essay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/why-metaplot-matters-in-world-of.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/why-metaplot-matters-in-world-of.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/why-metaplot-matters-in-world-of.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/why-metaplot-matters-in-world-of.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer