18T17:16:17-08:00","id":1528851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528849#post1528849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 10 to 1 odds is that Lucita isn't really gone and she is still active in her city. There is some hints that Talley didn't take her down at all and something else is happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked that the Sabbat book flat out says that Sabbat Lucita is an imposter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:17:26-08:00","id":1528852,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Matt Corleone;n1528811]Honestly, I think the disaster that is V5 just vindicated the Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas/Supers With Fangs crowd completely in the long run while H5 and W5 further cemented said vindication.<br /> <br /> Strange I never was a trenchcoat and katana dude and loved the James Bond look myself with fangs or the Sherlock Holmes with a cowboy vibe look.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T18:21:22-08:00","id":1528863,"title":"","content":"I can say I'm not against camp in my VtM games.<br /> <br /> Hell, I literally wrote a luchador Nosferatu into this chronicle for no other reason than if a scene starts getting excessively boring or stupid, I can interrupt it by blasting reggaeton, and have him show up, dropkick someone or deliver a chair shot before running off. Maybe start a good old fashioned feud with a PC or something stupid. Or, send his famulus (a pigeon which, naturally has a tiny little luchador mask matching his own) to crap on someone, or his three-dot Retainer who's a ghouled mini-estrella. He's even an Osiris, and his Herd are ring girls.<br /> <br /> Lucha libre is awesome, Nosferatu are awesome. Luchador Nosferatu is awesome squared. Especially since he's the Prince's herald, he delivers every one of her proclamations or edicts as he would a wrestling promo.<br /> <br /> But the setting is deliberately designed as post-Gehenna, and it drives home how vampires are <i>really</i> scraping the bottom of the barrel to have anything approaching a functioning society for a guy <i>this</i> expressly stupid to be Herald. And this particular Nosferatu has a <i>really</i> depressing backstory, about how he played rudo to his mortal brother's tecnico, and their big break was this grand and elaborately planned storyline where they were going to switch roles...then he was Embraced by an elder who didn't understand kayfabe, for him to get his &quot;revenge&quot;. Now, he gets to play rudo...<i>forever</i>.<br /> <br /> Camp is fun, but I'm all about satire and substance. &quot;Trenchcoats and katanas&quot; provides the former, but not necessarily the latter, and for that it just comes off as terribly edgelord to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T22:55:00-08:00","id":1528872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528811#post1528811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the disaster that is V5 just vindicated the Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas/Supers With Fangs crowd completely in the long run while H5 and W5 further cemented said vindication.<br /> <br /> And with said vindication comes a repudiation of the Pretentious Personal Horror Uber Alles/&quot;So Deep and Artsy&quot; crowd as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been playing since 1999, had my Fair share of trenchcoat &amp; katanas characters, never bene into Deep and Artsy games, and I would never ever use &quot;Legacy&quot; rules again for a T&amp;K Vampire game.<br /> <br /> After having tried V5 Combat rules, the sheer thought of going back to 4 Rolls just to see if I hurt you scares me \ud83d\ude01<br /> <br /> I much prefer V5 rules, which can be supplemented with Free Advanced rules and the W5 and H5 new Combat gimmicks. We have Critical Damage rules!<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition as a book also has quite HUGE Trenchcoat and Katanas vibes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T22:56:42-08:00","id":1528873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528844#post1528844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently, Justin doesn't work with Paradox anymore, which was quite surprising. He mentioned it on Facebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very old news, he left to head a new RPG project at the beginning of 2023.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T23:04:13-08:00","id":1528874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528840#post1528840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine the difference is Justin Achilli is a fan of Vampire: The Masquerade. So he's way more protective of that old lore.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, he seems (from what everyone else has said) to HATE Werewolf: The Apocalypse. Or at least isn't a fan of it. So that old lore goes right in the trash.<br /> <br /> Or at least someone in positions of power in Paradox has no love for Werewolf (and Hunter: The Reckoning). I don't want to make assertions about individual people. All that's clear is that Vampire got preferential treatment to its existing lore, while the other games are almost complete reboots. (And what gets retained is mangled or, in the case of the Get of Fenris, <i>slandered</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I've observed , it's a lead development issue.<br /> <br /> As Lead Developers, both Martin Ericsson and Matthew Dawkins were for a soft retcon with a philological continuation for all games.<br /> <br /> Justin and Renegade team are into soft reboot (hard reboot being CoFD).<br /> <br /> That said, they all have shown love and committment to the IP. I mean, everyone Is judging Justin's work on W5 on his personal taste as expressed in early 2000s Forum Wars. <br /> <br /> So , he Is the One being slandered way more than the GoF, if you allow me an hot take: his professionalism and impressive game design curriculum are considered less important than 20-years old discussione on long dead forums.<br /> <br /> This Is grudgebearing on a Warhammer Dwarves' scale!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T00:30:06-08:00","id":1528876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528874#post1528874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I've observed , it's a lead development issue.<br /> <br /> As Lead Developers, both Martin Ericsson and Matthew Dawkins were for a soft retcon with a philological continuation for all games.<br /> <br /> Justin and Renegade team are into soft reboot (hard reboot being CoFD).<br /> <br /> That said, they all have shown love and committment to the IP. I mean, everyone Is judging Justin's work on W5 on his personal taste as expressed in early 2000s Forum Wars.<br /> <br /> So , he Is the One being slandered way more than the GoF, if you allow me an hot take: his professionalism and impressive game design curriculum are considered less important than 20-years old discussione on long dead forums.<br /> <br /> This Is grudgebearing on a Warhammer Dwarves' scale!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Justin did lead us along about the true reason that the Get weren't present, for many months, and oddly thought that dedicated items detracted from the horror of the setting. That said, still not nearly on the level of Karim's &quot;One tribe of Indigenous American Garou is more than enough!&quot; shit, or his desire to ignore the Fenrir killing off the Swords of Heimdall to make the Swords the entire tribe, which then got quieted down and shuffled into Hauglosk turning Garou into fascists.<br /> <br /> At least Justin's decisions weren't predicated on assuming LARP as the default, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T01:42:45-08:00","id":1528878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528874#post1528874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I've observed , it's a lead development issue.<br /> <br /> As Lead Developers, both Martin Ericsson and Matthew Dawkins were for a soft retcon with a philological continuation for all games.<br /> <br /> Justin and Renegade team are into soft reboot (hard reboot being CoFD).<br /> <br /> That said, they all have shown love and committment to the IP. I mean, everyone Is judging Justin's work on W5 on his personal taste as expressed in early 2000s Forum Wars.<br /> <br /> So , he Is the One being slandered way more than the GoF, if you allow me an hot take: his professionalism and impressive game design curriculum are considered less important than 20-years old discussione on long dead forums.<br /> <br /> This Is grudgebearing on a Warhammer Dwarves' scale!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Justin did say stuff like how if you like the lore of the WOD then WOD5E isn't for you and you should play the 20th Anniversary edition instead. Then there was the odd excuse for why the Get of Fenris were turned into antagonists. He claimed the reason was that no one on the writing-team could come up with four distinct verbs for the Tribe. Throwing the people who worked on the game under the bus like that wasn't nice. Even more so because it wasn't the real reason. Also, the fact that parts of the book copied work from the canceled Hunters Entertainment W5-version was never officially mentioned. We only learned about that because JF Sambrano spoke out.<br /> <br /> Also, let's not forget how exactly it all went down when he left. In October 2022 you got the first preview for W5 and then you fast forward to January 2023 when Justin Achilli declares the writing-process to be over - only to follow that up a couple of days later with how he would leave as lead-developer and he also already had a new job lined up that he would start at immediately. The writing was finished but everything else (editing, layout etc.) wasn't finished. So he left way before the book was actually finished. When the scandal surrounding the Glass-Walker-preview happened with the traced photo, Justin Achilli was already long gone. That whole process was... odd, to say the least. Was the writing-process really finished? Or did it just have to be finished because Justin Achilli had already lined up another job? Since when did he know that he would hard-out in January 2023? Did it distract him?<br /> <br /> And then it was also weird for Paradox to not have any sort of transition prepared in advance for when Justin Achilli left. The in-house WOD-team at Paradox still doesn't have a replacement for Justin Achilli's position. Who knows what's even going on over there these days...Is development happening on the next corebook? Who knows... maybe... I guess we'll see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T02:13:25-08:00","id":1528880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528878#post1528878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Justin did say stuff like how if you like the lore of the WOD then WOD5E isn't for you and you should play the 20th Anniversary edition instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's look at <i>DrivethruRPG</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, 20th Anniversary edition: current sales position is 42.<br /> <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, fifth edition: current sales position is 92.<br /> <br /> It does look like people are taking his advice...<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know it's a bit of a cheap shot, and that V5 has other sales outlets. It's still, however, hardly an endorsement of the current edition of the game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T03:47:04-08:00","id":1528886,"title":"","content":"I rarely wade into this part of the forum these days, but I'll ramble a little.<br /> <br /> In my view, it's quite possible for V5 to have (or have had) the best of both worlds - entry level, accessible books with little to no metaplot (as James mentions, books like Diablerie: Mexico, Alien Hunger, etc. - and we have them in the form of Trails of Ash and Bone and the Players Guide - which I still think needs an apostrophe), <b>and </b>metaplot heavy, world expanding books (as CT mentions, Beckett's Jyhad Diary, though I'd put it at the extreme end of that wedge - and we have them in the form of Cults of the Blood Gods and Forbidden Religions). I anticipate we'll keep making books of both types at Onyx Path, albeit not for Vampire or the World of Darkness, specifically.<br /> <br /> One approach does not eliminate the other. But designers and fans alike can become tribal and see one thing as ruining, or harming the other, and so they pivot to &quot;this is my way and your way doesn't work for me, brother.&quot; It's perfectly normal for any artist to want to leave their own mark or steer a property under their control in a way that appeals to them, and they think the audience will appreciate. Some new fans will jump on the changes as a good thing, some old fans will jump off because they see the changes as a bad thing. As we see with a lot of long lasting fictional worlds (DC with the New 52; Doctor Who's various regenerations under different showrunners; Mortal Kombat's recent reboot, just to name a few), it's impossible to launch a new &quot;edition&quot; or introduce a metaplot shake-up without pissing some people off. But I very much believe it's possible to make one edition connect to another coherently and satisfy audiences from both camps (not 100% of the audience, ever, but some), even if some of that audience avoids picking up <i>this </i>book in favour of <i>that</i> book. Being able to say &quot;this book isn't for me but I'm looking forward to the next one&quot; is a much healthier mindset than &quot;this book killed the line and my enthusiasm.&quot;<br /> <br /> The fault, dear Brutus, is not in our stars, but in our selves. We shouldn't see every book as something we should be beholden to, no more than a fan of Doom Patrol in the New 52 should be expected to buy Green Arrow just because he crosses over with them in one issue. And that's okay. If you like V5 just based on the core book and can run a thousand plots from it alone, that's just as fine as wanting to buy every book because you want to keep up with the adventures of Lucita. I'd argue that for the Storyteller who can do that, V5 has been a tremendous success.<br /> <br /> I see metaplot as a hook to keep people engaged and interested, but not one that's going to work for everyone, which means I try to ensure every book has <i>some</i> metaplot and <i>some </i>material for people who aren't interested in that kind of thing. I can see from this thread that there are real fans of metaplot and people who don't give a damn about Theo Bell et al. For all that there are some people saying &quot;I don't want another book of Thaumaturgy rituals&quot; or whatever, it's books of powers and player options that always sell the best across the entire RPG industry, including Vampire. I'm sure Renegade's newest Blood Sigils book has done very well. So these books need to exist to cater to the fans who want them, just as books with metaplot content need to exist for other fans. And I think material to satisfy both can exist in the same book each time. You can probably tell from all the books I developed for V5 that that was my design philosophy. <br /> <br /> And you can by all means disagree as to whether it worked.<br /> <br /> This thread shows there are a lot of different, clashing views as to &quot;what would have been better for V5?&quot; Everyone has an opinion. For me, I developed the game I'd want to run or play, barring instances where I was obliged to add this thing or that thing at the behest of the license owner. In none of those cases did it ruin Vampire for me. You pick and choose the bits you want to use and keep the rest of the toys in their box.<br /> <br /> As an aside, as the co-developer of Beckett's Jyhad Diary, and a frequent writer and developer for the first few years of V5, I refute the common complaint that we didn't continue the plots in BJD. We were never going to do that with every single plot, because the plots introduced in that book are there for players to explore and resolve in their chronicles. The fundamental complaint about Vampire of old is that Lucita and Anatole, or whichever NPC was flavour of the month, would move the plot along regardless of the players' actions. I still think this is a silly complaint, as a decent Storyteller would insert the protagonists into pivotal roles instead of using the stand-in NPCs. But despite my view, I'm aware of the complaint that &quot;this chronicle just lets me sit back and watch as NPCs complete the story&quot; (then <i>do something!</i>), so it would have made no sense for Beckett to write a sequel resolving every single plot hook of the hundreds introduced in BJD. I made links to at least a handful of plots in BJD (and other V20 and earlier books) in every V5 book I worked on, and that ended when I stopped working on V5, but that just means the plot is there for you to explore. If, for example, we had the plot of Enoch waking up from BJD be immediately resolved in V5, what would be the point of introducing it in BJD? Those plots are open for a reason, and part of the reason I enjoyed V20 so much was it enabled me to expand metaplot without furthering it. BJD is a tool. Storytellers and players who see metaplot as a limitation to play (&quot;the Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting says Thay is now overrun with undead so we can't play our games set there&quot;) would probably be better off not engaging with it. <br /> <br /> If you're a fan of old metaplot and you want to see it in V5, it's a valid criticism to say &quot;I want to see more of this.&quot; It's less valid to say &quot;It's not there&quot; because it is, at least in most of the books. It may not be the metaplot you in particular want to see, but who really was going to continue the story of the Blood Brother psycho surgeon Dr. Varona? <br /> <br /> As another aside, I'm no big advocate for The Fall of London. I agree it's one of the weakest V5 books, for a myriad of reasons not relating to the quality of the writers. I remember sitting on the balcony at the Modiphius offices, the summer heat scorching the top of my head (back then I had hair, but it was thinning), and discussing the plot they wanted in that book. They wanted a time-hopping, D&amp;D, Curse of Strahd style campaign. What came out isn't exactly that. But I find the idea that you could discount it due to Mithras's presence and plotting a little shallow. He's a key power player and antagonist and your characters are operating in his shadow, but that's one of the key elements of Vampire - powerful vampires push you around, so you can try to cut them off at the knees. Now, if your coterie decides to serve and save Mithras, good job bootlicker! You've helped the Powers That Be. If your coterie undermines him, that's even better. There's room for stories like that, and not everyone needs to like them. I'd argue The Fall of London would have appealed to a wider audience if it hadn't had the whole &quot;you wake after year of torpor&quot; start, but I'll stop beating around the weeds on this one. Point is, there are plenty of good reasons to dislike that chronicle, but I'd argue the presence of a controlling methuselah is pretty typical for Vampire.<br /> <br /> Do I think V5 would have been better if it had removed all methuselahs and elders as it mooted doing in the core book? Absolutely not. Because it only mooted it, and in the same book (and Camarilla, and Chicago, etc.), had contemporary quotes from vampires such as Lucinde and Talley, who are hardly young fledglings. The point of the Beckoning is for Storytellers to pick and choose the elders they want to keep, and dispose of the rest. The reason Menele was removed but Helena was not, in Chicago, was because we needed to show that the Beckoning affects vampires differently, and some devise methods of staving it off. Nerissa was added at the request of Paradox, as I recall, and we were advised to keep several well known elder figures (Critias among them) to create that connectivity between editions of Vampire. Lucita and Vykos are later mentioned in the Sabbat book as still being around, so the Beckoning is, like BJD, a tool. Storytellers should use it to craft the World of Darkness they want. Wholesale removal of every one of these interesting characters would make Vampire a tonally different game.<br /> <br /> Anyway, work calls. Just wanted to dump my rambling thoughts out here. Have a good one!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T04:43:16-08:00","id":1528889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a>, can you recognize that the new bane of Lasombra was loosely based on the old clan's weakness? Or the phagocytosis of unique disciplines like Serpentis by Protean, Dementation by Dominate, Obtenebration and Necromancy/Mortis/Thanatosis/etc fused in Oblivion? Basically that the new things from V5 rooted ftom things that were already in game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T05:41:11-08:00","id":1528894,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the insights into how the sausage is made, particularly THE FALL OF LONDON, Matthew Dawkins.<br /> <br /> I think most of what you say is pretty common sense interpretation of how to deal with metaplot and how these things relate to your home game. I see metaplot as basically coming in two flavors for most games, you either use them as the basis for an adventure at your home game or it's background flavor for the world as a whole. Also, some of us with disposable income do buy all the books just to enjoy the setting for its own sake (Anatole or Ramona or Live Play NPCs as they may be).<br /> <br /> And yes, BJD is kind of on the extreme end of things but if you're a lore junkie like me (to an annoying level as everyone here can attest), it was pure sugar. I mean, I will never visit Istanbul with my group and never visited Constantinople in the Dark Ages but found the Michael and Mary the Black stuff fascinating. Ditto Vykos and Dracon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T11:25:36-08:00","id":1528934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528880#post1528880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's look at <i>DrivethruRPG</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, 20th Anniversary edition: current sales position is 42.<br /> <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i>, fifth edition: current sales position is 92.<br /> <br /> It does look like people are taking his advice...<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know it's a bit of a cheap shot, and that V5 has other sales outlets. It's still, however, hardly an endorsement of the current edition of the game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to consider Drivethrurpg is the main Sales channel people in the Anglosphere can get a copy of V20 core, while you can get V5 on Renegade website, retail stores, web shops and also Drivethrurpg. V20 has also some 7 years of additional massed sales on it's back.<br /> <br /> . Outside the Anglosphere, V20 core Is localized in different languages, and so Is V5, which however seems t\u00f2 have stronger distribution agreements.<br /> <br /> Also, we have icv2 sales data from the US market: V20 has never reached the top 5 Sales chart, while V5 has reached It three times since It went out.<br /> <br /> OPP kickstarters for C5 were all very successful.<br /> <br /> The RPG market is much wider than Drivethrurpg, nowadays. And luckily so!<br /> <br /> V5 hasn't succeeded in many of its stated goals, but as far as we know it has good commercial numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T11:30:27-08:00","id":1528936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528934#post1528934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 hasn't succeeded in many of its stated goals, but as far as we know it has good commercial numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest thing to say in V5's favor is they have international reach that V:TM flat out did not have before.<br /> <br /> The controversy for THE CAMARILLA wouldn't have been life threatening if there wasn't a Russian branch pumping out local copies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T14:43:17-08:00","id":1528948,"title":"","content":"We're doing this again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528934#post1528934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, we have icv2 sales data from the US market: V20 has never reached the top 5 Sales chart, while V5 has reached It three times since It went out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is even more meaningless than the DTRPG numbers.<br /> <br /> ICv2 primarily relies on surveys of physical distributors, and have been very slow in start to try to factor in e-commerce and crowdfunding numbers into their rankings. All of V20 sales numbers were never included in ICv2's considerations because at the time they didn't rank games that didn't have physical distribution at all. We have no idea how V20 would have ranked (and ICv2 can be kinda iffy because they don't do individual books, and have been extremely inconsistent on things like whether to count the World of Darkness as one entry, or each game-line separately), if all the V20 Kickstarters and DTRPG sales were actually considered by the survey, or even moreso how it would have ranked if ICv2 treated all the 20th books as one entry.<br /> <br /> DTRG is the one place where the two products are actually being directly compared to each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 hasn't succeeded in many of its stated goals, but as far as we know it has good commercial numbers. </div> </div> </div>We don't actually know this. As I've pointed out every time this comes up, we don't know what Paradox's numbers actually are. Selling more books isn't the same as having good commercial numbers. It's easier to look at other media like film where there's better tracking of things, where there are countless examples of box office bombs that still sold huge numbers of ticket.<br /> <br /> The best indicator we have of if Paradox considers V5 a success are their shareholder reports. The TTRPG side of the WOD hasn't been mentioned in their shareholder reports since they bought the IP. They haven't even reported if they've finally broken even on the purchase yet. Even for a smaller side project, a company always wants to report good things to shareholders. &quot;This multi-million dollar acquisition we made has completely recouped its cost, and is now printing you some extra money,&quot; is something Paradox would say to its shareholders if it was true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T15:48:06-08:00","id":1528952,"title":"","content":"DTRPG is utterly meaningless to sales numbers for discussing a book that is internationally distributed in stores. This isn't an irrelevant comment, this is just pointing out that there's an entire medium of sales that's not being counted and unquestionably the primary one.<br /> <br /> Also, I brought it up earlier, but why are people even caring about comparing sales figures? It has no relevance to the artistic merit and whenever it comes up in these discussion, it doesn't actually change anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The best indicator we have of if Paradox considers V5 a success are their shareholder reports. The TTRPG side of the WOD hasn't been mentioned in their shareholder reports since they bought the IP. They haven't even reported if they've finally broken even on the purchase yet. Even for a smaller side project, a company always wants to report good things to shareholders. &quot;This multi-million dollar acquisition we made has completely recouped its cost, and is now printing you some extra money,&quot; is something Paradox would say to its shareholders if it was true. </div> </div> </div>I mean, the shareholder reports indicates 100% of White Wolf LLC is licensing. Which is to say they don't actually get paid for any of these. So a better question is what does Renegade's shareholder reports say.<br /> <br /> Their shareholder report also still lists Bloodlines 2 being developed by Hardsuit labs that they own 1/3rd of (and haven't divested themselves of).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-19-2024, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T17:01:57-08:00","id":1528958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528952#post1528952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DTRPG is utterly meaningless to sales numbers for discussing a book that is internationally distributed in stores. This isn't an irrelevant comment, this is just pointing out that there's an entire medium of sales that's not being counted and unquestionably the primary one.</div> </div> </div> </div>DTRPG sells internationally.<br /> <br /> And there's not really much evidence that brick &amp; mortar sales are the primary sales medium for TTRPGs.... even D&amp;D is pushing to go even more digital and less physical. Physical stores matter, and have even had a resurgence on some level, but nobody in the TTRPG industry avoids online sales, while lots of TTRPG books don't have physical distribution at all. Nobody serious about making money off of their TTRPG is going to pick physical distribution only over digital distribution only. Ideally they'd have both, but maintaining both requires significant overhead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I brought it up earlier, but why are people even caring about comparing sales figures? </div> </div> </div>You're getting sucked into it too. You're not just trying to get people away from this line of discussion.<br /> <br /> And the why is simple: figures present an air of &quot;facts&quot; and thus objectivity, while artistic merit is a subjective judgement. Our personal feelings on the artistic merit of a book can be wildly different without either person being &quot;wrong.&quot; Citing a factual data point can't simply be disputed on opinions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It has no relevance to the artistic merit and whenever it comes up in these discussion, it doesn't actually change anything. </div> </div> </div>Has debating the artistic merit ever really changed anything either?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, the shareholder reports indicates 100% of White Wolf LLC is licensing. </div> </div> </div>White Wolf Entertainment AB (which is the official name as registered by Paradox) was eliminated as a separate entity and is just an imprint of Paradox now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is to say they don't actually get paid for any of these. </div> </div> </div>What? No. Paradox licenses out the WW IPs. Other people <b>pay Paradox</b> to make these things. Renegade pays Paradox to make WoD books. Onyx Path pays Paradox to make Exalted books. That revenue stream is part of what makes shares in the company valuable, and thus is important to shareholders. Paradox has a fiduciary duty to tell it's investors (aka shareholders) what it's doing with the stuff it paid a significant chunk of change for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So a better question is what does Renegade's shareholder reports say. </div> </div> </div>Renegade Games Studio isn't a publicly traded company. There are no shares to buy, thus there are no shareholders, or shareholders reports. This is why we know so little about the TTRPG industry: most of the companies are private and thus have no responsibility to publish certain information. We know so much more about things like traditional fiction printing, TV, and films, because they're dominated by publicly traded companies, and thus we can get their shareholder reports.<br /> <br /> Also, Renegade didn't pay 10m SEK for the IP rights, and doesn't have any fiscal responsibility to ensure said debt it addressed to other stakeholders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their shareholder report also still lists Bloodlines 2 being developed by Hardsuit labs that they own 1/3rd of (and haven't divested themselves of). </div> </div> </div>These things are quarterly, and then annual, on business schedules. When things get updated in them can seem very detached from what we know based on public statements from the company. That's why I read over 30 documents the last time I looked at this to actually see the big picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T17:46:18-08:00","id":1528963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528948#post1528948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're doing this again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, we can take this to infinity and beyond.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIn your arguments I see no corroborating evidence that an edition of a game, available both in print and Digital, in retail and on Amazon, localized in English, Spanish, Portuguese and all the European main languages, with the main distributore following a regular publishing schedule, and with good numbers on Drivethrurpg despite no need seelping there, as well as wide instances of good physical sales in the main world market, is significantly less successful than an edition which lived mainly on Kickstarters and indie distribution, and whose International licensing agreements were never as deep, in terms of following the line expansion.<br /> <br /> As for shareholder success, I'm fairly sure that considering that all of V5 revenue comes from licensing, Paradox probably gets from It as much as needed to pay the people working on It, and that's an afterthought for a multi - billion dollari Company. By the way, margins on hard back RPG books are VERY low, but that said, Renegade Is still actively and strongly supporting and distributing the line.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 01-19-2024, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T17:59:08-08:00","id":1528965,"title":"","content":"Because &quot;success&quot; isn't an objective thing. If you want to consider success &quot;as many copies in as many hands as possible,&quot; the evidence is considerably different than if you consider success, &quot;making a net profit,&quot; or, &quot;making the best VtM game possible.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T11:49:51-08:00","id":1529027,"title":"","content":"Success to in regards to entertainment for me is pretty simple. Did I greatly enjoy what I read, played or watched. If the answer is yes then I feel I got my money's worth out the products.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T12:41:23-08:00","id":1529031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528965#post1528965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;success&quot; isn't an objective thing. If you want to consider success &quot;as many copies in as many hands as possible,&quot; the evidence is considerably different than if you consider success, &quot;making a net profit,&quot; or, &quot;making the best VtM game possible.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's absolutely irrelevant to quality and I don't see what the point in speculating on it is either. Though I think most people think it's worked out well.<br /> <br /> This very much like, &quot;Star Wars is a huge loss for Disney!&quot;<br /> <br /> But there's very little evidence for that either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T16:17:46-08:00","id":1529047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528849#post1528849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 10 to 1 odds is that Lucita isn't really gone and she is still active in her city. There is some hints that Talley didn't take her down at all and something else is happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so too, I doubt that they'd kill VtM poster girl. Therefore my sensationalist criticism, towards her &quot;death&quot;.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T16:40:00-08:00","id":1529048,"title":"","content":"I think they've kind of written themselves into a corner with lucita since she's very much out of touch with what v5 presents of the game. She's on a path, she's sabbat, she's an absolute badass etc and she doesn't really fit how her clan is presented in 5th.<br /> <br /> They're probably not going to kill her off but I don't think we'll see much of her for the time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T16:45:25-08:00","id":1529049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529048#post1529048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they've kind of written themselves into a corner with lucita since she's very much out of touch with what v5 presents of the game. She's on a path, she's sabbat, she's an absolute badass etc and she doesn't really fit how her clan is presented in 5th.<br /> <br /> They're probably not going to kill her off but I don't think we'll see much of her for the time being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean as far as anyone knows, they HAVE killed her off.<br /> <br /> It's just fans are ignoring it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It is kind of hilarious that the attempts to make her a more &quot;stereotypical&quot; Sabbat as Signature Character for the Clan moved her away from what the Clan has become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T17:37:26-08:00","id":1529054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529031#post1529031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's absolutely irrelevant to quality and I don't see what the point in speculating on it is either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, things like this need <i>some</i> sort of quantitative analysis and sales figures are about the best (really, only) available. And given game companies are generally profit-driven, sales dictate whether products receive post-release support or supplements. Case in point, how V20 was originally going to be a one-and-done commemorative release with as much content packed into it as possible, and (as far as I know or have read) it wasn't anticipated to single-handedly revive the intellectual property.<br /> <br /> In the bigger picture, frankly Paradox and RGS would do well to take a lesson from WotC or Black Library's handling of Forgotten Realms' and Warhammer's metaplot: provide a stable world-state for playable content, publish city or sect content intended for play within the confines of that world-state, and leave metaplot advancement to separately-published fluff. Advancing metaplot by way of pre-published module is just dumb, and has never really worked in practice the way designers seem to intend.<br /> <br /> Case in point, Fall of London. I think it might have been more interesting and less divisive had it been a dual release: one being a canon novel that details the metaplot events, the other being a city book that represents the city before and after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T18:15:17-08:00","id":1529057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529054#post1529054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point, Fall of London. I think it might have been more interesting and less divisive had it been a dual release: one being a canon novel that details the metaplot events, the other being a city book that represents the city before and after.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually felt Fall of London was an attempt to actually give some detail to a major event in the setting that had originally just been thrown in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T19:15:25-08:00","id":1529060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529031#post1529031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's absolutely irrelevant...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And yet, you keep talking about it like it's relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This very much like, &quot;Star Wars is a huge loss for Disney!&quot;<br /> <br /> But there's very little evidence for that either. </div> </div> </div>There's the opposite. It's demonstrably true that Disney has made billions off of their Star Wars acquisition... again shareholder reports. We know how much the purchase cost, and we know how much the Lucasfilm subdivision makes. There's no guesswork to do, just actually looking at the paperwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T20:38:28-08:00","id":1529064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528965#post1528965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;success&quot; isn't an objective thing. If you want to consider success &quot;as many copies in as many hands as possible,&quot; the evidence is considerably different than if you consider success, &quot;making a net profit,&quot; or, &quot;making the best VtM game possible.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> I recently read Ben Riggs's &quot;Slaying the Dragon&quot;, about the slow death of TSR back in the 80s and 90s. (Good book, highly recommend).<br /> <br /> One thing the book makes clear is that many of its products sold a fair number of units (at least at first), as far as the creatives working at TSR knew. What they didn't know - what TSR management refused to tell them - is that many of those same products were not, and likely could never be, profitable. Many of these had to do with unnecessary expenses, like leather-bound prestige books, or including VHS tapes or CDs in the box sets. And then the products price not reflecting these added expenses. So even if they sold gangbusters, they would never make their money back at the price being asked (and selling for what the products were actually worth would have meant selling fewer units).<br /> <br /> To be fair, as the book shows, there were many problems with the way TSR was run, that contributed to its slow decline into insolvency. (Including quirks seemingly unique to TSR, like the &quot;loan&quot; style arrangement it had with Random House).<br /> <br /> Another pertinent angle to TSR's decline, irrespective of sales, was how it supporting many different campaign settings simultaneously ended up cannibalizing its own fanbase. They would put out a new setting, usually in one or more box sets, in the hopes the various kinds of D&amp;D worlds would attract new players. A &quot;bait &amp; hook&quot; strategy, as Riggs calls it. That this would turn more people into D&amp;D players. In reality, most people won't or can't juggle multiple campaigns, in different settings. If you invest lots of money into the Forgotten Realms, for example, you probably won't play in other settings. Either because you don't have the time for more than one campaign, or because even when you end one and start another, you're more likely to start a new one in the setting you know (and which has a bunch of other published material you haven't gotten a chance to explore).<br /> <br /> In effect, each new setting - almost a game unto itself - put new players into silos. It created Ravenloft or Forgotten Realms or Dark Sun or Birthright fans. Not D&amp;D fans. Meaning no matter how successful those were, they weren't translating into a larger D&amp;D fanbase, willing to buy lots of products. And because most product lines are never as profitable as their core product (none of the supplements for Ravenloft were as profitable as the Ravenloft boxed set, which in turn was less profitable than the AD&amp;D core books), each new line was an increasing expense for diminishing returns. (It's why WotC these days usually only puts out one book for a given setting, unless it proves really popular or it's Forgotten Realms).<br /> <br /> A product can move units, and still not be profitable (or not profitable <i>enough</i>). Given TSR's unique situation, it was never enough. (Indeed, the same incentive structures it worked under were also killing it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-24-2024, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T22:06:23-08:00","id":1529068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529057#post1529057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually felt Fall of London was an attempt to actually give some detail to a major event in the setting that had originally just been thrown in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is if writers, designers, and leads are insistent on a metaplot with distinct canon events which fundamentally shape the game world, those metaplot events make <i>extremely</i> poor content for a game module. It mandates railroading players, and -- at best -- only offering aesthetic differences in outcome relevant only to the player characters in question. In which case (and it's always the case), just commission a companion novel. That's been a consistent factor in published game modules throughout WoD's history, and it's still consistent today.<br /> <br /> Few players are interested in a game in which their characters get ushered from one set piece to another, and ultimately get to watch from the sidelines as every problem is fixed (or broken beyond repair) at the end by one metaplot character or another. Tabletop roleplay thrives on player agency, and that's at unreconcilable odds with metaplot event modules which must by definition arrive at a predetermined conclusion with a predetermined resolution.<br /> <br /> That's where Warhammer/40K and Forgotten Realms goes right. Rulebooks are toolkits with information on a default world-state, and just enough context to explain the why's and how's of it. They leave metaplot the purview of fiction external to rulebooks, and there if players want immersion deeper than that which is necessary to play the game, but ultimately optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T02:21:11-08:00","id":1529078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529049#post1529049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is kind of hilarious that the attempts to make her a more &quot;stereotypical&quot; Sabbat as Signature Character for the Clan moved her away from what the Clan has become.</div> </div> </div> </div>She didnt even really fit it before that v5 tries to wedge the lasombra back into the da magister box (with obvious issues) but a lot of her initial characterisation is pushback against it. Realistically with current lore they should have her go loyalist or moderate and pushing back against 5th ed jellybrain Sabbat. But that would require a u turn in how Sabbat are written as orcs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 01-21-2024, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T05:34:50-08:00","id":1529085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529078#post1529078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She didnt even really fit it before that v5 tries to wedge the lasombra back into the da magister box (with obvious issues) but a lot of her initial characterisation is pushback against it. Realistically with current lore they should have her go loyalist or moderate and pushing back against 5th ed jellybrain Sabbat. But that would require a u turn in how Sabbat are written as orcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Loyalist Sabbat are the jellybrain Sabbat. Remember the FREEDOM Sabbat were the most crazy murder hobo-like.<br /> <br /> I do think the Sword of Caine book made the Lasombra defection much-much more understandable.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, these guys are fucking nuts. I'm outta here.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T05:58:17-08:00","id":1529087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529068#post1529068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue is if writers, designers, and leads are insistent on a metaplot with distinct canon events which fundamentally shape the game world, those metaplot events make <i>extremely</i> poor content for a game module. It mandates railroading players, and -- at best -- only offering aesthetic differences in outcome relevant only to the player characters in question. In which case (and it's always the case), just commission a companion novel. That's been a consistent factor in published game modules throughout WoD's history, and it's still consistent today.<br /> <br /> Few players are interested in a game in which their characters get ushered from one set piece to another, and ultimately get to watch from the sidelines as every problem is fixed (or broken beyond repair) at the end by one metaplot character or another. Tabletop roleplay thrives on player agency, and that's at unreconcilable odds with metaplot event modules which must by definition arrive at a predetermined conclusion with a predetermined resolution.<br /> <br /> That's where Warhammer/40K and Forgotten Realms goes right. Rulebooks are toolkits with information on a default world-state, and just enough context to explain the why's and how's of it. They leave metaplot the purview of fiction external to rulebooks, and there if players want immersion deeper than that which is necessary to play the game, but ultimately optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perceptive, you've literally described the worst Storyteller possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Because the whole point of metaplot incorporation should be that players feel like they're actively a part of the world and able to influence the events happening around them. It' certainly not something that should be happening &quot;over there.&quot; It also sounds like a spectacularly shitty ST that wouldn't be able to make the players feel like theyr'e able to influence events even if certain things happen beyond their control.<br /> <br /> The Fall of London is also a weird example because the player characters can have probably more effect on how things play out than probably any other published module. You can result in the death of Mithras, the takeover of London by the Camarilla, the elimination of the SI, and many other possibilities. It's a much more TSR/WOTC-esque module in the end because the player characters can basically do what those epic level campaigns for 5th Edition allow. You can slay Tiamat, fail, side with her or whatnot in THE RISE OF TIAMAT module just like you can do here. THE CURSE OF STRAHD is one of the all time most popular modules of all time (and based on the all time most popular RAVENLOFT) and has less ability to influence the outcome than the Fall of London.<br /> <br /> For me, The Fall of London and THE SACRIFICE are the two top tier examples of allowing the player characters to have relevance to events and incorporating how metaplot should incorporate the players. There, the player characters play an intricate role in how the Lasombra become part of the Camarilla or can even throw a wrench in it for a couple of years and influence how their campaign will go from then on.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in how people think metaplot should be handled in modules by contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-21-2024, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T08:31:09-08:00","id":1529092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529087#post1529087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my perceptive, you've literally described the worst Storyteller possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Because the whole point of metaplot incorporation should be that players feel like they're actively a part of the world and able to influence the events happening around them...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the ST, it's how the books were written from the beginning. If a workable ST has to break published content down to bare bones and rebuild to give players a sense of agency, it's not workable content from the perspective of providing a good chronicle/adventure path. Good fluff maybe, but not good <i>game</i> content.<br /> <br /> At this point I've written literally dozens of threads about Transylvania Chronicles alone -- including when I ran it -- about the problems with it from a player agency standpoint, and how to make it a <i>chronicle</i> first and a World of Darkness theme park ride second, compared to how the module is published which puts the &quot;theme park ride&quot; aspect first. You've participated in a lot of those threads, so I know you're aware of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...It also sounds like a spectacularly shitty ST that wouldn't be able to make the players feel like theyr'e able to influence events even if certain things happen beyond their control.<br /> <br /> The Fall of London is also a weird example because the player characters can have probably more effect on how things play out than probably any other published module. You can result in the death of Mithras, the takeover of London by the Camarilla, the elimination of the SI, and many other possibilities... </div> </div> </div>And at the end, there has to be a &quot;canon&quot; resolution for metaplot to continue. Even if it's the rote standard White Wolf &quot;shit happened, nobody knows exactly what, those involved disappeared&quot; narrative punt which is the ultimate slap to the face of player agency as it essentially retcons out anything players might have done in the course of the chronicle.<br /> <br /> At least put something akin to an &quot;this is the canon ending, but proceeding otherwise pushes the chronicle into alternative continuity and it's on the storyteller to work out the narrative beats from then on&quot; disclaimer somewhere. Much as how Transylvania Chronicles' book four has multiple sidebars on how to proceed from the last three stories in alternate continuity, as well as how to segue into a modern nights methuselah chronicle, or move straight into either Lair of the Hidden or Gehenna. But at that point, why even bother with the published module in the first place if it's to move into alternate continuity anyways?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...It's a much more TSR/WOTC-esque module in the end because the player characters can basically do what those epic level campaigns for 5th Edition allow. You can slay Tiamat, fail, side with her or whatnot in THE RISE OF TIAMAT module just like you can do here. THE CURSE OF STRAHD is one of the all time most popular modules of all time (and based on the all time most popular RAVENLOFT) and has less ability to influence the outcome than the Fall of London... </div> </div> </div>This highlights the issue more than anything else.<br /> <br /> In the former, regardless what player characters do Tiamat regains her full portfolio, and even if the PC's fail to banish her to Avernus someone else does. The latter isn't even a metaplot event, and in fact is something of an <i>anti</i>-metaplot event.<br /> <br /> Characters from <i>any</i> setting can be drawn into Ravenloft, and their adventures in Ravenloft exist entirely separate from that setting. Strahd's titular curse is to exist in a quasi-time loop, repeating the same events over and again. The books go out of their way to highlight how the PC's romp is neither the first time it's happened nor will it be the last time; regardless what happens, Barovia will repopulate, Strahd will resurrect, and there is no way to actually break the cycle as Strahd simply cannot comprehend what he did to be confined in Ravenloft was wrong. If I've heard correctly, the latest re-release of the module even includes guidelines on how to run it a <i>second</i> time, under auspices the now high-level PC's <i>return</i> to put an early end to a subsequent cycle -- or were themselves corrupted and &quot;punished&quot; to try redeeming Strahd for all eternity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd be interested in how people think metaplot should be handled in modules by contrast. </div> </div> </div>Well, I already threw my two cents in on this: keep metaplot and game content separate. Publish game content with a baseline stable world-state, and publish companion fiction for metaplot events that move the story forward and/or bridge editions. I'm unopposed to modules <i>like</i> Fall of London, but they need to be designed and written from the under the context of &quot;this is what happens, these events are simply too big for one coterie to impact, but the story is in how PC's meet Final Death or by some miracle make it out the other side&quot; opposed to &quot;players get to flirt with affecting metaplot, but it's really just a facade of agency as things happen the way they're published to happen anyways.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T10:22:09-08:00","id":1529095,"title":"","content":"Just a point on sales. Renegade products have not been carried by Ingram, North America's largest, and pretty much only, nationwide distributor of books and sidelines to book stores, since January 2022. This means that stores would have to use another distributor or deal directly with Renegade to carry their products. Other RPGs are still carried by Ingram. Also, one must remember that the PDF of V20 is less expensive than V5 on DTRPG, and V20 is frequently on sale. V5 never seems to be included in these sales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T12:03:59-08:00","id":1529164,"title":"","content":"I just recently picked up the Players Guide and I found it worth the buy and gave us better ideas to improve our Kindred coterie and answering my questions on how they were going to handle the Ravnos &amp; Tzismce clans and their Discipline spreads. So I view it as a helpful addition to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:25:12-07:00","id":1536963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5#post1528497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me personally, I feel they should have done the same thing they did with WtA 5th editon and just remade the game. I understand not all the changes were liked, but I feel it could have been a more welcome change instead of VTM continuing the overall same routine from the older editions. Maybe they could have taken stuff from VTR or Sorcerer(which imo fits vampire a little better). Perhaps they could have added a concept like the covenants to the game, or even give vampires a light boost in regards to powers and the options for powers.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyway. What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they tried to, and did, make the game better with Requiem 2.0, but the folks who treat the metafiction as fact rebelled. So, they shoehorned the best stuff from Requiem onto Masquerade, and gave us the shitshow the lunatics demanded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:31:08-07:00","id":1536964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ragged robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528551#post1528551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but fall of london isnt very good.....</div> </div> </div> </div>blasphemy! Prepare for final death!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:32:37-07:00","id":1536965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528561#post1528561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, that's easy enough to solve: multiverse. [Ravnos], Malkav, or any of the mental/illusion dealers created this both as a pocket dimension or a very strong hallucination. They exist there, encapsulated, and we can again have Lasombras as an independent clan of the children of Cappadocius.</div> </div> </div> </div>But see, that would require initiative, and imagination, and not bowing down to established cannon and dogma! Can't have that! Malkav's sister is Malakai, and that's that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:37:47-07:00","id":1536966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528590#post1528590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but it wasn't terrible either and I like the idea that the only reason the Second Inquisition &quot;cleansed&quot; London was they were just pawns of Mithras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much 97.947474% of the fiction written for this franchise. Did it include a<br /> description of &quot;Tearing meat?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:41:42-07:00","id":1536968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528678#post1528678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I'll break down to you. Since V5 is hammering VtR mechanics (very poorly) it makes no sense to keep publishing new material, because, editorially, the games are fused in one, so, VtR is editorially redundant. If V5 keeps like that, there won't be new CofD, because they're now canonically oWoD. Now is clearer?</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR is clearly an attempt to fix the obvious mechanical and lore flaws of the original. But folks love their mythology, and now we're stuck with this shitshow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:59:18-07:00","id":1536969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528692#post1528692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the way I prefer to see metaplot in games. You get the broad outline &quot;this character dies. This event happens,&quot; and then the book provides information on the setting and the way the situation has built up to this point, but then leave it up to the ST and players to figure out how the events actually play out. The worst way is when the metaplot is on rails like To Grandmother's House We Go, which is (on many levels) among the worst metaplot adventures I've seen in an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. A lot of the VtM &quot;supplements&quot; from 30 years ago were literally &quot;Bystander Witness&quot; adventures. Like the awful &quot;Watch the Niktuku kill the most badass sorceress on the planet!&quot; adventure. Wasn't that fun?! Let's do it again in Chicago where you can't even touch Menele(us) or Helena! But Paris(rius) dies, so it's awesome, right?! RIGHT?! Let's do it again when the Ultimate Badass Mage/Werewolf/Ghoul gets turned into an ashtray in Stygia! FUCKING TUBULAR, DUDE! That'll let the poser anarchist Wolverine writers know we're not buying that hyper John Wayne Syndrome Bullshit! Ask again in 30 years how Haight changed society for the better!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 06-08-2024, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T03:30:25-07:00","id":1536972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1529085#post1529085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, the Loyalist Sabbat are the jellybrain Sabbat. Remember the FREEDOM Sabbat were the most crazy murder hobo-like.<br /> <br /> I do think the Sword of Caine book made the Lasombra defection much-much more understandable.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, these guys are fucking nuts. I'm outta here.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the were initially considered unplayable antagonists. And they should have stayed so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T10:05:18-07:00","id":1536988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1536972#post1536972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why the were initially considered unplayable antagonists. And they should have stayed so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This inspired a thread of mine. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536991-sabbat-as-nuanced-player-characters-vs-murder-hobo-npcs\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...rder-hobo-npcs</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-08-2024, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T12:04:44-07:00","id":1537424,"title":"","content":"Cannon and Mythology are quite important as it sets the groundwork for the universe your playing in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T12:28:21-07:00","id":1537569,"title":"","content":"I wonder if abandoning the trappings of a TTRPG entirely would've been the best course for a V:tM revival after V20. It's been a long, long time since the game's target demographic has been &quot;people who play TTRPGs&quot; and not &quot;fans of V:tM&quot;; if these fans are primarily interested in the game for its metaplot, reviving the V:tM label for novels/comics/video games/what-have-you set within the cWoD universe might've just turned out to be a safe investment. Expanding V5 beyond the TTRPG medium seems to be a priority for Paradox, anyway.<br /> <br /> Barring that, I think literally anything that extricates V:tM from V:tR would've been better for the label than what they ended up doing. I don't think reviving V:tM was worth the canning of V:tR, not least when the result is some strange mixture of the two; sometimes it might be better for the dead to stay that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T12:44:32-07:00","id":1537573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537569#post1537569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a long, long time since the game's target demographic has been &quot;people who play TTRPGs&quot; and not &quot;fans of V:tM&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While there were people who were traditional roleplaying gamers who gravitated to VtM when it was first released, the game was famous for attracting a large number of non-gamers. VtM was the first RPG for lots of people who were attracted to it simply because they liked Anne Rice novels, vampires in general, were interested in the Goth subculture or similar, or that it didn't seem to be about combat. Lots of people who never would have played D&amp;D and similar games became interested in VtM. I noticed lots of people involved in drama or theatre began playing. I think these people from non-gaming backgrounds were easily half the game base, if not more. It's a big reason why White Wolf grew so quickly in the nineties. They were tapping into a market that TSR and other gaming companies were not doing.<br /> <br /> Certainly TTRPGS were not the sole means of attracting an audience. They were really the first company that pushed Live Action as a medium, and that attracted lots of people to it. They pushed early into media with books and the TV show. And I know the Bloodlines videogame also attracted a fair number of people who did not play RPGs earlier. Not everything worked as expected, but they certainly had lots of success.<br /> <br /> I think a tabletop version of the game/setting is pretty much essential, but supporting other forms of the setting is a smart idea and not exclusive to a tabletop game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T13:01:16-07:00","id":1537577,"title":"","content":"I think metaplot in general ruins RPGs. But I would be fine with a compromise where the WoD picked ONE location which would be a &quot;living campaign&quot; setting that gets updated over time for those people who really, really, really like RPGs as a form of passive, serial entertainment, and want to see how different writers periodically update the local setting and its NPCs. (Since VtM has a very worldwide fanbase now, I'd also be OK with each major demographic getting its own city to play with - one for North America, one for Europe, and one for Latin America (maybe others too) where local game writers/creators could develop. Obviously there's a lot of talent interested in the game in each of those locations that could provide a lot of local flavor where people located elsewhere would miss.<br /> <br /> You could pick a city and design it in a way that you could justify characters from all sects, visitors from the more minor clans, bloodlines, and groups. That way all sorts of stories could be told. You could even try it as a &quot;shared world&quot; style anthology series like the old Thieves' World or Wild Cards where the editor kept continuity and consistency (or at least tried to) between the different authors.<br /> <br /> Just don't do that to the greater setting as a whole. A single vampire domain (or Garou protectorate, or whatever) can remain isolated. Some STs would ignore it entirely and create their own chronicle, ignoring canon. Others would incorporate it into their chronicle, but not base their games there (but might have the PCs visit that city at some point). Some might set their chronicles only there. Those who really want to follow characters in the VtM setting like its a comic book or serial fiction could have their kick, but it wouldn't alienate others.<br /> <br /> One could argue this is what Chicago By Night is becoming or could be, but I think it's the wrong city for it. CbN was not designed to be such a setting, and lots of players used that first established setting to do their own games, all of which went into their own direction. What would work best is a brand new city designated from the very beginning as a living campaign domain so that everyone buying the sourcebook knew what they were going to get, and thus not be disappointed when it got updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T13:23:07-07:00","id":1537581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537577#post1537577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could argue this is what Chicago By Night is becoming or could be, but I think it's the wrong city for it. CbN was not designed to be such a setting, and lots of players used that first established setting to do their own games, all of which went into their own direction. What would work best is a brand new city designated from the very beginning as a living campaign domain so that everyone buying the sourcebook knew what they were going to get, and thus not be disappointed when it got updated.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of gets into the Chronicles of Darkness vs. World of Darkness divide, ironically.<br /> <br /> Which is, &quot;It's not that the new material isn't good. It's the fact that the old material already has fans and none of them are guaranteed to move to the new stuff.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lorraine Williams created a dozen new settings for Dungeons and Dragons during her tenure as head of TSR in hopes of creating new fans of D&amp;D that would be attracted to them. Instead, everyone just started dividing themselves among the various settings and no longer buying material for D&amp;D as a whole but just their chosen settings. Which is why D&amp;D doesn't really do that anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T15:25:16-07:00","id":1537585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537573#post1537573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While there were people who were traditional roleplaying gamers who gravitated to VtM when it was first released, the game was famous for attracting a large number of non-gamers. VtM was the first RPG for lots of people who were attracted to it simply because they liked Anne Rice novels, vampires in general, were interested in the Goth subculture or similar, or that it didn't seem to be about combat. Lots of people who never would have played D&amp;D and similar games became interested in VtM. I noticed lots of people involved in drama or theatre began playing. I think these people from non-gaming backgrounds were easily half the game base, if not more. It's a big reason why White Wolf grew so quickly in the nineties. They were tapping into a market that TSR and other gaming companies were not doing.<br /> <br /> Certainly TTRPGS were not the sole means of attracting an audience. They were really the first company that pushed Live Action as a medium, and that attracted lots of people to it. They pushed early into media with books and the TV show. And I know the Bloodlines videogame also attracted a fair number of people who did not play RPGs earlier. Not everything worked as expected, but they certainly had lots of success.<br /> <br /> I think a tabletop version of the game/setting is pretty much essential, but supporting other forms of the setting is a smart idea and not exclusive to a tabletop game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is there's no reason not to do multiple ones. Dungeons and Dragons became the juggernaut it did because it leveraged novels, the tabletop RPG, movies, and video games all into a package that was everywhere.<br /> <br /> V:TM could be a brand.<br /> <br /> And was a brand.<br /> <br /> But sort of lost the thread somewhere along the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T20:24:26-07:00","id":1537596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537581#post1537581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sort of gets into the Chronicles of Darkness vs. World of Darkness divide, ironically.<br /> <br /> Which is, &quot;It's not that the new material isn't good. It's the fact that the old material already has fans and none of them are guaranteed to move to the new stuff.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lorraine Williams created a dozen new settings for Dungeons and Dragons during her tenure as head of TSR in hopes of creating new fans of D&amp;D that would be attracted to them. Instead, everyone just started dividing themselves among the various settings and no longer buying material for D&amp;D as a whole but just their chosen settings. Which is why D&amp;D doesn't really do that anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was an issue. It's one of the reasons why TSR started introducing more cross-pollinated settings, like Ravenloft and Spelljammer and then releasing events or including characters from other gamelines into the new settings, for example bringing Lord Soth and Vecna into Ravenloft in order to pull fans of different gamelines into Ravenloft and then hopefully use that as a springboard to get them into other gamelines as well. In practice it didn't work that well, but we got some really amazing things out of that period of D&amp;D (in fact, I'd say that was my favorite period of D&amp;D) so I'm still really glad that it happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T20:28:50-07:00","id":1537597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537585#post1537585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is there's no reason not to do multiple ones. Dungeons and Dragons became the juggernaut it did because it leveraged novels, the tabletop RPG, movies, and video games all into a package that was everywhere.<br /> <br /> V:TM could be a brand.<br /> <br /> And was a brand.<br /> <br /> But sort of lost the thread somewhere along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty clear that Paradox has dropped the ball bigtime when it comes to the World of Darkness. They had some big plans when they first bought the rights, like the idea of a One World of Darkness and it felt like they wanted to make the WoD into a pretty major IP but then just ended up bungling it again and again. It seems like they've dropped the whole One World of Darkness idea altogether. V5 came out 6 years ago, and I still don't really know what Paradox's plans for the WoD are these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T23:50:28-07:00","id":1537603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537585#post1537585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is there's no reason not to do multiple ones. Dungeons and Dragons became the juggernaut it did because it leveraged novels, the tabletop RPG, movies, and video games all into a package that was everywhere.<br /> <br /> V:TM could be a brand.<br /> <br /> And was a brand.<br /> <br /> But sort of lost the thread somewhere along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is important to recognise how this works, though. <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons </i>built a successful game and then branched out, and the reason is this: as a game it offered something pretty unique and, through this, attracted fans. It then branched out to solidify and extend the fanbase. The novels were pretty bad, though, and most of the computer games were mediocre. <br /> <br /> From a <i>Vampire</i> viewpoint, the error with V5 was not to build the game first <i>then </i>to move on to other media. There are a million vampire novels on the market, many of which are better than anything the World of Darkness has to offer. You shouldn\u2019t try to compete with them until you have built up your brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T13:44:15-07:00","id":1537632,"title":"","content":"Fair point James.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T06:18:24-07:00","id":1537699,"title":"","content":"I'd made it 70% the same.<br /> <br /> But remove the Beckoning (terrible idea to remove the conceptual 'The Man' to take down) and kept the elders and ancients more prominent in the game setting.<br /> As someone else said, the characters need something to 'punch up' instead of 'punch down'.<br /> <br /> Also I find a few renamings incredibly boring (The Ministry especially, I would just renamed them Setites and that's it).<br /> <br /> The Sabbat could be reduced to a faction that went somewhat in hiding or somewhat more cultish instead of a controlling big domains faction of the revised era.<br /> I don't have too much complaints about it<br /> But it shouldn't have been removed as a player option.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs I have no complaints they were pushed more on the forefront like in 1st edition, but they should have worked in making them more interesting. Subcultures, subfactions, player options. A la revised Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It's good that the Clans don't have precise sect separations.<br /> All clans in all sects is good<br /> <br /> Some stuff and changes I feel are improvements (the new Toreador weakness, the Tremere being split in different houses)<br /> <br /> I dislike the basically removal of the bloodlines, a few were fan favourites<br /> <br /> I don't dislike the push of the thin-bloods. It's one more player option<br /> <br /> The resonance of the blood still sounds like an uneccesary complication to me, but it can stay as an option<br /> <br /> So to sum it up, expand and not reduce.<br /> <br /> I could have been in favor of a corebook that reduces the options but without negating them and allowing their inclusion in supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T19:55:56-07:00","id":1537779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537699#post1537699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd made it 70% the same.<br /> <br /> But remove the Beckoning (terrible idea to remove the conceptual 'The Man' to take down) and kept the elders and ancients more prominent in the game setting.<br /> As someone else said, the characters need something to 'punch up' instead of 'punch down'.<br /> <br /> Also I find a few renamings incredibly boring (The Ministry especially, I would just renamed them Setites and that's it).<br /> <br /> The Sabbat could be reduced to a faction that went somewhat in hiding or somewhat more cultish instead of a controlling big domains faction of the revised era.<br /> I don't have too much complaints about it<br /> But it shouldn't have been removed as a player option.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs I have no complaints they were pushed more on the forefront like in 1st edition, but they should have worked in making them more interesting. Subcultures, subfactions, player options. A la revised Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> It's good that the Clans don't have precise sect separations.<br /> All clans in all sects is good<br /> <br /> Some stuff and changes I feel are improvements (the new Toreador weakness, the Tremere being split in different houses)<br /> <br /> I dislike the basically removal of the bloodlines, a few were fan favourites<br /> <br /> I don't dislike the push of the thin-bloods. It's one more player option<br /> <br /> The resonance of the blood still sounds like an unnecessary complication to me, but it can stay as an option<br /> <br /> So to sum it up, expand and not reduce.<br /> <br /> I could have been in favor of a corebook that reduces the options but without negating them and allowing their inclusion in supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a good argument that the game is just terribly extra.<br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat has lost Mexico City, Montreal, and many other territories thanks to its Civil War and the Second Inquisition. It exists but is just weakened as an organization.<br /> <br /> 2. The Lasombra have grown in the Camarilla, the Tzimisce have a faction that have joined the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> 3. The Anarchs have grown more powerful thanks to the Followers of Set organizing them and their prolific breeding.<br /> <br /> 4. Don't exile the Brujah<br /> <br /> 5. The Second Inquisition is a powerful dangerous group but not actually interested in destroying the Masquerade and more bark than bite unless it has Kindred support like London or Vienna (maybe have Vienna's sacking be the next Transylvania Chronicles)<br /> <br /> 6. Remove the Kuei Jin but imply that a bunch of Cainites exist as a separate sect.<br /> <br /> 7. Keep the Ashirra and Camarilla merger to make it a more global organization.<br /> <br /> There's plenty to do here that would have been a decent setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T21:35:54-07:00","id":1537782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537569#post1537569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if abandoning the trappings of a TTRPG entirely would've been the best course for a V:tM revival after V20. It's been a long, long time since the game's target demographic has been &quot;people who play TTRPGs&quot; and not &quot;fans of V:tM&quot;; if these fans are primarily interested in the game for its metaplot, reviving the V:tM label for novels/comics/video games/what-have-you set within the cWoD universe might've just turned out to be a safe investment. Expanding V5 beyond the TTRPG medium seems to be a priority for Paradox, anyway.<br /> <br /> Barring that, I think literally anything that extricates V:tM from V:tR would've been better for the label than what they ended up doing. I don't think reviving V:tM was worth the canning of V:tR, not least when the result is some strange mixture of the two; sometimes it might be better for the dead to stay that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not a novel idea and that was the plan from the get go. They were going to do Bloodlines 2, had talks about a possible movie/TV show and the rest will flow from that. <br /> <br /> But now is almost a decade later, Bloodlines 2 has been stuck for ages in a development hell, there's not a pip about the promised TV series (tho I don't think anyone sane would want people who slaughtered the Netflix &quot;The Witcher&quot; series to be handling their IPs). So what we have left is a couple of mediocre video games (Werewolf: Earthblood, Vampire: Swansong) and some Visual Novels (I heard Coteries are ok). Oh, and there was a Wraith VR game I think, I doubt many heard of that one. Not too impressive for 9 years of work. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T21:50:29-07:00","id":1537783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537603#post1537603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is important to recognise how this works, though. <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons </i>built a successful game and then branched out, and the reason is this: as a game it offered something pretty unique and, through this, attracted fans. It then branched out to solidify and extend the fanbase. The novels were pretty bad, though, and most of the computer games were mediocre.<br /> <br /> From a <i>Vampire</i> viewpoint, the error with V5 was not to build the game first <i>then </i>to move on to other media. There are a million vampire novels on the market, many of which are better than anything the World of Darkness has to offer. You shouldn\u2019t try to compete with them until you have built up your brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, YMMV but Baldur's Gate is a classic (it is also the reason CD Projekt exists), Icewind Dale was good, Planescape: Torment was great. Shadows over Mystara and Tower of Doom were pretty popular on the arcades. <br /> <br /> And no, TTRPGs are a relic of the past so building brands on them is a fool's errand. World of Darkness, especially Vampire, has enough of a nostalgia factor to build on that. So if there was a good movie, or TV show or video game based on the IP people would flock to that. Now however cinemas seem to be following in RPGs footsteps, that WoD TV show is not happening so I guess the last savior must be Bloodliness 2 but after being stuck in development hell for so long I would not be holding my breath for its success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T22:24:14-07:00","id":1537786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537783#post1537783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, YMMV but Baldur's Gate is a classic (it is also the reason CD Projekt exists), Icewind Dale was good, Planescape: Torment was great. Shadows over Mystara and Tower of Doom were pretty popular on the arcades.<br /> <br /> And no, TTRPGs are a relic of the past so building brands on them is a fool's errand. World of Darkness, especially Vampire, has enough of a nostalgia factor to build on that. So if there was a good movie, or TV show or video game based on the IP people would flock to that. Now however cinemas seem to be following in RPGs footsteps, that WoD TV show is not happening so I guess the last savior must be Bloodliness 2 but after being stuck in development hell for so long I would not be holding my breath for its success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dungeons and Dragons is actually selling more than it did at any point in its history and so much so that they make more money from it at Hasbro than any other board game.<br /> <br /> It's just....D&amp;D is the only game in town these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-22T02:32:18-07:00","id":1537793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537603#post1537603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is important to recognise how this works, though. <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons </i>built a successful game and then branched out, and the reason is this: as a game it offered something pretty unique and, through this, attracted fans. It then branched out to solidify and extend the fanbase. The novels were pretty bad, though, and most of the computer games were mediocre.<br /> <br /> From a <i>Vampire</i> viewpoint, the error with V5 was not to build the game first <i>then </i>to move on to other media. There are a million vampire novels on the market, many of which are better than anything the World of Darkness has to offer. You shouldn\u2019t try to compete with them until you have built up your brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably, there's been a good degree of success in building the game.<br /> <br /> WOD5E products were well received as kickstarters (both on the OPP side and on the boardgames side), and have reached between top 3 and top 5 on icv rankings consistently in the last years. They have good International distribution deals, the STV vault Is a success and they are also well placed on Drivethru despite internal competition from Wod20 and COFD and above all the fact that Renegade actively discourages buying from Drivethru.<br /> <br /> <br /> Problem Is, the success was built surely despite all the management problems of the IP, community management issues, and despite the evidente failure at branching out in the transmedia realm: while this can also be a point for optimism (had things been better managed, what could have been achieved?), surely there Is some limiti at how an IP can be successful against all odds.<br /> <br /> As Simeone who mostly likes what has been done with WOD5e, I Hope they can get the boat navigating smoothly in the next years.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-22T05:08:37-07:00","id":1537797,"title":"","content":"I think the big mistake of WOD5E has been to focus on redefining and narrowing down what the World of Darkness is. Rather than obsessing over making everything street-level only, personal horror etc., they should've taken an expansive perspective. 20th Anniversary, Chronicles of Darkness, introducing new lore like the Beckoning or just being a beginner-friendly blank slate and making the game more of a toolbox, boardgames, cardgames... It should've been embraced that there are many facets and aspects to the WOD-IP at this point. Besides even if one were to be concerned about divided attention between all these various lines of games under the WOD IP, it's not like if you cancel CofD, for example, then no Urban Fantasy personal horror game can appear on the market to compete with WOD. So in that sense, I think it would've gone further to corner that type of game on the market by having both WOD5E and CoD out there rather than just the former.<br /> <br /> After all, canceling the 20th-line and CofD hasn't led to V5 shooting up the charts. No fan of those lines was immediately like &quot;Oh well, I guess I <i>have </i>to play WOD5E now.&quot;. Of course, it doesn't work like that. And the success of the Storytellervault shows that as well. Instead, you have all this content shoved into that digital corner when you could've released official products which even now still have an audience who are interested, as the success of the STV indicates.<br /> <br /> The climate on the community-side also would've benefited a lot from this as well. Sure, there will be people who like one thing more than the other. But you wouldn't have to go to them and tell them stuff like &quot;If you like the old werewolf-editions, this new edition isn't for you.&quot;. By clinging to this narrowed-down and redefined version of WOD5E the pitch and tone of the conversation also became more exclusionary.<br /> <br /> Also, this narrowed-down version was hampered by inconsistency. You have a book like Chicago By Night on one hand with a lot of Loresheets and references to the past while the V5 Players Guide dismissively calls Loresheets &quot;vampire arcana&quot; that most people at the table probably don't even care about. And even now with another change in leadership, you get yet another slightly different take on this narrowed-down vision for WOD5E.<br /> <br /> At this point, I think the best thing to do would be for Paradox to just let Renegade manage the whole thing on their own. Because if there's one thing Paradox has shown over the last couple of years (both in terms of WOD5E and them as a videogame-publisher), it's that they have developed a real knack for pushing projects in the wrong direction somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T12:05:50-07:00","id":1537834,"title":"","content":"I do hope that they add more lore sheets in future products as a nod to the old school fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T14:11:10-07:00","id":1537902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537834#post1537834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that they add more lore sheets in future products as a nod to the old school fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are adding more again but it's still nowhere near what we got with Onyx Path supplements. At least it's better than the snark and disdain we got during the H5 and V5 Players Guide era. The H5 core had a whole sidebar explaining why the book didn't have Loresheets. And now it feels like Renegade is acting there's some sort of unwritten law that H5 can't have Loresheets. I think, similar to how the H5 core was needlessly restrictive with hunter-orgs, there's no need for the unimaginative approach of just not figuring out what Loresheets are in the context of H5.<br /> <br /> But that was par for the course for that era of WOD5E: It took elements from V5's game-design and erased them. That was the thrust of game-design in the last couple of years. That's another part where I think WOD5E just failed. It took V5 and instead of coming up with inventive new ways to adopt the system for mortal hunters and werewolves, the approach was more akin to thoughtless, wild swings with a sledgehammer. H5 is worse than W5 in that regard for sure but I never felt like the game-design direction for those two corebooks made a lot of sense in that regard. Instead of learning from how CofD worked in 2E, we're right back at the beginning where each splat is an island and it ranges from hard to nigh impossible to have crossovers between the systems described in these corebooks. And sure, I haven't met a lot of people who even want to do crossover with a WOD-game. But rather my thinking is that if you would want to make WOD more beginner-friendly, wouldn't it make sense to have a situation where it's super-easy for somebody who has played VtM in the past to easily shift to playing WtA? But thus far... take the dice... Hunger-dice, Desperation-dice, Rage-dice... It's such an obvious throughline, it's easy to imagine that an M5 might have something like Paradox-dice. And yet... They all work differently. Each splat so far handles these dice very differently. And that's a bit baffling because I think Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures could absolutely have been a template for WOD5E. Instead both H5 and W5 live in their own worlds. And sure, you can do that... but the whole point was to sacrifice the lore and complexity of past editions to make things more beginner-friendly. But as a franchise, WOD5E has only been pushing against that so far by making things more confusing and more complicated in how each splat works. You can't just take somebody who played V5 and have them play H5 or W5. Overreach/Despair and Brutal Outcomes are very distinct from Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures. It's the opposite of beginner-friendly.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you have the dice with symbols on them from Renegade... it sucks to be you. Some smartass during the development of W5 decided that Rage-dice needed to be different from Desperation-dice and Hunger-dice. Or didn't care or realize that there was a difference. Bad stuff triggers on a 1 for Hunger- and Desperation-dice but for Rage-dice it's 1 and 2, so the Rage-dice with symbols are different. Talk about beginner-friendly... You might think your Hunger-dice you bought for V5 would also work for W5 (after all they also worked for H5) - but then you find out that this isn't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T14:35:35-07:00","id":1537904,"title":"","content":"If I won the lottery and bought the WoD IP from Paradox, I'd outright do a hard retcon and declare the entire V5 era (and tbh, a major chunk of the late Revised era) to be non-canon and we'd reset things back to a mix of V20 and 1e/early 2e in terms of setting and themes.<br /> <br /> I'd still keep WoD 5E material on the Storyteller's Vault but it would be cordoned off and would be treated as an entirely separate continuity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T01:33:14-07:00","id":1537987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537902#post1537902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But rather my thinking is that if you would want to make WOD more beginner-friendly, wouldn't it make sense to have a situation where it's super-easy for somebody who has played VtM in the past to easily shift to playing WtA? But thus far... take the dice... Hunger-dice, Desperation-dice, Rage-dice... It's such an obvious throughline, it's easy to imagine that an M5 might have something like Paradox-dice. And yet... They all work differently. Each splat so far handles these dice very differently. And that's a bit baffling because I think Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures could absolutely have been a template for WOD5E. Instead both H5 and W5 live in their own worlds. And sure, you can do that... but the whole point was to sacrifice the lore and complexity of past editions to make things more beginner-friendly. But as a franchise, WOD5E has only been pushing against that so far by making things more confusing and more complicated in how each splat works. You can't just take somebody who played V5 and have them play H5 or W5. Overreach/Despair and Brutal Outcomes are very distinct from Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures. It's the opposite of beginner-friendly.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you have the dice with symbols on them from Renegade... it sucks to be you. Some smartass during the development of W5 decided that Rage-dice needed to be different from Desperation-dice and Hunger-dice. Or didn't care or realize that there was a difference. Bad stuff triggers on a 1 for Hunger- and Desperation-dice but for Rage-dice it's 1 and 2, so the Rage-dice with symbols are different. Talk about beginner-friendly... You might think your Hunger-dice you bought for V5 would also work for W5 (after all they also worked for H5) - but then you find out that this isn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more.<br /> <br /> I'm currently in the mood to make my regular group to have a few one shots to try the different original splats, Mage, Changeling, Wraith, etc.<br /> <br /> And I came to the realization that another reason for the bigger success of Vampire is that it's beginner-friendly even in concepts: vampires drink blood, they use it to fuel powers, if they get too hungry they risk frenzy.<br /> That's it, as far as simple explanations go.<br /> <br /> If you want to give a players group a try out at mage or changeling, just explaning how it works from their character perspective won't be that easy at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T01:50:15-07:00","id":1537988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537902#post1537902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are adding more again but it's still nowhere near what we got with Onyx Path supplements. At least it's better than the snark and disdain we got during the H5 and V5 Players Guide era. The H5 core had a whole sidebar explaining why the book didn't have Loresheets. And now it feels like Renegade is acting there's some sort of unwritten law that H5 can't have Loresheets. I think, similar to how the H5 core was needlessly restrictive with hunter-orgs, there's no need for the unimaginative approach of just not figuring out what Loresheets are in the context of H5.<br /> <br /> But that was par for the course for that era of WOD5E: It took elements from V5's game-design and erased them. That was the thrust of game-design in the last couple of years. That's another part where I think WOD5E just failed. It took V5 and instead of coming up with inventive new ways to adopt the system for mortal hunters and werewolves, the approach was more akin to thoughtless, wild swings with a sledgehammer. H5 is worse than W5 in that regard for sure but I never felt like the game-design direction for those two corebooks made a lot of sense in that regard. Instead of learning from how CofD worked in 2E, we're right back at the beginning where each splat is an island and it ranges from hard to nigh impossible to have crossovers between the systems described in these corebooks. And sure, I haven't met a lot of people who even want to do crossover with a WOD-game. But rather my thinking is that if you would want to make WOD more beginner-friendly, wouldn't it make sense to have a situation where it's super-easy for somebody who has played VtM in the past to easily shift to playing WtA? But thus far... take the dice... Hunger-dice, Desperation-dice, Rage-dice... It's such an obvious throughline, it's easy to imagine that an M5 might have something like Paradox-dice. And yet... They all work differently. Each splat so far handles these dice very differently. And that's a bit baffling because I think Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures could absolutely have been a template for WOD5E. Instead both H5 and W5 live in their own worlds. And sure, you can do that... but the whole point was to sacrifice the lore and complexity of past editions to make things more beginner-friendly. But as a franchise, WOD5E has only been pushing against that so far by making things more confusing and more complicated in how each splat works. You can't just take somebody who played V5 and have them play H5 or W5. Overreach/Despair and Brutal Outcomes are very distinct from Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures. It's the opposite of beginner-friendly.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you have the dice with symbols on them from Renegade... it sucks to be you. Some smartass during the development of W5 decided that Rage-dice needed to be different from Desperation-dice and Hunger-dice. Or didn't care or realize that there was a difference. Bad stuff triggers on a 1 for Hunger- and Desperation-dice but for Rage-dice it's 1 and 2, so the Rage-dice with symbols are different. Talk about beginner-friendly... You might think your Hunger-dice you bought for V5 would also work for W5 (after all they also worked for H5) - but then you find out that this isn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole development process has been a mess. When Paradox first announced they were purchasing White Wolf, they began pitching their idea for a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; creating a setting that would get shared across all of the splats. I figured we would end up with a system where you'd have the basic rules for the game, and then each gameline would add a new set on top (sort of like a template). But it's clear that idea died early on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T07:45:13-07:00","id":1537996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537988#post1537988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Paradox first announced they were purchasing White Wolf, they began pitching their idea for a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; creating a setting that would get shared across all of the splats. I figured we would end up with a system where you'd have the basic rules for the game, and then each gameline would add a new set on top (sort of like a template). But it's clear that idea died early on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> Just about a year or two later they were pondering the idea of following what Marvel currently has.<br /> Different versions of their IP in tabletop games, digital games, tv shows, comic books, novels. You don't have one Peter Parker Spider-Man, you have many different versions of it.<br /> It's not a bad idea.<br /> Different mediums tend to have different type of audiences. VtM Bloodlines is the WoD universe, but it isn't exactly the same 1:1 and that's good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T11:10:33-07:00","id":1538006,"title":"","content":"I really liked V5 but there's a few changes I would have made.<br /> <br /> Elder rules and get ride of blood potency. It works for requiem but doesn't fit thematically in masquerade.<br /> <br /> Keep onyx oath in charge of books. All the best v5 books come out of the onyx oath era.<br /> <br /> Keep up the lore sheet trend. I liked those and new books have less or none.<br /> <br /> Generally advantages as a concept need a rework. I dislike the merits and flaws model. <br /> <br /> Make the sabbat playable. Combine the ashirra into the camarilla. Expand the camarilla into Asia and give us a basis for a few more Asian cities. Keep the anarchs nominally in camarilla.<br /> <br /> Make touchstone rules more robust.<br /> <br /> More discipline powers.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-04T21:55:39-07:00","id":1538109,"title":"","content":"Camarilla and Anarch domians in Japan, Hong Kong and South Korea would be cool or South America. I do like the blood potency being tied to your generation as an interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T06:12:57-07:00","id":1538127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1538109#post1538109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camarilla and Anarch domians in Japan, Hong Kong and South Korea would be cool or South America. I do like the blood potency being tied to your generation as an interesting idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean....in Legacy Tokyo was a Camarilla city which shared domain with the Hungry Dead, Hong Kong was fully Camarilla up until it was handed back and is now contested territory with both Camarilla, Hungry Dead and Anarchs wheeling and Dealing. South Korea....from recollection had the Nagaraja, Lasombra and a smattering of independents working both for and against the Green Courts. South America has many, many Sabbat and Camarilla held cities with a smaller number of Anarch domains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T14:36:46-07:00","id":1538153,"title":"","content":"It would be nice if they offered revised editions for those settings, but it sounds like it's not on the drawing board at this time. But I wouldn't say no to a revised Children of the Night sourcebook with older and new signature clan characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T07:27:40-07:00","id":1562552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1528827#post1528827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point, part of me hopes Bloodlines 2 ends up as a financial failure. V5's continued support and success largely rides on Paradox propping it up at all costs so they can make sure Bloodlines 2 becomes a thing.<br /> <br /> If Bloodlines 2 flops, V5 will go down with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive the thread necromancy, but how does it feel to be a prophet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T09:46:39-07:00","id":1562565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562552#post1562552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive the thread necromancy, but how does it feel to be a prophet?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a monkey's paw curling because there is no saying if V6 is not going to be worse than V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","user":"sathriel","date":". 08-04-2026, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:38:39-07:00","id":1562660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5#post1528497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me personally, I feel they should have done the same thing they did with WtA 5th editon and just remade the game. I understand not all the changes were liked, but I feel it could have been a more welcome change instead of VTM continuing the overall same routine from the older editions. Maybe they could have taken stuff from VTR or Sorcerer(which imo fits vampire a little better). Perhaps they could have added a concept like the covenants to the game, or even give vampires a light boost in regards to powers and the options for powers.<br /> <br /> That's just what I think anyway. What about you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have bought it then. That's not a knee jerk reaction on my part or me trying to be dismissive, it's the fact that I returned to V5 because it had Chicago by Night updated. I wanted to see old friends like Kevin Jackson, Anita Wainwright, and Modius again.<br /> <br /> I was hoping until it became clear they were never coming back to see individuals like Lucita,Jan, and Theo Bell in their updated forms. <br /> <br /> Basically, it's like, &quot;I didn't buy Vampire: The Requiem because I'm here for the Old World of Darkness, its stories, and its NPCs. Why would I want another game that doesn't include these?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's why Beckett's Jyhad Diary is one of my all time favorite supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T13:35:01-07:00","id":1562683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1537783#post1537783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, YMMV but Baldur's Gate is a classic (it is also the reason CD Projekt exists), Icewind Dale was good, Planescape: Torment was great. Shadows over Mystara and Tower of Doom were pretty popular on the arcades.<br /> <br /> And no, TTRPGs are a relic of the past so building brands on them is a fool's errand. World of Darkness, especially Vampire, has enough of a nostalgia factor to build on that. So if there was a good movie, or TV show or video game based on the IP people would flock to that. Now however cinemas seem to be following in RPGs footsteps, that WoD TV show is not happening so I guess the last savior must be Bloodliness 2 but after being stuck in development hell for so long I would not be holding my breath for its success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they really? They seem to be selling more than they did in the 80s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T13:45:14-07:00","id":1562685,"title":"","content":"They are.<br /> <br /> Even obscure ones (relative to their obscurity)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T16:23:51-07:00","id":1562700,"title":"","content":"I don't want to argue about how D&amp;D sold a million copies only in the first year while selling another couple hundred thousands in consecutive years while 5E has 1.4 million lifetime sales, how to count digital sales. It's a complicated matter and the argument I will concede because my main point lies elsewhere. <br /> <br /> When I said that RPGS are a relict of bygone era I was talking about their relevance to the entertainment. D&amp;D has it as we can see from Hasbro trying to make it into a movie. WoD has it too due to nostalgia and fodness for original Bloodliness as messy as it was. Cyberpunk had it and it was reignited with the video game. It's unlikely that we are going to see Kult TV show or Shadowrun movie (anyone remember Mutant Chronicles movie? It exists).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T21:47:49-07:00","id":1562710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562700#post1562700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to argue about how D&amp;D sold a million copies only in the first year while selling another couple hundred thousands in consecutive years while 5E has 1.4 million lifetime sales, how to count digital sales. It's a complicated matter and the argument I will concede because my main point lies elsewhere.<br /> <br /> When I said that RPGS are a relict of bygone era I was talking about their relevance to the entertainment. D&amp;D has it as we can see from Hasbro trying to make it into a movie. WoD has it too due to nostalgia and fodness for original Bloodliness as messy as it was. Cyberpunk had it and it was reignited with the video game. It's unlikely that we are going to see Kult TV show or Shadowrun movie (anyone remember Mutant Chronicles movie? It exists).</div> </div> </div> </div>I made the statement Paradox bought World of Darkness to make video games of it and the RPG as well as books were a side benefit they had little interest in save as promotion.<br /> <br /> Sadly, Bloodlines 2 was a bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T22:11:02-07:00","id":1562713,"title":"","content":"But they have never been that relevant to entertainment, they were an extremely niche thing that only nerdy weirdos liked.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D, VtM and many others got to be influential in entertainment because many popular artists of all kinds were nerdy weirdos in the past and played them, but they only got to be relatively known to the general public in the last, what, 10 years at most? Before that this influence was considerably oblique.<br /> <br /> Most people who watched the Dungeons and Dragons cartoon never figured out it was about a pen and paper game, and that was the most direct reference for a very long time. The last time TTRPGs got media attention was to accuse us of being Satan worshippers.<br /> <br /> Only from the end of the 2000s, early 2010s we got celebrities admitting publicly that they played TTRPGs and things started to change.<br /> <br /> How popular are live play games in YouTube now? How many went to watch the last D&amp;D movie because it was a D&amp;D movie? Stranger Things was all over the place with references. Before? We had a minute or so in the early scenes of E.T.<br /> <br /> So we're now having the highest moment of visibility and media influence ever, and also the most book sells, not just for big names but for the whole market.<br /> <br /> What we may not have is big, memorable titles <i>in the opinion of old players</i> like we had before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T02:08:31-07:00","id":1562722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562713#post1562713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they have never been that relevant to entertainment, they were an extremely niche thing that only nerdy weirdos liked.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D, VtM and many others got to be influential in entertainment because many popular artists of all kinds were nerdy weirdos in the past and played them, but they only got to be relatively known to the general public in the last, what, 10 years at most? Before that this influence was considerably oblique.<br /> <br /> Most people who watched the Dungeons and Dragons cartoon never figured out it was about a pen and paper game, and that was the most direct reference for a very long time. The last time TTRPGs got media attention was to accuse us of being Satan worshippers.<br /> <br /> Only from the end of the 2000s, early 2010s we got celebrities admitting publicly that they played TTRPGs and things started to change.<br /> <br /> How popular are live play games in YouTube now? How many went to watch the last D&amp;D movie because it was a D&amp;D movie? Stranger Things was all over the place with references. Before? We had a minute or so in the early scenes of E.T.<br /> <br /> So we're now having the highest moment of visibility and media influence ever, and also the most book sells, not just for big names but for the whole market.<br /> <br /> What we may not have is big, memorable titles <i>in the opinion of old players</i> like we had before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree. D&amp;D was &quot;very well&quot; known to the public as it was one of the main black sheeps of the satanic panic era. Anyone remembers Tom Hanks' &quot;Mazes and Monsters&quot;? And then we have Dungeons and Dragons cartoon, D&amp;D laying the groundwork for crpgs with stuff like Pool of Radiance from SSI or Eye of the Beholder from Westwood Studios. And then we have classic Bioware with Baldur's Gate, Icewind Dale and Planescape: Torment. Baldur's Gate sold 2 milion copies on release when video games where much less mainstream than nowadays. And then we have 2 movies in the 90s<br /> <br /> And yes, I got you, Stranger Things references D&amp;D and uses D&amp;D terminology but it's as D&amp;D as Blade is VtM if not less. <br /> <br /> But I grant you that, I am not as plugged in the zitgeist as I used to be back in my young days so I may be blind to the going ons. Baldur's Gate III was massive and it revived the interest in crpgs, also D&amp;D crpgs, Owlcat is going to make BG4 and tho I don't have any interest in watching actual plays I am aware that stuff like LA by Night and Critical Role is massively popular on the youtubez.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T08:35:13-07:00","id":1562732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562722#post1562722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strongly disagree. D&amp;D was &quot;very well&quot; known to the public as it was one of the main black sheeps of the satanic panic era. Anyone remembers Tom Hanks' &quot;Mazes and Monsters&quot;? And then we have Dungeons and Dragons cartoon, D&amp;D laying the groundwork for crpgs with stuff like Pool of Radiance from SSI or Eye of the Beholder from Westwood Studios. And then we have classic Bioware with Baldur's Gate, Icewind Dale and Planescape: Torment. Baldur's Gate sold 2 milion copies on release when video games where much less mainstream than nowadays. And then we have 2 movies in the 90s<br /> <br /> And yes, I got you, Stranger Things references D&amp;D and uses D&amp;D terminology but it's as D&amp;D as Blade is VtM if not less.<br /> <br /> But I grant you that, I am not as plugged in the zitgeist as I used to be back in my young days so I may be blind to the going ons. Baldur's Gate III was massive and it revived the interest in crpgs, also D&amp;D crpgs, Owlcat is going to make BG4 and tho I don't have any interest in watching actual plays I am aware that stuff like LA by Night and Critical Role is massively popular on the youtubez.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the thing, D&amp;D was known in the Satanic Panic, but not as a media franchise.<br /> <br /> CRPGs are an almost distinct phenomena, it used to be common for many players of them to not know they're based on pen and paper. D&amp;D was far more of a reference to being nerd than recognized as entertainment. Up to 2005 being nerd wasn't cool in any way (now at least nerds are seen as liking some cool stuff, despite still being weird losers, but saying that out loud is bad now, and you make exceptions for rich nerds).<br /> <br /> And CRPGs were nonetheless niche within a niche market. Video Games became a big thing also late 2000s, early 2010s, CRPGs took more years and still aren't staples of the industry, the games you're citing are classics, but they represent 50 years of developments, in a time when games were made by nerds, for nerds, and they're classics, but not commercial powerhouses.<br /> <br /> JRPGs grew bigger and they're based on the hobby, too, just not a US style imitation. Final Fantasy was, for most of its development, a D&amp;D game, only later it changed before release. But still, niche market even when they were seriously ahead of CRPGs.<br /> <br /> About Stranger Things, it's seriously more D&amp;D than Blade os VtM, because Blade isn't VtM. Stranger Things isn't about D&amp;D, but the characters are D&amp;D players using D&amp;D names and references. Blade is from 1973 and makes generic vampire referenced in the Marvel Universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T02:30:28-07:00","id":1562867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5#post1528497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me personally, I feel they should have done the same thing they did with WtA 5th editon and just remade the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I'm loath to say it, openly admitting the 5th edition was a reboot would have been far more preferable to them making it a reboot, but pretending it wasn't.<br /> <br /> Seriously, there are so many changes introduced in V5, that the game is practically unrecognizable now. <br /> <br /> Starting things over from scratch would have been the better route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T09:37:59-07:00","id":1562874,"title":"","content":"That's a subjective opinion DarkKing and not really an objective one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T13:16:40-07:00","id":1562877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562874#post1562874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a subjective opinion DarkKing and not really an objective one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely hard disagree, but I'll respect your right to have your own opinion on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T17:03:47-07:00","id":1562885,"title":"","content":"Honestly there are so many things that could've been done to create a better 5th edition line, but they all ultimately stem largely from one main source. The utter mismanagement by the IP owners. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T21:11:19-07:00","id":1562890,"title":"","content":"Mismanagement is such a broad term its kinda meaningless. It's kinda like saying, &quot;Well, the biggest reason we didn't win the sports game is they scored more than we did.&quot;<br /> <br /> IMO the core issue is that Paradox didn't understand (and I'm not sure they have figured it out yet) what the IP needed to expand past what Onyx Path was doing so things could grow beyond a TTRPG popular enough to keep a small-but-medium-by-TTRPG-standards company going.<br /> <br /> Even something like, &quot;make a new edition that's easier to translate into video games,&quot; is more nuanced than it can seem and Paradox clearly didn't seem to understand that. For example, what kind of video game you're making is going to change what mechanical directions you'd want the TTRPG rules to move towards drastically, or if your video game strategy is to have a lot of different types of video games use the same IP, you might not care that much about the TTRPG mechanics vs. keeping a consistent mood and theme so the franchise feels consistent in that sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T00:09:49-07:00","id":1562893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562890#post1562890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mismanagement is such a broad term its kinda meaningless. It's kinda like saying, &quot;Well, the biggest reason we didn't win the sports game is they scored more than we did.&quot;<br /> <br /> IMO the core issue is that Paradox didn't understand (and I'm not sure they have figured it out yet) what the IP needed to expand past what Onyx Path was doing so things could grow beyond a TTRPG popular enough to keep a small-but-medium-by-TTRPG-standards company going.<br /> <br /> Even something like, &quot;make a new edition that's easier to translate into video games,&quot; is more nuanced than it can seem and Paradox clearly didn't seem to understand that. For example, what kind of video game you're making is going to change what mechanical directions you'd want the TTRPG rules to move towards drastically, or if your video game strategy is to have a lot of different types of video games use the same IP, you might not care that much about the TTRPG mechanics vs. keeping a consistent mood and theme so the franchise feels consistent in that sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said mismanagement because it sums it up all in one go. Otherwise my post would be a novel's length if I went into detail. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T13:12:17-07:00","id":1562906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562867#post1562867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I'm loath to say it, openly admitting the 5th edition was a reboot would have been far more preferable to them making it a reboot, but pretending it wasn't.<br /> <br /> Seriously, there are so many changes introduced in V5, that the game is practically unrecognizable now.<br /> <br /> Starting things over from scratch would have been the better route.</div> </div> </div> </div>O disagree because I think that was not the real problem.<br /> <br /> The problem with the changes made wasn't that they were many, it's that they were erratic, incomplete and incoherent. They threw a lot of new ideas, but didn't commit to any.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition, Hecata, Tremere Bombing, Beckoning... Everything happened but made no difference. They were shallow rather than open, instead of giving options to explore they kind of said it didn't matter.<br /> <br /> A number of changes are just there. Mexico City and Montreal switching from Sabbat to Camarilla isn't a bad thing in itself, regardless of how polemic it would be regardless. But the way it was done? One day the SI came, killed everyone, then left and the Cam took as if there was no risk in a city that just got wiped out of vampires, and somehow it really is, and in 5 years it's as if they had been there for at least 50? What the fuck?<br /> <br /> Problems like those come from lack of vision for the larger product and that would bite then no matter what they tried.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562890#post1562890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mismanagement is such a broad term its kinda meaningless. It's kinda like saying, &quot;Well, the biggest reason we didn't win the sports game is they scored more than we did.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall agree, but I think in this case it applies because of the decision hierarchy level where the problems were worse, which we can see by patterns followed consistently.<br /> <br /> Paradox spent 10 years trying to grow outside of Grand Strategy games, but they committed a fundamental error over and over: assuming they had all the know-how they needed, when they didn't actually understood their own success at the corporate level.<br /> <br /> Every project, every move, every PR statement and analysis carried the indelible mark of the upper management assuming that success in one thing means competence by default, and that this is replicable across the board.<br /> <br /> There was one thing, one that any company in a similar position would have done if correctly managed: hire business experts in a new field. That's what give us a chance, not a certainty but a chance, that V6 will turn out better.<br /> <br /> And I say that mismanagement fits because it's a cascading effect. Lack of know-how was the source, but the manifestation of the problem was a series of bad decisions all over the place, and as generic as it is, mismanagement ends up being the best way to describe the common factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T14:31:28-07:00","id":1562907,"title":"","content":"The TTRPG space is a very hard place to hire specifically &quot;business&quot; experts. WotC is basically the only organization in the industry where business expertise can really be separately from some level of creative expertise. The vast majority of successful people in the TTRPG business world are creatives that learned business as they went. I would number Ken Hite (someone Paradox did hire for V5's creation) and Jason Carl into that category. Jess Lanzillo started in setting and world building before she moved up the WotC ranks.<br /> <br /> Saying Paradox didn't hire experts feels a little off when, well, they did, and then they did again, and then again. If the problem was not bringing in experts for their projects, then it doesn't seem like they failed to do so even if they made hires that didn't fix the problems just because of having expertise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T15:17:17-07:00","id":1562908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562906#post1562906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> O disagree because I think that was not the real problem.<br /> <br /> The problem with the changes made wasn't that they were many, it's that they were erratic, incomplete and incoherent. They threw a lot of new ideas, but didn't commit to any.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition, Hecata, Tremere Bombing, Beckoning... Everything happened but made no difference. They were shallow rather than open, instead of giving options to explore they kind of said it didn't matter.<br /> <br /> A number of changes are just there. Mexico City and Montreal switching from Sabbat to Camarilla isn't a bad thing in itself, regardless of how polemic it would be regardless. But the way it was done? One day the SI came, killed everyone, then left and the Cam took as if there was no risk in a city that just got wiped out of vampires, and somehow it really is, and in 5 years it's as if they had been there for at least 50? What the fuck?<br /> <br /> Problems like those come from lack of vision for the larger product and that would bite then no matter what they tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, White Wolf seems to have a recurring problem with this kind of thing. V5 was far from being the first book in their franchise where the creative team lacked communication with each other and just slapped together their own ideas.<br /> <br /> I'm nervous about V6 stating that V5's lore will still be relevant to the setting. But at least the mechanical system looks better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T20:20:30-07:00","id":1562917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562907#post1562907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying Paradox didn't hire experts feels a little off when, well, they did, and then they did again, and then again. If the problem was not bringing in experts for their projects, then it doesn't seem like they failed to do so even if they made hires that didn't fix the problems just because of having expertise.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression was that they hired creatives more than business experts. A business needs to do market analysis, marketing strategy, estimate ROI, define logistics.<br /> <br /> A big part of Onyx Path success was figuring out production lines and cost assessment. It's not glamorous, but as incredible as their art is, it would have sunk without that. And that's the areas Paradox seemed, for all I could see, to sit in their own laurels when they should look for a grounded view on how things worked and how to adapt strategies and temper expectations.<br /> <br /> You can hire a creative first with experience in the back office part, but that's not what I saw, although I may have missed something. I saw them hiring creatives with experience in the hands on part, maybe public reach, but that's about that. The obvious, sure, but not where their weaknesses were.<br /> <br /> This isn't about TTRPGs, either, but everything they tried for those years outside their niche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562908#post1562908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand, White Wolf seems to have a recurring problem with this kind of thing. V5 was far from being the first book in their franchise where the creative team lacked communication with each other and just slapped together their own ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Or rather, not to this level.<br /> <br /> The main problem here is the non commitment to decisions, sometimes <i>in the same book</i>. The core of V5 has both an almost invincible SI and a Camarilla that's already running business as usual except when not.<br /> <br /> 2nd Ed had a lot of stuff thrown almost at random, but within each book the matter was taken to its consequence and frequently enough later books would assume previous ones unless retcon was the point.<br /> <br /> Revised had a far tighter grasp on the goal within each line, even if treating the lines as more independent than before. Take a game line and the timeline through the books is mostly coherent, give or take a few hiccups.<br /> <br /> V5 tried to do everything without compromise. The things are there, but not the consequences or developments. In the very books were they happen they're usually stripped of much further effects. Big changes all over the place yet the society of the Kindred is mostly the same.<br /> <br /> It's less the lack of a single theme linking every book and more the lack of wanting the events to actually change something. That's what makes the impression you have: things change as time goes on, but you don't see the setting react as you would expect, so it doesn't feel the same setting.<br /> <br /> What would happen in Legacy if the Beckoning started? What would happen if Vienna got hit by missiles? What would happen if suddenly all tech hid surveillance for a new Inquisition? Or what would happen if all those high ranking government officials all over the world had this knowledge about vampires?<br /> <br /> All of those could happen in Legacy, but the result wouldn't be V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T22:36:48-07:00","id":1562919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562917#post1562917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression was that they hired creatives more than business experts. A business needs to do market analysis, marketing strategy, estimate ROI, define logistics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jason Carl had lots of experience on that end before coming into Paradox, and that's why Paradox had Tobias Sjogren running the original White Wolf subsidiary over Martin (as he was a video game business expert)<br /> <br /> I don't really see a point in belaboring this, but it's not that Paradox didn't feel a need to hire people or move people internally to help manage new IPs. They brought in new management level folks when they went on their acquisition spree too; not just for the TTRPG stuff.<br /> <br /> The problem is the same problem that's hit most of the video game companies that went wild after an already booming period had the pandemic bump leaving them all flush with cash: they over extended. Microsoft and Sony - who are more flush with business experts than Paradox has employees - are struggling from completely misreading how the 2020s were going to be business-wise, combined with shareholders that want the magic money line to go up and don't care if it was only going up for years because of a unique and unsustainable set of circumstances.<br /> <br /> When I said the mismanagement was too broad of a brush, I'm not saying the problems weren't at the top, but that there's much more specific things to look at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A big part of Onyx Path success was figuring out production lines and cost assessment. </div> </div> </div>Considering what Rich has said publicly about this, a bigger part was relearning and readjusting things that were assumed to be able to work how they did back in the days when White Wolf was independent. What seems to be the most dangerous point for Onyx Path was when a lot of the &quot;old guard&quot; that were around from the CCP acquisition started to move on, and there was a serious gap in how on-boarding their replacements happened leading to some internal restructuring around what's centralized and what's left to the individual line developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T23:37:31-07:00","id":1562925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562917#post1562917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would happen in Legacy if the Beckoning started? What would happen if Vienna got hit by missiles? What would happen if suddenly all tech hid surveillance for a new Inquisition? Or what would happen if all those high ranking government officials all over the world had this knowledge about vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>My sentiments exactly. The Second Inquisition wasn't built to last, because the way they went about handling things was simply not sustainable.<br /> <br /> There's only so many times you can use the <i>&quot;counter terrorist operation&quot;</i> excuse on domestic soil, before the locals start to wonder where the fuck all these terrorists came from, and who we are going to war with.<br /> <br /> As for the government officials... what would a bunch of ultra rich, ultra powerful individuals want with a species who's bodily fluids provide the means to eternal youth? Hmmmm, I wonder?<br /> <br /> <br /> Second Inquisition surveillance tech would have been discovered in a heartbeat. We've got hacktivist groups in real life who keep a sharp lookout for any corporations who try to slip that shit into their products, and warns the public about it. If they found out the government or even the catholic church were involved, they would blast it on every media platform they could find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T00:00:32-07:00","id":1562928,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562917#post1562917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression was that they hired creatives more than business experts. A business needs to do market analysis, marketing strategy, estimate ROI, define logistics..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and 6e is going for the opposite extreme since from what little I saw of alpha it has a very design by committee feel to it. especially since it haphazardly takes part from TTRPG and grafts it on to it's self like a weird chimera system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T03:08:44-07:00","id":1562933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562919#post1562919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is the same problem that's hit most of the video game companies that went wild after an already booming period had the pandemic bump leaving them all flush with cash: they over extended. Microsoft and Sony - who are more flush with business experts than Paradox has employees - are struggling from completely misreading how the 2020s were going to be business-wise, combined with shareholders that want the magic money line to go up and don't care if it was only going up for years because of a unique and unsustainable set of circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected, indeed. This is a better reading than my own. It does seem right now that they're going more carefully this time, and I'm partially surprised with V6, anyway, and the decision to apparently chose WoD to be the thing they'll commit to for the time being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562925#post1562925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My sentiments exactly. The Second Inquisition wasn't built to last, because the way they went about handling things was simply not sustainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point.<br /> <br /> If you look at the changes, few things in V5 go against old lore, even if a lot feel contrived. But take any of those, or even all of them, and they could conceivably have occurred. So to say V5 changed things too much? Lore wise, I wouldn't say so.<br /> <br /> But what they did was poorly written and didn't follow through. They wanted to go big and still have the same status quo. That's why we can't easily like their plots in the way they did them, and why it feels like a different game despite really not being all that different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562928#post1562928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah and 6e is going for the opposite extreme since from what little I saw of alpha it has a very design by committee feel to it. especially since it haphazardly takes part from TTRPG and grafts it on to it's self like a weird chimera system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's neither the opposite nor surprising. It's what you should expect of an early draft.<br /> <br /> How hard is it to understand the concept of a Playtest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:13:07-07:00","id":1562940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562933#post1562933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the point.<br /> <br /> If you look at the changes, few things in V5 go against old lore, even if a lot feel contrived. But take any of those, or even all of them, and they could conceivably have occurred. So to say V5 changed things too much? Lore wise, I wouldn't say so.<br /> <br /> But what they did was poorly written and didn't follow through. They wanted to go big and still have the same status quo. That's why we can't easily like their plots in the way they did them, and why it feels like a different game despite really not being all that different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can not, and will not accept the idea that the Society of Leopold were failing to get the job done, because they lacked government support.<br /> <br /> They were supported by the Catholic church. You know, one of the biggest religious institutions on the planet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:37:37-07:00","id":1562943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562940#post1562940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were supported by the Catholic church. You know, one of the biggest religious institutions on the planet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> As any great institution, the Catholic Church is a multitude of systems and factions. Not every member knows of the Society, not everyone who knows approves of it. They face resistance from within the church for several reasons, not the least of it being that they're usually zealots with little to no tolerance to other faiths, something the Church long learned to not be a defensible position for it in the modern world.<br /> <br /> The very idea that monsters exist against the laws of YHWH is against church doctrine, so depending on how the ST chooses to run then church, the SoL can be seen as dangerously close to heresy, with enemies just waiting for an opportunity to excommunicate them.<br /> <br /> It's especially fitting if you remember the Church also has supernatural beings among both the faithful and the clergy, ranging from Lasombra that are literal cardinals to an order of nuns that's also a Camp of the Black Furies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:48:34-07:00","id":1562944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562943#post1562943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very idea that monsters exist against the laws of YHWH is against church doctrine, so depending on how the ST chooses to run then church, the SoL can be seen as dangerously close to heresy, with enemies just waiting for an opportunity to excommunicate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooo, what do they think the Society of Leopold is actually doing, if they don't believe in monsters?<br /> <br /> What was that whole period of witch burning about, if people weren't practicing magic?<br /> <br /> How can you blame the devil for tempting you towards evil, unless demons walk among you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T08:51:59-07:00","id":1562958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562944#post1562944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo, what do they think the Society of Leopold is actually doing, if they don't believe in monsters?<br /> <br /> What was that whole period of witch burning about, if people weren't practicing magic?<br /> <br /> How can you blame the devil for tempting you towards evil, unless demons walk among you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not saying they don't believe in monsters. They don't believe monsters can defy Divine Law.<br /> <br /> The original Inquisition was about orthodoxy and fighting heresy. The Vatican never formally condemned anyone for witchcraft.<br /> <br /> A lot of the violence of the Inquisitions was not formally by the Church. Most witch burnings were either by the local population or secular authorities. Priests regularly endorsed or even blessed the mob, but without formalization.<br /> <br /> Official doctrine held that the Devil couldn't do anything besides presenting temptation. Magic granting was either by YHWH or mere delusion. The actual targets were people saying Jesus was not part of a Trinitarian entity and other theological schisms.<br /> <br /> By the way the Church didn't even had authority over non Christians. Most of the time it relied on kings exiling Jews and Pagans, forcing them to convert to stay in their homes, which then would give the Church authority to watch over proper observance.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, and the thing you shouldn't ignore: it was not a monolith. There were those in the Church that believed all sorts of things. Most of the time, Church positions on things were the result of internal politics and debates. Sentiments changed back and forth, definitions were proposed, accepted, rejected, revised. You'd rarely if ever have any unanimity outside a few basic assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T10:48:20-07:00","id":1562969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562958#post1562958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not saying they don't believe in monsters. They don't believe monsters can defy Divine Law.</div> </div> </div> </div>*laughs in Lilith / Nephandi / Demonic / Fae*<br /> <br /> At least they tried. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T12:49:50-07:00","id":1562972,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, VtM doesn't assume a platonic benevolent YHWH. So it's perfectly in line with lore that all of those could have been commanded or manipulated by the Creator, if there is one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while the WoD never explored this for long, going by the discussions within the Church in the Middle Ages we could have all sorts of orders inside it with varying relations to the various supernatural splats. Moncada and other Lasombra priests could be actually formal members, there could be orders seeking to elevate some splats to recognized miracles, even a redeemed demon would be acceptable for some.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say they'd all exist openly or safely within the Church, but they would dispute papal attention and try to maneuver their beliefs into recognition and their enemies into being branded hereticals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T13:38:40-07:00","id":1563038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562958#post1562958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original Inquisition was about orthodoxy and fighting heresy. The Vatican never formally condemned anyone for witchcraft.<br /> <br /> A lot of the violence of the Inquisitions was not formally by the Church. Most witch burnings were either by the local population or secular authorities. Priests regularly endorsed or even blessed the mob, but without formalization.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> By the way the Church didn't even had authority over non Christians. Most of the time it relied on kings exiling Jews and Pagans, forcing them to convert to stay in their homes, which then would give the Church authority to watch over proper observance.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, and the thing you shouldn't ignore: it was not a monolith. There were those in the Church that believed all sorts of things. Most of the time, Church positions on things were the result of internal politics and debates. Sentiments changed back and forth, definitions were proposed, accepted, rejected, revised. You'd rarely if ever have any unanimity outside a few basic assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are really good distinctions I often see blurred. The Church as an organization did not do these things nor did it will them done (in as much as an organization can will, which in this case is quite a bit). The members of the Church were nowhere near as consistent. The Malleus Maleficarum is a good example as it was written by a clergyman and promoted torture of witches. It was also condemned by the Inquisition both because it promoted torture and because it was doctrinally wrong. <br /> <br /> The one thing I would disagree with though is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Official doctrine held that the Devil couldn't do anything besides presenting temptation. Magic granting was either by YHWH or mere delusion. </div> </div> </div>Eh... sort of but not really. That's not a doctrine I can find. I did a quick search of the Catechism and it's not there that I can see. Nor would I expect it to be, since we have the accounts of saints like St Padre Pio who reported being physically beaten by demons. The Book of Job and the demoniacs in the Gospels are also indications that demons are quite capable of more than temptation if they are allowed to be. That's the real distinction. The devil and his ilk can only do what God lets him. For most people this does appear to be limited to temptation and adjacent things, but not for all people, situations, or times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-12T14:27:14-07:00","id":1563043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563038#post1563038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... sort of but not really. That's not a doctrine I can find. I did a quick search of the Catechism and it's not there that I can see. Nor would I expect it to be, since we have the accounts of saints like St Padre Pio who reported being physically beaten by demons. The Book of Job and the demoniacs in the Gospels are also indications that demons are quite capable of more than temptation if they are allowed to be. That's the real distinction. The devil and his ilk can only do what God lets him. For most people this does appear to be limited to temptation and adjacent things, but not for all people, situations, or times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I exaggerated.<br /> <br /> The more precise point is magic, doctrine did not have the notion of demons teaching magic that don't come from YHWH and with his authority. It was, or rather is literally not a thing. If YHWH is the ultimate source and authority, existence outside him is impossible.<br /> <br /> Demons couldn't then &quot;give&quot; magic, thought they could enact their own powers and teach secrets if permitted, although the Church rarely recognized such interventions formally. Even possession was seen as unlikely in many periods, with exorcists existing at the fringes of the Church rather than as a pillar.<br /> <br /> Witchcraft wasn't condemned, belief in it was. Magic done in the name of YHWH existed, the whole situation was far more complex, with far more actors and variety and a lot of change as time went on.<br /> <br /> All that isn't to say the Church is innocent from all accusations, but that it was way more nuanced and internal conflicts abounded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T12:24:48-07:00","id":1563069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563043#post1563043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, I exaggerated.<br /> <br /> The more precise point is magic, doctrine did not have the notion of demons teaching magic that don't come from YHWH and with his authority. It was, or rather is literally not a thing. If YHWH is the ultimate source and authority, existence outside him is impossible.<br /> <br /> Demons couldn't then &quot;give&quot; magic, thought they could enact their own powers and teach secrets if permitted, although the Church rarely recognized such interventions formally. Even possession was seen as unlikely in many periods, with exorcists existing at the fringes of the Church rather than as a pillar.<br /> <br /> Witchcraft wasn't condemned, belief in it was. Magic done in the name of YHWH existed, the whole situation was far more complex, with far more actors and variety and a lot of change as time went on.<br /> <br /> All that isn't to say the Church is innocent from all accusations, but that it was way more nuanced and internal conflicts abounded.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a huge chunk of Church history, accusation of witchcraft was more likely to get you burned than being a witch because they denied magic existed.<br /> <br /> Texts like the 10th-century <i>Canon Episcopi</i> taught that believing a person could physically fly or transform into an animal was a heresy and a lack of true faith in God.<br /> <br /> A downside of the Protestant Reformation was that these pagan traditions and superstitions were revived as legal accusations by people like James I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T15:53:29-07:00","id":1563071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563069#post1563069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a huge chunk of Church history, accusation of witchcraft was more likely to get you burned than being a witch because they denied magic existed.<br /> <br /> Texts like the 10th-century <i>Canon Episcopi</i> taught that believing a person could physically fly or transform into an animal was a heresy and a lack of true faith in God.<br /> <br /> A downside of the Protestant Reformation was that these pagan traditions and superstitions were revived as legal accusations by people like James I.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't deny magic. They denied that the devil could grant magic. YHWH could and did. There are lots of magical grimoires of the time that taught spells using prayers to keep the spirits under control, including the famous Lesser Key of Solomon, and those were not persecuted by the church.<br /> <br /> Being burned by the church was also the last resource, as there was a long process to try and convince the person to recant, and even then the church would refrain from interfering most of the time. There are reasons why those superstitions persisted.<br /> <br /> Very few in the clergy were completely in line with official doctrine, even because discussing doctrine was their job. So to say the church did not formally condemned something isn't to say members of the church didn't participate. They did, and too frequently the church would let it pass to a certain extent.<br /> <br /> Another important distinction is that not every trial about supernatural events were church trials. From witchcraft to vampirism, plenty of cases were judged by secular institutions, not by the Church, which was also how many in the clergy found ways to promote violence without formal Church involvement.<br /> <br /> This happened since the beginning, by the way, it was not a post-Reformation phenomenon. It is true that the Reformation brought a lot of changes to theological and moral landscapes, and the schismatic churches were free to shape doctrine, but by no means this kind of belief is new or exceptional to the period.<br /> <br /> Finally, talking about &quot;these pagan traditions and superstitions&quot; is an abject level of religious prejudice, it's disgusting. It carries within several wrong and ugly assumptions about the beliefs of non-christians that foment violence way more than curb it. I don't think this level of offensive language should be tolerated here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T07:35:32-07:00","id":1563092,"title":"","content":"<br /> There's an important distinction which I think gets lost when most people see texts like the Canon Episcopi. Demons can't grant inherent magical abilities, but they can do things themselves that people aren't capable of. As an alleged example, one of the possible origins of the idea of witches riding broomsticks is that demons couldn't give someone the power to fly, but they could lift and move objects including those people were riding on. How accurate that is, I don't know, but some of the spell books of the time included spells to summon demons and make them do things.<br /> <br /> Part of why we know this is a phenomenon from the Middle Ages known as clerical necromancy and a lot of the spellbooks and other occult works of the time were written by priests and exorcists. Now in one sense that shouldn't be too surprising because priests and clerics made up a disproportionate percentage of the people who could read and write. But they also compiled books of occult knowledge using information they got from demons during exorcisms. Or sometimes they would summon the demons directly for the knowledge because they wanted to bypass the unfortunate element of someone being possessed. And sometimes they also wanted to skip the knowledge part and just summon a demon to do something directly.<br /> <br /> Now this was not an authorized Church practice. In fact, none of this was okay with the Church. These clerics were forgetting several important things, including that demons are lying bastards, are more intelligent and conniving than humans, and that working with demons is dangerous to the soul. This practice likely did a lot more spiritual damage than we will ever know. Nevertheless, the writers and readers of these books could often think that they were doing a good thing by invoking the power of Christ to learn from demons or even unleash their power on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T16:08:33-07:00","id":1563110,"title":"","content":"On the denial of magic (or the denial the devil could grant magic), one of the fun things is reading how many of the church's authors would tie themselves into knots in order to try and explain things. Like, the Old Testament is filled with stories of Israel's enemies and rivals having sorcerers that can cast magic, and that they do so without drawing on God's power. For example, one of the most famous examples is in Exodus where Moses calls of God to turn his staff into a snake. Then the Pharoh summons his sorcerers and they use magic to turn their staves into snakes. But since Moses god was stronger than Egypt's gods, Moses snake eats the others.<br /> <br /> So this necessitated the argument that God was actually the one that supplied Pharoh's sorcerers or the sorcerers of other groups with magic, and God was doing this as a way of testing the faith of the Israelites. Sometimes God would grant miracles to Israel's enemies to punish the Israelities, but then he'd turn around and grant even better miracles to the few Israelities who remained faithful since the whole goal was to test their face. So people who refused to accept the existence of the Christian God could cast magic, it's just that God was the one granting them that power as a way of testing the people who were actually faithful to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T22:25:33-07:00","id":1563113,"title":"","content":"The Israelites of the time had no need for such mental gymnastics, though. They believed their national god was the strongest, not the only one.<br /> <br /> It's among the many things in their beliefs and in the bible(s) that simply weren't the way it is said in current mainstream Christian doctrines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T19:05:21-07:00","id":1563134,"title":"","content":"I wrote a bit about Elijah demonstrating other gods didn't exist to show this change wasn't awhile ago but that is getting a bit off topic.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm kind of reminded from a very minor controversy of SHADOW OF MORDOR (the video game) which had a bunch of collectibles that tied into larger Middle Earth mythology. The controversy was where you come across an idol that belonged to ancient Numenor that venerated Morgoth as the &quot;God of Evil.&quot; Basically, people commented that Morgoth was a Valar and not a god of any sort even if he was worshiped AS A GOD by the fallen Numenoreans and later the people under Sauron's direct rule. Which led to the funny commentary that differentiating Eru, Valar, Maiar, and Morgoth's fallen servants from gods was probably something that was only of interest to theologians or the Istari.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T20:24:40-07:00","id":1563135,"title":"","content":"You can't even dignify yourself to apologize for what you said earlier, eh?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563134#post1563134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote a bit about Elijah demonstrating other gods didn't exist to show this change wasn't awhile ago but that is getting a bit off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what happens in 1 Kings and is a later development.<br /> <br /> Elijah doesn't seek to prove other gods aren't really. He seeks to prove Ba'al weren't real. And he did so (or rather, this part of 1 Kings was written do claim so) for a specific reason: at first YHWH was a storm god, but Ba'al was the storm god worshipped in the area at the time. That was not about a broader challenge, it was a dispute for the portfolio of sky and storms.<br /> <br /> 1 Kings is among the most recent books to be written down, mid to late 6th century BCE, and even then it's not monotheistic unless you brute force the interpretation that a dispute against Ba'al is somehow against the concept of godhood.<br /> <br /> It's by this time that IIRC Josiah initiates the reforms that establish monolatry, which is not the same thing. The bible has books written as long ago as the 14th century BCE, 8 centuries before Josiah, and through all this time they were polytheistic even if El, and later YHWH, was the national god, and the Hebrews were there before, as all that was first oral tradition.<br /> <br /> So we're talking at least about a thousand years of polytheism before monolatry is established and the worship of other gods forbidden. It would take at least 400 more years, possibly 600, before this monolatry got changed into actual monotheism, or something that resembles it.<br /> <br /> We have no sign of monotheism in the whole OT when we look at the old texts and the context of the time, only things that can be misinterpreted when looked at by people from completely different places and eras. And keep in mind that neither is the bible presented in chronological order, nor were the stories written like that. As an example, Deuteronomy seem to take place by the 14th century BCE, has at least some passages that probably were oral tradition by then or a few centuries later, but only got written a few decades before 1 Kings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T07:19:08-07:00","id":1563143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563134#post1563134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote a bit about Elijah demonstrating other gods didn't exist to show this change wasn't awhile ago but that is getting a bit off topic.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm kind of reminded from a very minor controversy of SHADOW OF MORDOR (the video game) which had a bunch of collectibles that tied into larger Middle Earth mythology. The controversy was where you come across an idol that belonged to ancient Numenor that venerated Morgoth as the &quot;God of Evil.&quot; Basically, people commented that Morgoth was a Valar and not a god of any sort even if he was worshiped AS A GOD by the fallen Numenoreans and later the people under Sauron's direct rule. Which led to the funny commentary that differentiating Eru, Valar, Maiar, and Morgoth's fallen servants from gods was probably something that was only of interest to theologians or the Istari.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could write an extremely nerdy fanfic out of the concept of in-universe middle earth theologians debating each other on various pieces of lore. <br /> <br /> It would have an extremely small set of fans, but they would also be extremely invested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T19:47:56-07:00","id":1563151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563143#post1563143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could write an extremely nerdy fanfic out of the concept of in-universe middle earth theologians debating each other on various pieces of lore.<br /> <br /> It would have an extremely small set of fans, but they would also be extremely invested.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it would actually have a way larger set of readers than it has any right to, and I'd be one of them.<br /> <br /> But that was stupid, Black N\u00fcmenorians calling Morgoth a god was perfectly within canon, as was humans in general venerating any Valar as a god. Eru, Ill\u00favathar, Valar and Maiar were elven words used by elven theologians, mainly the Noldor who had literally lived with the Valar and Maiar in their earthly paradise.<br /> <br /> Only by the Third Age would this lore spread among humans, even then just very little. And the Dwarves and Hobbits wouldn't give a damn anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T20:14:38-07:00","id":1563154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563151#post1563151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say it would actually have a way larger set of readers than it has any right to, and I'd be one of them.<br /> <br /> But that was stupid, Black N\u00fcmenorians calling Morgoth a god was perfectly within canon, as was humans in general venerating any Valar as a god. Eru, Ill\u00favathar, Valar and Maiar were elven words used by elven theologians, mainly the Noldor who had literally lived with the Valar and Maiar in their earthly paradise.<br /> <br /> Only by the Third Age would this lore spread among humans, even then just very little. And the Dwarves and Hobbits wouldn't give a damn anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dwarves have the dubious honor of being unplanned for additions that Eru just said, &quot;Sure, why not.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think, officially, Hobbits are just an unusual breed of Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T20:45:29-07:00","id":1563156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563154#post1563154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dwarves have the dubious honor of being unplanned for additions that Eru just said, &quot;Sure, why not.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think, officially, Hobbits are just an unusual breed of Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still extremely miffed at the &quot;pagan traditions&quot; thing, you have no idea how offensive it is and in how many ways, to lots of people and cultures, many of them persecuted actively.<br /> <br /> Christians beating us to social or literal death and then calling their violence &quot;pagan traditions&quot; is not something I can tolerate and keep my peace of mind.<br /> <br /> And to be clear: I'm talking Christianized Europe, Americas and South of Sahara Africa in the period from mid 4th century to today. I'm not saying violence and persecution are exclusive to Christianity in a broader sense, but it is a particularly Christian thing in the context I live, you live, and most forum members live. Christians from Japan, for example, are in their right to feel persecuted by the Shinto majority because they are. There. In Japan.<br /> <br /> On Hobbits Tolkien refused to give a definitive answer, his position AFAIK was that they'd been found out at all too late for any evidence of their origin to be known. But the did recognize that being mutated humans was the most likely by far with the little we know.<br /> <br /> Despite how perfectionist within a given book he was, he also was generally extremely averse to treating any concept in his work as set in stone. He could be quite passionate about that.<br /> <br /> This, and killing Nazis, which is a legit, noble passion we should always remember and praise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T23:02:42-07:00","id":1563160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563154#post1563154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dwarves have the dubious honor of being unplanned for additions that Eru just said, &quot;Sure, why not.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think, officially, Hobbits are just an unusual breed of Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many races are there? Elves, Man, Dwarfs, Ents, Dragons, Orcs &amp; Goblins, Trolls, Intelligent animals, missed anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T00:24:34-07:00","id":1563162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563156#post1563156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still extremely miffed at the &quot;pagan traditions&quot; thing, you have no idea how offensive it is and in how many ways, to lots of people and cultures, many of them persecuted actively.<br /> <br /> Christians beating us to social or literal death and then calling their violence &quot;pagan traditions&quot; is not something I can tolerate and keep my peace of mind.<br /> <br /> And to be clear: I'm talking Christianized Europe, Americas and South of Sahara Africa in the period from mid 4th century to today. I'm not saying violence and persecution are exclusive to Christianity in a broader sense, but it is a particularly Christian thing in the context I live, you live, and most forum members live. Christians from Japan, for example, are in their right to feel persecuted by the Shinto majority because they are. There. In Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could rant about this for hours if given a chance. Nothing pisses me off faster than the genocides of my ancestors (the norse/germanic faithfuls) being minimized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T01:23:44-07:00","id":1563163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563160#post1563160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many races are there? Elves, Man, Dwarfs, Ents, Dragons, Orcs &amp; Goblins, Trolls, Intelligent animals, missed anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides Hobbits?<br /> <br /> Spirits, Giants, Huorns and unique beings, though Tolkien gave very little information on those.<br /> <br /> Giants are cited briefly in The Hobbit when the group is trying to cross the Misty Mountains, before the Orcs take them. They hear in the distance the collisions of the rocks Giants throw at each other. Current editions of the book were slightly modified to fit the LotR, so this part remaining means it is as canon as we can say there's one. It's also during the day IIRC, so they can't be Trolls.<br /> <br /> Huorns are a very specific ambiguity. Ents look like trees and were created by the Vala of trees, but they're very specifically are not trees, but treelike Free People. Huorns are either what happen when an old tree becomes animated or an Ent becomes too static, partly an equivalent to intelligent animals, but tinged by Tolkien's love for trees. The Old Willow-Man is probably a Huorn, and in the book the Huorns are the true saviors in the Battle of Helm's Deep. Weird, scary saviors everyone is thankful for and no one is feeling like going say hi.<br /> <br /> Spirits of many types are cited, but they're also given little to no explanation. Goldberry is a river spirit, the Barrow-Wights are evil spirits possessing corpses, not their original owners. Ghosts. Through all books we actually see a lot of mentions of spirits of things that can be spirits, but they never get much of many explanation and no one ever told anything about where spirits come from, which is itself strange for Tolkien and his many treatises on absolutely everything even when it is to conclude we can't know.<br /> <br /> Unique beings generally fall in the same overall category, but add an important distinction: the mystery is the point. Most races have known history, if not their origin, then at least when and in which circumstances they appeared and theories in what they may be. Spirits are mostly just stated as such or something to that effect and it seems to be explanation enough. But Tom Bombadil, or the strange statues in Rohan are specifically depicted as something that do begs for an explanation, not just unexplained to the reader but active holes in how even the most wise understand the world. Something about them is a contradiction, a challenge to how things are phenomenologically supposed to be.<br /> <br /> You can count some variations, too, besides just ethnicities. Among humans we have the Dr\u00faadan and N\u00famenorians. The first were just between the size of a Hobbit and a Dwarf and were the very first human tribe the elves found in Beleriand. Their eyes glowed red sometimes. N\u00famenorians are technically humans but are actually elf-touched and blessed. Aragorn is one of them and he's more than 70 when Frodo meets him, dying with more than 200 years, more than a fucking century after the end of the story.<br /> <br /> Entwives are another mystery for the reader. If on one hand they seem obvious, they seem to have some fundamental distinctions in their nature besides gender<br /> <br /> Saruman made the Uruk-Hai and the Half Orcs. The first bigger, meaner, braver and actually more militaristic for real than Orcs. The second capable of passing for ugly humans despite being orcs.<br /> <br /> Finally the Olog-Hai, the new breed of Troll that Sauron created but we get very little about them, contrary to quite the thorough depiction we get from Saruman's creations.<br /> <br /> Honorable mention for Istarii and Balrogs. They may be Maiar, but did form each a semi-race of their own even if limited in number.<br /> <br /> Note: by the mid 20th century of Middle Earth it is confirmed that Elves, Dwarves and Hobbits are still around, while Dragons, Orcs and Trolls are confirmed extinct. Many fans know about the importance of the Appendix in LotR, but no one tells you about the preface. It changes your understanding of the book drastically if you pay attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T01:35:05-07:00","id":1563164,"title":"","content":"I think we should return to the topic at hand. Tolkien stuff is pretty off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:39-07:00","id":1563165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563162#post1563162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could rant about this for hours if given a chance. Nothing pisses me off faster than the genocides of my ancestors (the norse/germanic faithfuls) being minimized.</div> </div> </div> </div>In America we have this happening right now with indigenous faithful from Canada to Chile. Here in Brazil Pentecostal churches convert the natives with methods made to galvanize their anger and frustration against their own people. Sacred places vandalized or destroyed, and sometimes holy people of the native faiths are brutalized.<br /> <br /> All by other natives? Yes, but as the end result of a very, very deliberate program that prey on their economic and social crisis in the name of a tradition that I can assure you, isn't in any way, shape or form &quot;pagan&quot;.<br /> <br /> Make my neopagan problems seem laughable in comparison and I already suffer with the dozens to hundreds of micro aggressions people commit every day by assuming YHWH as such an obvious fact.<br /> <br /> African Roots Religions as we call here have to deal daily with Terreiros being vandalized, or hit by arsonists. Even Kardecists, and you can't get more white people religion than those guys are targeted sometimes. I've seen a case years ago in an apartment building where one of the tenants found out another was Kardecist. They planned everything, invaded the apartment of the other with 12 good members of the church and I don't remember now if the victim survived after being hospitalized.<br /> <br /> Brazil is not the worse. Far from it. We manage to protect our &quot;fringe religions&quot; way better than the lawless cyberpunk hellscape sitting between Mexico and Canada.<br /> <br /> And while I defend the Japanese Catholics for being really persecuted and it's a very ugly situation (though not as physically violent), they have always been the group most prone to vandalize holy places of others in Japan. They still do it today, not all of them, not most of them, but not a negligible portion of them and not without some cover-up by the community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T01:52:59-07:00","id":1563166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563164#post1563164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should return to the topic at hand. Tolkien stuff is pretty off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Covering social problems, though, is in my opinion the main thing that would have been better for V5, because it was offensive to call that sanitized joke Gothic Punk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T02:58:58-07:00","id":1563168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563166#post1563166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Covering social problems, though, is in my opinion the main thing that would have been better for V5, because it was offensive to call that sanitized joke Gothic Punk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with both of your posts. It sadly would never have happened given the foundations of V5 was rotted given who built them. We're talking about someone who shoved a claustrophobe into a closet and talked about challenging &quot;safe spaces&quot; in an interview. You'd need completely different people than those we got to build the foundation needed for covering social problems properly and tastefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T03:28:46-07:00","id":1563170,"title":"","content":"The main thing that would have been better for V5 would have been a better metaplot with a lot of depth to it. Really bring the continuity from the 90s into the modern age.<br /> <br /> Really difficult to pull of though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T12:13:33-07:00","id":1563185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563156#post1563156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still extremely miffed at the &quot;pagan traditions&quot; thing, you have no idea how offensive</div> </div> </div> </div>So noted.<br /> <br /> No offense was intended but it should also be clear it doesn't refer to Christianity or real world Pre-Christian or post-Christian indigenous European faiths. It refers only to Middle Earth and the barely described religious practices of Valar worship. I think it's important that we do draw strong lines whenever possible between fiction and reality. <br /> <br /> My apologies for making it unclear that I wasn't referring to anything but fictional subjects in the world.<br /> <br /> Which I bring back to the Gothic Punk discussion of the fact that a lot of the changes seemed designed to avoid issues among the fandom versus actual issues within the setting. The Sabbat was not a playable faction because, and this is just my speculation, they didn't want stories of players slaughtering hosts of innocents and playing human head football like...well, the Sabbat do.<br /> <br /> To be fair, early V5 was riddled with controversies too. Sometimes justified, sometimes not. Remember the Chechnya Incident written by an author trying to bring attention to RL injustices...in the most questionable manner possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-17-2026, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T12:58:17-07:00","id":1563189,"title":"","content":"I remember that particular muck up. Involving vampires with it was questionable from the start to be honest and requires a very delicate hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T14:32:55-07:00","id":1563194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563170#post1563170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing that would have been better for V5 would have been a better metaplot with a lot of depth to it. Really bring the continuity from the 90s into the modern age.<br /> <br /> Really difficult to pull of though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being averse to criticism and scandal is part of this. I didn't say there's worse was lack of political engagement just because I like it, but because this engagement <b><i>is</i></b> the fuel of the countercultural impetus behind what White Wolf did in the 90s and Onyx Path in the 2010s.<br /> <br /> Another problem was wanting to have the cake and eat it by proposing several plots but want to keep the setting stable, so nothing follows to their proper conclusion.<br /> <br /> Finally simply being stingy and control freak with the book rollout. Few books approved, cheap partners, conservative investment in the wrong moments. There's simply not enough published material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563185#post1563185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So noted.<br /> <br /> No offense was intended but it should also be clear it doesn't refer to Christianity or real world Pre-Christian or post-Christian indigenous European faiths. It refers only to Middle Earth and the barely described religious practices of Valar worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrase I'm miffed about is in post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/167\" >V20 Ghouls Outline Panel Recap</a> and was about the Inquisition tangent. Wrong apology, the Tolkien part was ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563185#post1563185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I bring back to the Gothic Punk discussion of the fact that a lot of the changes seemed designed to avoid issues among the fandom versus actual issues within the setting. The Sabbat was not a playable faction because, and this is just my speculation, they didn't want stories of players slaughtering hosts of innocents and playing human head football like...well, the Sabbat do.<br /> <br /> To be fair, early V5 was riddled with controversies too. Sometimes justified, sometimes not. Remember the Chechnya Incident written by an author trying to bring attention to RL injustices...in the most questionable manner possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat part they made pretty clear several times that it was simply not &quot;their vision&quot; for the game and what that vision was. Saying they had any moral fears is to ignore several times they said they didn't want alternatives to Humanity, didn't think the Sabbat should be more than mindless Lost Boys and didn't care if anyone disagreed.<br /> <br /> When it came to their very narrow vision of the setting in the first years they were quite open and perfectly wiling to offend the fandom. This is not what happened.<br /> <br /> Controversies take many forms and can be dealt with in many ways. Those differences are not superficial. White Wolf got into several controversies back in the day due to trying to tackle issues and messing up. And their response each time was to hear the fandom, learn more, try again doing better. They never avoided controversy and that was key. It was the reason why despite all the bad takes, the players from minority groups gravitated in droves to WoD. We love it because it remember we exist, our issues are real, and they try even if it opens them up to criticism.<br /> <br /> Paradox did it exactly once. Their reaction was to shut down image risks, going for &quot;safe diversity&quot;: when you have people of all kinds, but somehow they don't face any problems because their world is horrible, but horrible with an open mind and equity policies.<br /> <br /> All their other controversies were just errors by incompetence or lack of awareness rather than misplaced awareness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563189#post1563189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that particular muck up. Involving vampires with it was questionable from the start to be honest and requires a very delicate hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bigger problem wasn't even that. Old WW did similar fuck ups several times. They never gave up, recognized the error and committed to do better.<br /> <br /> Had Paradox asked how to do better and tried to learn more about Chechnya to improve rather than give up, things would have gone way better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T17:58:47-07:00","id":1563205,"title":"","content":"FYI -<br /> <br /> The Chechnya thing wasn't Paradox but very much the writer who lived in Georgia (the country not the state). Even today I'd rather not identify him despite how easily it is to figure out who it was from this information alone.<br /> <br /> It was very much motivated by his own horror at friends being persecuted in RL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T03:30:43-07:00","id":1563218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563205#post1563205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI -<br /> <br /> The Chechnya thing wasn't Paradox but very much the writer who lived in Georgia (the country not the state). Even today I'd rather not identify him despite how easily it is to figure out who it was from this information alone.<br /> <br /> It was very much motivated by his own horror at friends being persecuted in RL.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Paradox in the sense that everything done by an employer publicly in the name of a company is the company doing it.<br /> <br /> This is both social and legal staple. Unless a given piece has explicit wording about the company transferring responsibility to the author, if it was publicized or published by the company it is the company.<br /> <br /> You can't constantly treat an entity made of a collection of people as not responsible by the actions of those people. It's actually the other way around.<br /> <br /> And in the specific Chechnya debacle, the company had assumed responsibility to revise and approve/veto things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T07:02:37-07:00","id":1563223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563194#post1563194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bigger problem wasn't even that. Old WW did similar fuck ups several times. They never gave up, recognized the error and committed to do better.<br /> <br /> Had Paradox asked how to do better and tried to learn more about Chechnya to improve rather than give up, things would have gone way better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might've gone a bit better initially, but with the sort of people they'd hired, I doubt it would've amounted to much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T12:52:21-07:00","id":1563230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563223#post1563223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might've gone a bit better initially, but with the sort of people they'd hired, I doubt it would've amounted to much.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all related. Which kind of people they hired, kind of decision they took, kind of spiel they gave, and kind of market goals they sought and kind of setting they envisioned, all came from the kind of stupid they were.<br /> <br /> Each is both partly cause and partly because of the others in a feedback loop of company culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T14:07:56-07:00","id":1563234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563230#post1563230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all related. Which kind of people they hired, kind of decision they took, kind of spiel they gave, and kind of market goals they sought and kind of setting they envisioned, all came from the kind of stupid they were.<br /> <br /> Each is both partly cause and partly because of the others in a feedback loop of company culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a incestuous cancerous growth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T02:23:01-07:00","id":1563244,"title":"","content":"Probably would help any wod developer to play some solid Ars Magica games. Just for the long form structure of seasonal play. Setting matters more when your characters live through a few years or decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T23:55:24-07:00","id":1563275,"title":"","content":"Making them consider the impact of the rules on the setting, its lore and its worldbuilding would be a nice start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T03:21:09-07:00","id":1563332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563194#post1563194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it came to their very narrow vision of the setting in the first years they were quite open and perfectly wiling to offend the fandom. This is not what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's honestly kind of weird. The brazen disregard for WoD's longtime fans. Not just with V5, but H5 and W5 too.<br /> <br /> Like, Paradox bought the rights to World of Darkness <i>specifically</i> to mine its intellectual property. It was a bid to exploit 90s nostalgia.<br /> <br /> And yet, the developers displayed contempt for long-time fans who had opinions about WoD, and who wanted to play it with the setting tentpoles and options they always had. Paradox insisted pissing off &quot;Legacy&quot; players was no big deal, presumably because they felt they didn't need them to be successful.<br /> <br /> Which is it, Paradox? Did you want their money or didn't you?<br /> <br /> WoD is a nostalgia property. Big chunks of its fanbase are oldheads. It's comparatively rare for someone to really want a new round of editions if they weren't around for the original. Even those who DID come in later (like myself) fell in love with the original versions (or the WoD20 versions, which were not terribly different). I would argue it's difficult to get wholly new fans - many who weren't even alive during Classic WoD's original run - without a large number of existing fans to onboard people. (Because TTRPGs are a Folk Tradition, passed on from one practitioner to another).<br /> <br /> What did Paradox think was going to happen here? That it would be a <i>Field of Dreams</i> situation, and new fans would just <i>show up</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T07:55:39-07:00","id":1563335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563332#post1563332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's honestly kind of weird. The brazen disregard for WoD's longtime fans. Not just with V5, but H5 and W5 too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's not exactly what happened.<br /> <br /> The specific reason behind their attitude at the time was actually a very common problem the fan base had in the 90s.<br /> <br /> Just like most IPs, WoD has many ways to be engaged with, many interpretations and takes, many phases and elements added, moved or ignored along the years.<br /> <br /> And like many IPs, some fans are passionate not just about the game, but about their own preferences and takes. For them, their tastes are the One True Way, their interpretation the Gospel Truth, and alternatives are ignorance at best and offenses at worse.<br /> <br /> Unlike most IPs, WoD had a number of authors back then that actively defended and fed this attitude, and had a particularly narrow vision of how the game should be &quot;properly played&quot;. An extremely pedantic bunch with serious views of Vampire as some superior art form that was meant to be played with artistic intent.<br /> <br /> Some of the most important authors in the first five years of White Wolf followed this path, and that included the game's creator himself, Mark Rein-Hagen. That made fans feel validated that their narrow, angst heavy, street level theatrical inner monologue way wasn't just fun, but worth demeaning and humiliating other people over.<br /> <br /> Yes, Rein-Hagen is this kind of person. Today he's still active and the same obnoxious prick as ever. He was called to participate in V5 back when precisely because of this, there is also a reason why most publishers don't call him, but they did. The Paradox CEO that pushed for the acquisition of WoD was from this bunch, as was Ericsson, the lead writer.<br /> <br /> I'd like to say it was somehow capitalism's fault that V5 went the way it went, but it was really a problem of the first two or three generations of players, a problem that should have died in the 90s, but survived to plague us today.<br /> <br /> V5 is what happens when someone who only cares about their own vision get their hands in a beloved IP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T12:03:35-07:00","id":1563346,"title":"","content":"You see that in every fandom and we are guilty of this to some extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T12:55:30-07:00","id":1563348,"title":"","content":"That's why I'm adamant about not indulging those who say if they could they'd make VtM this or that, and ignore V5 completely, even if I like their proposals: because that's the attitude that created V5 in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you want the setting to get rid of elements you don't like just because you don't like them, and/or if you want to do to V5 and its fans what you feel they did to you, you're just the same kind of jerk that'll commit the same kind of errors and I wouldn't trust you with the IP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T18:25:24-07:00","id":1563355,"title":"","content":"I feel like if they were going to remove a faction from the game, it should have been the Anarchs, not the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs collectively agreeing to declare open war against the Camarilla doesn't make any sense from a lore perspective, seeing as how the Anarchs are supposed to be about the freedom of self rule, and how each Anarch ruled domain has wildly different forms of government from each other.<br /> <br /> They are by no means a unified group who agree on policy. While it's acceptable that one or two domains may have decided to throw down the gauntlet, the entire sect is a different story.<br /> <br /> ALSO, the Anarchs would have to be even more stupid than I was already lead to believe, if they genuinely thought that declaring war against the Ivory Tower during a second inquisition was the right call. Like, yeah, sure, you're going to fend off the full brunt of a global Hunter organization by yourself, without any sense of cooperation or resources?<br /> <br /> <br /> I believe it would have been better to have the Anarchs either swallow their pride and join the Camarilla officially, or have the Camarilla take off the kid gloves and forcefully absorb them into the organization. Then the Sabbat (the original Anarchs) could take on the role of being the antiestablishment sect of vampires within the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T23:17:30-07:00","id":1563359,"title":"","content":"Anarchs shouldn't even be a sect. They never formalized this arrangement, it makes no sense and wasn't a thing even in fan parlance before Revised.<br /> <br /> The sects are Camarilla and Sabbat, with the Camarilla declaring itself universal vampire law instead of a faction, technically everyone is Camarilla and Anarch is a generic name for any vampire in a Domain that's unsatisfied with the local Prince. They have no commonality and no actual allegiance outside the Camarilla, or even necessarily anything against the Camarilla, just the Prince.<br /> <br /> While they fit some fan expectations and are in theory possible developments, everything they did with the sects is wildly out of character and shallow, flattening things way more than doing anything favors and positively distorting what the sects were and did form the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T06:26:27-07:00","id":1563365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563355#post1563355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like if they were going to remove a faction from the game, it should have been the Anarchs, not the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs collectively agreeing to declare open war against the Camarilla doesn't make any sense from a lore perspective, seeing as how the Anarchs are supposed to be about the freedom of self rule, and how each Anarch ruled domain has wildly different forms of government from each other.<br /> <br /> They are by no means a unified group who agree on policy. While it's acceptable that one or two domains may have decided to throw down the gauntlet, the entire sect is a different story.<br /> <br /> ALSO, the Anarchs would have to be even more stupid than I was already lead to believe, if they genuinely thought that declaring war against the Ivory Tower during a second inquisition was the right call. Like, yeah, sure, you're going to fend off the full brunt of a global Hunter organization by yourself, without any sense of cooperation or resources?<br /> <br /> <br /> I believe it would have been better to have the Anarchs either swallow their pride and join the Camarilla officially, or have the Camarilla take off the kid gloves and forcefully absorb them into the organization. Then the Sabbat (the original Anarchs) could take on the role of being the antiestablishment sect of vampires within the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would not make sense because:<br /> <br /> 1) they wanted to make, as silly as it was, Anarch the default faction in V5<br /> <br /> 2) decisions were made about the setting and logic of those decisions in-game was rarely questioned or explored (not that it was unique to V5, we had a lot of those in Revised)<br /> <br /> Honestly, we could just stop at point 1. It was decided that Anarchs are &quot;good guys&quot; Sabbat are &quot;bad guys&quot; so one is getting propped up and the other is nuked down from the (writing) orbit. But for all the focus that was put on Anarchs the writing did not do anything to make the sect more compelling than it was in earlier editions as far as I could tell. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> that for most of the first two editions anarchs were just a rogue element of Camarilla but they could, in theory, have been made more than that. <br /> <br /> But it was not to be. Setites and Tzimisce joining the sect was not making it any more appealing - you could have played Tzimisce of Setite anarch before V5. But the core of the sect did not change, they still only mad esense in opposition to Camarilla and there was barely any attempt to give the sect depth as it was done with Assamites in Revised or with the True Hand in V20.<br /> <br /> IMO, V5 biggest sin was that it had a rich well of lore to draw from but they decided that a lot of that well is poisoned and unfit for fans' consumption so they decided to keep it away. Sabbat and KotE are prominent examples of it. They thought those were bad and if you wanted to play them you were bad and they were not going to accommodate you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T11:35:02-07:00","id":1563368,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that sums it up.<br /> <br /> Their decisions were the natural conclusion of a shallow, limited view of the game.<br /> <br /> Simply put, they didn't promote the Anarchs and ditched the Sabbat because they wanted to reduce/simplify sects. They did it because they thought the default game should be about playing Anarchs against the Camarilla and the Sabbat shouldn't be a playable option.<br /> <br /> Nuking the Sabbat and raising the Anarchs was not a strategy. It was the goal. Narrowing how the game can be played was not a means to an end. It was the end. Paradox didn't simplify the game to make it accessible, despite saying so. Removing &quot;wrong&quot; options was the goal all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T13:20:02-07:00","id":1563372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563365#post1563365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would not make sense because:<br /> <br /> 1) they wanted to make, as silly as it was, Anarch the default faction in V5<br /> <br /> 2) decisions were made about the setting and logic of those decisions in-game was rarely questioned or explored (not that it was unique to V5, we had a lot of those in Revised)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which proves they knew little, to nothing about the setting.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are full of shit. They have always been full of shit.<br /> <br /> Vampires are fundamentally selfish creatures at their very core. They cooperate only in the interest of self preservation, and will sell each other out the very instant they smell an opportunity to pull ahead of the competition. They are not a species who can survive in a society of equal opportunity, where they simply trust each other to cooperate.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why L.A was the <i>&quot;last remaining Anarch Free State.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Once again, the Anarchs had no sense of cohesion between them. Every domain had its own way of doing things. They were chaotic, disorganized rabble.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla may be tyrannical, but at least they had structure and rules to follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> <br /> So to reiterate, I think that in the wake of a Second Inqusition, the Anarchs should have bit the bullet and joined up with the Camarilla, or the Camarilla should have told them they didn't have the patience to put up with their crap anymore, and forced them to bend the knee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T13:28:59-07:00","id":1563374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563348#post1563348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I'm adamant about not indulging those who say if they could they'd make VtM this or that, and ignore V5 completely, even if I like their proposals: because that's the attitude that created V5 in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you want the setting to get rid of elements you don't like just because you don't like them, and/or if you want to do to V5 and its fans what you feel they did to you, you're just the same kind of jerk that'll commit the same kind of errors and I wouldn't trust you with the IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with this. But they're also in a bind because V5 is so antithetical to much that came before it. You can't easily bring back things they cut without some backpedalling.<br /> <br /> Take <i>Montreal by Night</i>\u2014per <i>CHAPTERS</i>, the entire Sabbat is wiped out there. If you wanted to bring back any of those classic characters, it involves some sort of backpedalling (though I think we discussed how to do this previously\u2014e.g., with the Sabbat luring the Camarilla in to infect them with Blood Rot, and then coming back to reclaim much of the city afterwards, with some of the key characters having fled in anticipation of this plan).<br /> <br /> You're gonna piss people off anyway, but hopefully, you don't also rub salt in the wound by going &quot;Haha!&quot; or pretending it never happened.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T13:50:31-07:00","id":1563375,"title":"","content":"After reading V5 back in the day, I recall walking away with the impression that the Camarilla were the better option and the Anarchs were now Sabbat-Lite at best. They just came across as too edgelordy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T15:05:57-07:00","id":1563378,"title":"","content":"Anarchs becoming its own sect is good for gameplay. Three core sects is a nice asymmetry, and hey, faction that could really use some world building.<br /> <br /> ...putting the sabbat as an npc faction neuters the first part.<br /> And they didn't resolve the core issue with the anarchs, they need a philosophy of power, a foundational idea, and a core narrative thematic that makes sense for them.<br /> <br /> Camarilla: Foundational idea: We maintain the masquerade. Narrative theme: In a camarilla game your PC pretends to be human. Power structure is feudal with strict hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Foundational idea: We fight ancients. Narrative theme: In a sabbat game you get to be the monster in a horror story. Power structure: Decentralized packs with a culture and structures to enforce loyalty and some hierarchical bonds, though less stringent than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Anarch: Foundational idea... Freedom but not really explained how they view it. Narrative theme: because we haven't really a developed take on the freedom thing you can't really play it so... Just pretend to be human. Power structure: eh, like the camarilla except the prince is called a baron and you could have more than one but probably it'll just be like the camarilla. Philosophy of power: directly related to their foundational idea and they don't really have one.<br /> <br /> Lot's of interesting things you could do with the anarchs but it requires some work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T16:36:51-07:00","id":1563383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563372#post1563372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which proves they knew little, to nothing about the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I don't think any generalized view is much better, you're missing a lot of it too.<br /> <br /> Precisely because the Anarchs have no sense of cohesion, saying they're full of shit or should have done this or that is missing their point completely.<br /> <br /> They can't be right or wrong if they don't have a unified position. Each Anarch is unique, their only commonality being the basic fact of having an opinion their local Prince don't agree with. No Anarch answers for any other Anarch. Any can be full of shit, or completely right, or anything in between.<br /> <br /> Similarly they can't decide to bow because they can't decide anything. There's no unified stand to bend one way or the other. The Camarilla can't do anything about &quot;them&quot; either because each one is a unique case. There's no &quot;Anarch Faction&quot; to do something about it.<br /> <br /> In the end that's the reason the game used to treat Anarch as an adjective, not a sect, and why any take on them as a sect is ultimately a misunderstanding. There's no organization that can answer to, react to or be held accountable for anything about them.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are an adjective to describe political opposition to the Prince in virtually any sense. It's what you call someone who isn't supporter or indifferent. That's that, the end, no more to say. That's also why only the Free States are Anarch, actually many other Domains saw their local Anarchs depose the local Prince. Those Anarchs elevated another Prince and ceased to be called Anarchs. And the Free States are less a political schism from the Camarilla and more places where no one has any real idea of what to do other than a vague notion that they don't want a new Prince and are willing to live in a no man's land instead.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't intrinsically selfish, either. They are culturally selfish, but as I said I'm another thread, in the end the very idea that this is their nature is actually an excuse to justify their very human decision to chose convenience. They're not innately selfish and the failure of the Free States is mainly for two reasons: lack of any actual unifying plan or political will to do better, and the setting requiring things to be fucked up in the books for your group to solve it out of not in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563374#post1563374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're gonna piss people off anyway, but hopefully, you don't also rub salt in the wound by going &quot;Haha!&quot; or pretending it never happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the gist of it, though.<br /> <br /> You will have to make decisions, and some are going to mess with things someone likes. The problem isn't to do it, but how you go about it.<br /> <br /> Basically to questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are you doing it because you think you have to, so you can implement improvements, or are you just ripping off what you don't like so you don't have to look at it?<br /> <br /> 2. Can you show respect for those who liked it and recognize in-character it was a thing, or are you just going to brush it off or be a dick to the people who dislike your take?<br /> <br /> Outside that, they have options. Getting the example of Ciudad del Mexico and Montreal, even in V5 the problem was not that they got taken by the Camarilla. The problem is that they takeover is hastily and badly written, their previous state mostly ignored and they run as if they had always been Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Just trying to make a good story about it and having the transition leave lasting impacts in the two cities would have made it completely different. Still piss off people? Sure. But it would feel like a legitimate decision we don't like rather than the asshole move it obviously was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563378#post1563378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs becoming its own sect is good for gameplay. Three core sects is a nice asymmetry, and hey, faction that could really use some world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd reframe it a little, though:<br /> <br /> The Anarch Free States becoming the base for a new sect would have been good for gameplay.<br /> <br /> Such a sect would have to be built, though, and it wouldn't be the sect of everyone who earlier had identified as Anarchs, they'd be their own faction, doing theirs own thing. Even if they get to use the name Anarch, the old concept would still exist as the political malcontents of wherever you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T19:54:27-07:00","id":1563394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563383#post1563383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but I don't think any generalized view is much better, you're missing a lot of it too.<br /> <br /> Precisely because the Anarchs have no sense of cohesion, saying they're full of shit or should have done this or that is missing their point completely.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify what I mean when I say they're full of shit, is that the Anarchs claim to oppose the Camarilla doctrine, yet they co-opted much of their systems and just changed the terminology.<br /> <br /> Barons might be lower ranked than Princes, but they're still a member of the aristocracy! If you wanted to differentiate them from the Ivory Tower, they should have been referred to by a more modern name.<br /> <br /> Since the Baron is <i>allegedly</i> someone who earned their position through charisma, rather than force, they could have been called the Anarch President; or maybe Anarch Mediator, who is trusted to weigh in on internal disputes.<br /> <br /> <br /> They also claim that everyone has a voice within their society; but in practice, this only applies to those who's voice echoes what they want to hear. The moment you start to criticize what the Anarchs are doing, they suddenly turn aggressive and say that you're part of the problem.<br /> <br /> Just look at how quickly Nines and Skelter resulted to hurling insults as soon as we try to defend the Camarilla. Hell, Nines even threatened to start a brawl when you point out the similarities between Princes and Barons.<br /> <br /> Then there was Isaac, who demands <i>&quot;a token of tribute&quot;</i> as a sign of proper respect in order for you to freely operate in Hollywood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 08-23-2026, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T04:15:30-07:00","id":1563400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563394#post1563394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify what I mean when I say they're full of shit, is that the Anarchs claim to oppose the Camarilla doctrine, yet they co-opted much of their systems and just changed the terminology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they?<br /> <br /> The Free States are not the whole of Anarchs or even a meaningful percentage of them. LA is not the whole of the Free States. Isaac is not the only or standard LA Baron. And Nines is not voicing some standard opinion within LA.<br /> <br /> You're generalizing from a few examples that have never been meant to represent anything beyond themselves. Just look at all LA Barons in the last few decades: Abrams is a standard feudal lord, Rodriguez barely imposes any rule beyond pure vitriol against Camarilla, Voerman has not a lick of a problem recognizing any of the Camarilla representatives and their territory claims (usually over Nines' territory), Ming Xiao isn't even Kindred and Jenna Cross isn't really Anarch, either, as they're no better for the Thin Blood in LA.<br /> <br /> Baron is a term the LA Anarch gangs from the 40s coined, a time when Los Angeles had 13 of them. It means nothing beyond those 13 gangs liked the word and no one ever cared enough to change it, even if Abrams is the only one to like it for real, the others don't give a fuck. And all that ignores the huge influence of Smiling Jack and his barony of himself.<br /> <br /> So how can you in LA alone say they're full of shit? They wouldn't side with the Camarilla? Nines and Abrams not, Voerman and Ming Xiao literally did and Cross wasn't offered the option. They coopted Camarilla systems? Well, Abrams and Voerman did, Nines, Cross and Ming most definitely didn't. They claim titles of aristocracy? Abrams is the only one big on that, the others don't care either way. Everyone has a voice? Only Nines claim that, out of five.<br /> <br /> And that's LA alone. Not a single statement on what &quot;the Anarchs&quot; defend as a faction applies to more than 2 of 5 effective Barons and that didn't cover a fraction of the population that is identified as Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T04:26:20-07:00","id":1563401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563400#post1563400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they?<br /> <br /> The Free States are not the whole of Anarchs or even a meaningful percentage of them. LA is not the whole of the Free States. Isaac is not the only or standard LA Baron. And Nines is not voicing some standard opinion within LA.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but first impressions are important, and Bloodlines 1 didn't give a very good first impression of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563400#post1563400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're generalizing from a few examples that have never been meant to represent anything beyond themselves. Just look at all LA Barons in the last few decades: Abrams is a standard feudal lord, Rodriguez barely imposes any rule beyond pure vitriol against Camarilla, Voerman has not a lick of a problem recognizing any of the Camarilla representatives and their territory claims (usually over Nines' territory), Ming Xiao isn't even Kindred and Jenna Cross isn't really Anarch, either, as they're no better for the Thin Blood in LA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who the heck is Jenna Cross?<br /> <br /> As for the Voermans, I always assumed that Therese was a Camarilla, due to how much she was trying to get into their good graces. Bertram even says flat out that she may be trying to establish herself as <i>&quot;Prince of Santa Monica.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Then there's the lore about Jeanette pegging Lacroix, which I seriously doubt he'd allow an Anarch to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563400#post1563400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So how can you in LA alone say they're full of shit? They wouldn't side with the Camarilla? Nines and Abrams not, Voerman and Ming Xiao literally did and Cross wasn't offered the option. They coopted Camarilla systems? Well, Abrams and Voerman did, Nines, Cross and Ming most definitely didn't. They claim titles of aristocracy? Abrams is the only one big on that, the others don't care either way. Everyone has a voice? Only Nines claim that, out of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minx Xiao isn't a cainite, she's Kuei Jin. A completely different species of undead from those of the western vampire. She shouldn't be lumped in as an example of possible Anarch behavior, because the term doesn't apply to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T05:21:09-07:00","id":1563407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563401#post1563401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but first impressions are important, and Bloodlines 1 didn't give a very good first impression of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Who the heck is Jenna Cross?<br /> <br /> As for the Voermans, I always assumed that Therese was a Camarilla, due to how much she was trying to get into their good graces. Bertram even says flat out that she may be trying to establish herself as <i>&quot;Prince of Santa Monica.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Then there's the lore about Jeanette pegging Lacroix, which I seriously doubt he'd allow an Anarch to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Minx Xiao isn't a cainite, she's Kuei Jin. A completely different species of undead from those of the western vampire. She shouldn't be lumped in as an example of possible Anarch behavior, because the term doesn't apply to her.</div> </div> </div> </div>A faction isn't based on first impressions and Bloodlines is a videogame from 2004. It's not a first impression, it happens literally 10 years after the original LA by Night sourcebook.<br /> <br /> Ming Xiao was counted among the Council of Barons for years, precisely until the events of the game. She's literally one of the canonical Anarch Barons and had recognized dominion over kindred in China Town as such, meeting the others Barons for discussions regarding the city as a whole.<br /> <br /> Therese is an Anarch Baron. She's not and has never been Camarilla, doesn't claim or want a position in their hierarchy, she's just fine with being allies with them.<br /> <br /> Cross is a Thin Blood who rose to prominence some time after the events in Bloodlines and is the <i>de facto</i> Baron of the Pier area, the others couldn't oust her.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines is a snapshot in one of the most extensively used and described cities in WoD across all lines. It barely touches everything there is to know about the city's Anarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:11:57-07:00","id":1563413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563407#post1563407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A faction isn't based on first impressions and Bloodlines is a videogame from 2004. It's not a first impression, it happens literally 10 years after the original LA by Night sourcebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the presentation was still relevant at the time, because it was made before V5 overhauled everything. Also, many of us had never even heard of World of Darkness until Bloodlines came out, because we were getting our gaming information from paperback magazines, instead of online gaming channels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563407#post1563407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ming Xiao was counted among the Council of Barons for years, precisely until the events of the game. She's literally one of the canonical Anarch Barons and had recognized dominion over kindred in China Town as such, meeting the others Barons for discussions regarding the city as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems odd, considering that literally every vampire in the city who has something to say about the Kuei Jin all unanimously tell you stay the hell away from them, because they are untrustworthy devils. Nines even comments about how the Kuei Jin just wholesale slaughtered the Anarchs when they first arrived in the city, and the Camarilla was able to gain a foothold because they had just recently finished a war with the Kuei Jin.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:40:34-07:00","id":1563417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563413#post1563413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and the presentation was still relevant at the time, because it was made before V5 overhauled everything. Also, many of us had never even heard of World of Darkness until Bloodlines came out, because we were getting our gaming information from paperback magazines, instead of online gaming channels.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's your ignorance about the setting, not the setting being mine the game.<br /> <br /> You are saying the Anarchs are X in the setting because your impression of the videogame was that the Anarchs in the game were X. I'm telling you the setting is wider and older than the videogame, and your impression of the videogame is already wrong given that Therese wasn't Camarilla at any point there.<br /> <br /> Now you're saying the game is the truth that matters to the setting because you didn't knew they'd setting before? Are this for real a serious statement? You're literally saying the setting should have the Anarchs not be like in the game despite the setting having the Anarchs not be like in the game?<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with you not knowing how things are in the actual TTRPG books. But saying the videogame is more relevant to the books than the books is bizarre.<br /> <br /> Ming Xiao arrived at war, then a lot of shit happened, I'll reiterate that the fucking game is a snapshot after 10 years of canon publication of the city, its supernatural inhabitants and its long history.<br /> <br /> Get out of videos of idiots blurting any stupid nonsense they find funny about the setting and go read and actual book, they're not hard to get even today and definitely not a long or hard read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:47:14-07:00","id":1563419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563417#post1563417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's your ignorance about the setting, not the setting being mine the game.<br /> <br /> You are saying the Anarchs are X in the setting because your impression of the videogame was that the Anarchs in the game were X. I'm telling you the setting is wider and older than the videogame, and your impression of the videogame is already wrong given that Therese wasn't Camarilla at any point there.<br /> <br /> Now you're saying the game is the truth that matters to the setting because you didn't knew they'd setting before? Are this for real a serious statement? You're literally saying the setting should have the Anarchs not be like in the game despite the setting having the Anarchs not be like in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying that this was the first impression a lot of us were subjected to. It's what got many of us into the World of Darkness franchise to begin with. If there was anything in the lore that contradicted that presentation, we didn't learn about it until later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563417#post1563417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ming Xiao arrived at war, then a lot of shit happened, I'll reiterate that the fucking game is a snapshot after 10 years of canon publication of the city, its supernatural inhabitants and its long history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, now, about 20 something years later. But as a newcomer to the franchise, I didn't know what to expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T10:55:47-07:00","id":1563421,"title":"","content":"Well, then that's it. The Anarchs aren't full of shit just because they're not full of anything in particular.<br /> <br /> Abrams is definitely full of shit, but he's just a Camarilla Elder that don't have enough power to hold praxis over a city, so he holds praxis over Hollywood and pretends he isn't weaker than the other Barons, except maybe for the one who's a literal Thin Blood.<br /> <br /> Voerman is easy the most powerful in LA in the present, and she's more than wiling to play with the Camarilla when they're in town. Nines is... There, I guess. He's the only one among the four current Barons (Ming is out of the picture) who's anything like what V5 calls an Anarch, and he's popular enough that if he gets behind something the other three are likely to follow suit by default, but otherwise he's just the guy people will point you to if you ask for anything resembling authority in Downtown, no surprise that LaCroix got to claim praxis over his turf and no one seemed to care, not even him.<br /> <br /> Janette doesn't count as Baron, by the way. As far as she's concerned, she lives to manage the Asylum and piss off Therese. She's influential in her own right, but more because of the club than anything else, being the same person isn't changing much in this regard.<br /> <br /> IIRC Nines did accept a truce with the Cam when the SI arrived, but you got how thrilling he finds the prospect. The others are pragmatic, so that's a no brainer to them. Also, Ming Xiao is out, but the Kuei-Jin are still in California in numbers and the local Camarilla already came to a truce with them after her fall, though in V5 they don't exist so who knows.<br /> <br /> Cross of course is barely sought out by anyone to talk about anything because they still have problems with Thin Bloods, but since her grip on the Pier is currently tight enough to hold her own against everyone else with just Thin Blood vampires at her side, I'd say she's still stronger than Abrams as a Baron.<br /> <br /> Other than those four, there used to be other three important factions whose current status we don't know. LA had one of the greatest Set temples in the US, but it fell some years before Bloodlines, still the Ministry may have numbers in and around the city. The Giovanni had one house that may or may not still stand. And the Sabbat had a priscus that had nothing to do with the infiltration the Fledgling wiped out.<br /> <br /> Mages and Demons also have a very strong presence there, so in a crossover game there may be all sorts of interactions between splats. LA is one of the hottest spots for the Ascension War this side of the Gauntlet, with a lot of factions coming and going all the time. I'd say most Mages in the US and a bunch in Canada and Mexico will probably go to LA at one point of another in their lives if they survive more than 5 years. The local Infernal Court is, or used to be, the biggest one in the world, and the city was the focal point of the most high profile activities of Lucifer himself and two or three Earthbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T05:14:20-07:00","id":1563562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563383#post1563383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the gist of it, though.<br /> <br /> You will have to make decisions, and some are going to mess with things someone likes. The problem isn't to do it, but how you go about it.<br /> <br /> Basically to questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are you doing it because you think you have to, so you can implement improvements, or are you just ripping off what you don't like so you don't have to look at it?<br /> <br /> 2. Can you show respect for those who liked it and recognize in-character it was a thing, or are you just going to brush it off or be a dick to the people who dislike your take?<br /> <br /> Outside that, they have options. Getting the example of Ciudad del Mexico and Montreal, even in V5 the problem was not that they got taken by the Camarilla. The problem is that they takeover is hastily and badly written, their previous state mostly ignored and they run as if they had always been Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Just trying to make a good story about it and having the transition leave lasting impacts in the two cities would have made it completely different. Still piss off people? Sure. But it would feel like a legitimate decision we don't like rather than the asshole move it obviously was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I went through the Montreal book to do exactly this for my own chronicles. You can still honour the V5 metaplot while honouring the past books. The easiest way is to have a small number of survivors, giving people the opportunity to have a few Cainites or a few embattled packs survive to serve as future plot seeds, and then portray the Camarilla as less stable/comfortable than they were in V5, with hints that the city is vulnerable and might be taken back if things go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T08:11:48-07:00","id":1563566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563383#post1563383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You will have to make decisions, and some are going to mess with things someone likes. The problem isn't to do it, but how you go about it.<br /> <br /> Basically to questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are you doing it because you think you have to, so you can implement improvements, or are you just ripping off what you don't like so you don't have to look at it?<br /> <br /> 2. Can you show respect for those who liked it and recognize in-character it was a thing, or are you just going to brush it off or be a dick to the people who dislike your take?<br /> <br /> Outside that, they have options. Getting the example of Ciudad del Mexico and Montreal, even in V5 the problem was not that they got taken by the Camarilla. The problem is that they takeover is hastily and badly written, their previous state mostly ignored and they run as if they had always been Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Just trying to make a good story about it and having the transition leave lasting impacts in the two cities would have made it completely different. Still piss off people? Sure. But it would feel like a legitimate decision we don't like rather than the asshole move it obviously was.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I said in other places - whatever writing/development decision they make they are going to anger someone, whatever. The only thing they can make sure is that it's good writing/decision that makes sense inside the setting. Meantime most of those decisions can be summed up with:<br /> <br /> Audience: Why did this happen, it makes no sense? <br /> Paradox: It's developer mandate, we don't have to explain it.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> Audience: What happened with the Fallen, Kuei-jin, etc.<br /> Paradox: I'm gonna need you to get all the way off my back about that. <br /> <br /> So it sounds like a &quot;fuck you&quot; to the people that are already invested in the setting and taking them for granted. <br /> <br /> There is also the big problem of limiting players options with stuff like implosion of Sabbat or elders vanishing beyond the horizon. WoD is great because of it's &quot;many worlds in one&quot; approach. Due to the unreliable narrators and conflicting information a lot of the setting is up to individual interpretation. V5 made that setting much smaller and limited. <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Bloodlines&quot; discussion I am always using the Revised approach to the WoD canon - stuff from books or video games are only canon if they are in the books. So Romuald and Katherine Wiese are canon but the exact events of &quot;VtM - Redemption&quot; do not have to be. Either way it's funny when people have played &quot;Bloodlines&quot; and start arguing about the setting with people who have read the books. It's like watching &quot;The Hobbit&quot; movie and arguing about Middle Earth without reading the books. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T22:00:23-07:00","id":1563586,"title":"","content":"I particularly think Montreal and Ciudad del M\u00e9xico are telling because in their fuck you attitude they didn't just disrespected fans and did poor writing, they effectively lost a golden opportunity to make really interesting stories.<br /> <br /> They focused on just making them Camarilla to have them as if they had always been Cam, and as a result they're pretty bland and generic when they could have been unique unstable colonies with plots and roles for PCs that don't exist elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Picture it: the Second Inquisition just had in the city one of their greatest, thorough victories. It has no surviving vampire power structure and any survivors are left in a danger zone where they must keep a low profile and extra care to survive. Even after a few years, while the SI has moved on it's safe to assume their vigilance in the city is still overwhelming. It's in this context that the Camarilla moves in.<br /> <br /> Local Camarilla is dominant, with no challenge to its claim, but that's not the same as an easy time. There's no old, well established influence in the city structures, and usual main targets are off limits as SI watchdogs. Local vampires are not powerful and stable, but adventurers or refugees fleeing their luck elsewhere to try the opportunities of a frontier colony style place. It is not a stable power, it's a tentative occupation of a still fresh battlefield.<br /> <br /> Sabbat vampires still wander around. They're under more pressure as the SI is likely to have more info on them, so they're in survival mode and not looking for a fight. Yet. But they're still older in the area and know more about it than the Camarilla newcomers. They're cut from the sect at large, or maybe acting as observers and spies, but compensate the lack of direct sect support with this greater level of integration in the city.<br /> <br /> Recognizing they history of the setting and the actual development of their own plot would get us something new and interesting to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T14:21:03-07:00","id":1563645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563407#post1563407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cross is a Thin Blood who rose to prominence some time after the events in Bloodlines and is the <i>de facto</i> Baron of the Pier area, the others couldn't oust her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, they couldn't, or didn't care enough to try?<br /> <br /> Most Thinbloods struggle to manifest their own disciplines, while those who do only seem to have access to 1 specific discipline (post V5). While in pre-V5, they could never advance their mastery beyond 3 dots (14th gen) or 2 dots (15th gen).<br /> <br /> Combine that with their inability to produce Ghouls, and the difficulties of embracing additional childe...<br /> <br /> Yeah, there's no logical reason for why this &quot;Jenna Cross&quot; should have been considered a legitimate power player. She is functionally a human with vampiric weaknesses.<br /> <br /> My theory is that any of the other Barons could snap her like a twig any time they wanted. But there's nothing in the Santa Monica pier that they actually want or need, so may as well let the bottom feeders squat there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T17:54:57-07:00","id":1563655,"title":"","content":"Jenna Cross could be like Kevin Jackson and has more than enough resources and contacts to protect her from such actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"u