ers from white room death battles, I can think of many different ways it may have played out.<br /> <br /> Not that it isn't hard to do. That's precisely why it's impressive that she could pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T20:27:30-07:00","id":1563664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563655#post1563655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jenna Cross could be like Kevin Jackson and has more than enough resources and contacts to protect her from such actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's sticking their neck out for a worthless Thinblood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T20:59:39-07:00","id":1563668,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the thin blood is more capable then most kindred like to admit and maybe a kindred feels some sort of connection to her and admires her drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T04:12:16-07:00","id":1563678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563664#post1563664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's sticking their neck out for a worthless Thinblood?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's politics, baby. If someone finds Cross's goals adrmirable or better yet, use her for their own goals they are going to lend her a hand and protect them. It is what has happened during the Third Sabbat Civil War.<br /> <br /> Joseph Pander was a lowly Caitiff in the sect who wanted recognition for clanless. Did Lasombra and Tzimisce running Sabbat cared about that? Hell no, but they thought he can be an useful tool and they supported him and used him to attack the Moderates. And he and his Caitiff did such a great job that they were given recognition as Panders &quot;clan&quot; within the Sword of Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T08:06:42-07:00","id":1563689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563678#post1563678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's politics, baby. If someone finds Cross's goals adrmirable or better yet, use her for their own goals they are going to lend her a hand and protect them. It is what has happened during the Third Sabbat Civil War.<br /> <br /> Joseph Pander was a lowly Caitiff in the sect who wanted recognition for clanless. Did Lasombra and Tzimisce running Sabbat cared about that? Hell no, but they thought he can be an useful tool and they supported him and used him to attack the Moderates. And he and his Caitiff did such a great job that they were given recognition as Panders &quot;clan&quot; within the Sword of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caitiff and Thinbloods are not interchangeable. Being one does not necessarily mean being the other as well.<br /> <br /> Also, it was my understanding that Pander had to fight for recognition; he didn't simply ask for it.<br /> <br /> Also, also, the Sabbat have only had 3 civil wars? Or for that matter, the first one ever actually ended? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T12:10:44-07:00","id":1563705,"title":"","content":"Both are looked down upon by the clans and are usually stuck at the bottom of the hierarchy and when someone like Jenna Cross or Mutker Bey gain significant clout it makes people nervous and wondering what did they miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-12-2026, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T14:35:55-07:00","id":1563706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563705#post1563705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are looked down upon by the clans and are usually stuck at the bottom of hierarchy and when someone like Jenna Cross or Mutker Bey gain significant clout it makes people nervous and wondering what did they miss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mukhtar may be caitiff, but he's also 7th generation, and has acquired 8 disciplines in his arsenal. One of which being 5 dots in Quietus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T14:42:11-07:00","id":1563707,"title":"","content":"And nervous they are, hence why they tried to get rid of Cross despite her domain being just the Pier area.<br /> <br /> Cross isn't accepted as a Baron. She just is one in practice regardless because they couldn't do something about it.<br /> <br /> It's also relevant to remember that attitudes toward Thin Bloods aren't universal, and while they're more open about believing Gehenna, Anarchs are also more tolerant in general. So while I know they tried to get rid of her, it's also possible that the other Barons won't resort to excess violence, either because they're not that pissed or because it would be bad rep.<br /> <br /> Going by their characters, Nines is likely to just ignore her or even offer token support out of ideology, and Therese would pretend she's not there as going too hard on the Thin Bloods will cost more than it's worth. Isaac is the only one I think would be really invested in getting rid of her, but he isn't much outside Hollywood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T14:57:22-07:00","id":1563709,"title":"","content":"Mr. Bey is still looked down upon despite being a 7th generation elder of fair power and many kindred seeth about it. The Jenna Cross situation makes them nervous because their is this young thin blood has acquired a respectable amount of influence and she is closer to human then they will ever be and the Anarchs don't want bad press if they use the same playbook of the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-12-2026, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:30:02-07:00","id":1563716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563689#post1563689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caitiff and Thinbloods are not interchangeable. Being one does not necessarily mean being the other as well.<br /> <br /> Also, it was my understanding that Pander had to fight for recognition; he didn't simply ask for it.<br /> <br /> Also, also, the Sabbat have only had 3 civil wars? Or for that matter, the first one ever actually ended? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do not ever remember saying they were interchangeable. It's the classic square-rectangle thing. Many Thinbloods are Caitiff but most importantly both groups are outcasts and pariahs in vampiric society. <br /> <br /> Again, I never said that Pander asked anyone. He fought for recognition of the Caitiff in the Sabbat by fighting at the behest of Lasombra and Tzimisce leaders of the sect (most likely Ultra-Conservatives who wanted a more authoritarian Sabbat) against the Moderates faction. After 2/3 of New York Sabbat were killed of during the conflict that lasted 100 nights Galbraith urged the warring sides to seat at the table and resolve matters by diplomatic talks. Anitribu were recognized as &quot;equals&quot; by the Lasombra and Tzimisce aristocracy of the Sabbat and Panders were recognized as a single clan. <br /> <br /> No, Sabbat had four Civil Wars, the brewing of the Fourth one is described in BJD and leads to the implosion of the Sword of Caine in V5. And First Civil War did officially end in 1803 with the signing of the Purchase Pact and the sect functioned in relative peace for sixty years until the Second Civil War broke out in 1863. Sabbat is fraught with internal conflict and the superiority complex combined with monomacy custom and more violent attitudes of the Sabbat Cainites lead to violent outbreaks. So hope that answers your questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:50:21-07:00","id":1563728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563707#post1563707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross isn't accepted as a Baron. She just is one in practice regardless because they couldn't do something about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There, that's the important distinction. The others do not officially recognize her status, even if she may function as one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2357\" data-vbnamecard=\"2357\">sathriel</a> Sorry, I wasn't trying to imply you used them interchangeably as such. What I meant was that there is a difference between gaining acceptance / power as a Caitiff vs doing so as someone who barely qualifies as a vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T18:11:10-07:00","id":1563732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563728#post1563728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There, that's the important distinction. The others do not officially recognize her status, even if she may function as one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2357\" data-vbnamecard=\"2357\">sathriel</a> Sorry, I wasn't trying to imply you used them interchangeably as such. What I meant was that there is a difference between gaining acceptance / power as a Caitiff vs doing so as someone who barely qualifies as a vamp.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that this distinction isn't as fixed as it seems.<br /> <br /> Vampire is a political game, and WoD is a system that deliberately puts a lot of weight over tactical advantages despite being discreet about them.<br /> <br /> Cross may still become enough of a force to have them recognize her. Not because she'll ever be as mystically potent, but because this is not about mystical potency. It is about being the person in a given area that others will listen too.<br /> <br /> For example, can one of the Barons move enough vampires to the Pier to threaten her? Do her subjects know the area well enough to get the upper hand in conflicts more often than not? What if lower Gen Kindred who live near to it just trust her leadership because she did a good job in an area the others neglected for years?<br /> <br /> Also, contrary to what some players insist as interpretation, there's no universal opinion on either Caitiff or Thin Bloods. The persecution is very specifically an Elder thing based on fear from eschatological beliefs. Common among Elders, less so among higher Generations and not everyone who believes do so in the same way.<br /> <br /> Legacy always made a point that Elders avoid being open in their aggression against those vampires precisely because it isn't a popular idea among the younger Generations, and the places where persecution is more open are also those where Elders feel considerably more secure in their positions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T08:21:04-07:00","id":1563784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1563732#post1563732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, contrary to what some players insist as interpretation, there's no universal opinion on either Caitiff or Thin Bloods. The persecution is very specifically an Elder thing based on fear from eschatological beliefs. Common among Elders, less so among higher Generations and not everyone who believes do so in the same way.<br /> <br /> Legacy always made a point that Elders avoid being open in their aggression against those vampires precisely because it isn't a popular idea among the younger Generations, and the places where persecution is more open are also those where Elders feel considerably more secure in their positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true about most things about the setting. The WoD is nuanced world where even quite homogenous groups have conflicting views and approaches. Even among the Camarilla vampires believing that Thinblood and/or Caitiff are a stain on vampiric society and sign of coming Gehenna they might be allying or helping/using Cross if they think she furthers their own goals. <br /> <br /> Anarchs are still doing petty political tug of war and their own goals might win over their inherent bias. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-03T15:07:12-08:00","id":1565108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528497-what-do-you-think-in-hindsight-would-have-been-better-for-v5?p=1562552#post1562552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive the thread necromancy, but how does it feel to be a prophet?</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels great and I am going to miss this forum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is poli